unt":null,"email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:02:50.459Z","repositoryId":1322604916,"sha":"d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"authoredDate":"2026-07-31T06:01:48Z","committedDate":"2026-07-31T06:01:48Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:02:50.459Z","repositoryId":1322604916,"sha":"d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:02:50.459Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:20:19Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:20:19Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"chore(api-client): re-vendor the contextplane spec, and follow two renames into it\n\n`check-spec-freshness` was failing: the vendored document predated eleven paths\nthe service had since renamed, so the one guard that exists to catch this repo\nfalling behind was reporting exactly that and nobody had acted on it.\n\nRe-vendored from contextplane at 243 operations over 191 paths, regenerated, and\nthe capability table in `capability-api-parity.test.ts` followed the two renames\nit named by hand:\n\n- `{provider_cap_id}` and `{capability_id}` became `{entity_id}` on adoptions and\n  subscriptions. One table backs the whole catalog and there is no `capabilities`\n  table, so three names for one identifier was three names for the same UUID.\n- `/v1/admin/capability-types` became `/v1/admin/entity-types`, following the\n  registry rename, and `{type_name}` became `{entity_type}` with it.\n\nThat test is the reason this was a four-line change rather than a silent one: it\nasserts every endpoint the capability table claims actually exists in the API\ndocument, so a rename upstream fails here instead of surfacing as a 404 in a\nbrowser.\n\nVerified: `lint`, `typecheck`, `ci:unit` (64 files, 611 tests) and all six static\nguards pass. `check-spec-freshness` now reports 243 operations matching.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe2d8aa4d0a288ab69ddd3e4f0041cf586468d40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/fe2d8aa4d0a288ab69ddd3e4f0041cf586468d40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDNhZjU5N2Q1NDczMjBlNDQ0ZGE2NTgzZWIyNWMwZGZhYjcxNzM4NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b","sha":"b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b"}],"sha":"3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:16:41Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T01:16:41Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"fix(chrome): the active indicator reaches the viewport edge, the label does not\n\nWork from another session, found uncommitted in the working tree. Verified\nagainst this repo''s gates and landed rather than left exposed.\n\nThe three-pixel accent now starts at the rail''s outside edge while the active\nsurface and every label keep the rail''s sixteen-pixel inline gutter. Moving the\nindicator inward with the menu content made the rail read as a card floating\ninside another card, which weakens the one signal the rail exists to give: where\nyou are.\n\nThe rule is written into `docs/04-design/01-standard.md` rather than left in the\nstylesheet, because the next person to adjust the gutter needs to know the\nindicator is deliberately not part of it. `AppShell.test.tsx` and the chrome\nend-to-end spec assert the split, so the two can no longer drift apart quietly.\n\nVerified: `lint`, `typecheck`, and `ci:unit` (64 files, 611 tests) all pass, as\ndo five of the six static guards.\n\n`check-spec-freshness` fails, and it fails independently of this change -- the\nvendored `contextplane.openapi.json` predates the parameter renames that landed\nin contextplane#23, so eleven capability paths still read `{capability_id}` and\n`{provider_cap_id}` where the service now says `{entity_id}`. No file in this\ncommit touches the vendored document. Re-vendoring is its own change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"510ef0191ee0412fe812affa23d96888d2ba2393","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/510ef0191ee0412fe812affa23d96888d2ba2393"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGIzMjkwNTZhMWUyODM3ODFjM2EwZTczNjdhZWQ2YmYyMDkyNzNmMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349","sha":"f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349"}],"sha":"b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b329056a1e283781c3a0e7367aed6bf209273f2b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:12:32Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:12:32Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"feat: modernize context workflows and shell experience\n\nSync the client to intent-based APIs, rebuild retrieval testing and receipt workflows, and refine shell navigation, search, typography, cards, and operational metrics.","tree":{"sha":"fcc5934edf365ac15312cca704a4e0b99a6e1368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/fcc5934edf365ac15312cca704a4e0b99a6e1368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGYwNDc3NTBlYWNjNDBkN2ZjNjUxMTRmZjYyMWUyZDZmZTZlNjIzNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de","sha":"18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de"}],"sha":"f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f047750eacc40d7fc65114ff621e2d6fe6e62349"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:57:44Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:57:44Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Align shell chrome with the reference\n\nMatch the 56px utility bar, 240px desktop rail, 72px tablet rail, page insets, active navigation treatment, and menu-only scrolling while preserving the resizable desktop navigation. Add component and browser regressions for desktop, tablet, and mobile geometry.\\n\\nVerified with all static, codegen, unit, mocked browser, bundle budget, production build, and secret checks; 607 unit tests and 72 browser tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"118bb83a340d0f9d2221c3477c9e850ed90b4a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/118bb83a340d0f9d2221c3477c9e850ed90b4a20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDE4YTAyNDZiNzUyMDYxYTUyNDQ0NDM2MzM0MDA0YTNmNTljYmU5ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018","sha":"d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018"}],"sha":"18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18a0246b752061a52444436334004a3f59cbe9de"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:16:14Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T04:16:14Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Align card headings with the reference\n\nCentralize card and tile headings in a Salt-only composition so semantic h2/h3 elements no longer inherit browser margins. Card titles now render at 20px over 14px descriptions with a 6px internal gap, 24px before content, and centered visuals and actions; navigation tiles use the documented 16px step.\\n\\nVerified desktop and mobile renders in light mode. The full static and codegen gates passed, 606 unit/component tests and 69 mocked browser tests passed, fetched remote bundles remain 352.5 KB and 347.0 KB gzip, and production secret scanning passed.","tree":{"sha":"6268749257c6c27b92a4bd061e5c323ca0aa3789","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/6268749257c6c27b92a4bd061e5c323ca0aa3789"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQ4Njk3YTUwMzQ1MzM1NDJjMTFkMmJjYWI4MzAzYmY0M2M0NmIwMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1","sha":"a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1"}],"sha":"d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d8697a5034533542c11d2bcab8303bf43c46b018"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T03:55:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T03:55:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Use semantic labels instead of generic pills\n\nReserve Salt Tag for confidence and change classifications, and Pill for the removable lifecycle filter. Render identity, counts, sources, ordinary enums, and table metadata as text; render state through a shared icon-and-label StatusLabel.\n\nVerified all 604 unit/component tests and 68 mocked federation tests. Static, accessibility, code-generation, production-secret, and bundle-budget gates pass; fetched remotes remain at 352.5 KB and 347.0 KB gzip.","tree":{"sha":"63099a0e28f1330aff23cc7da5de1d1357792036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/63099a0e28f1330aff23cc7da5de1d1357792036"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE1YjQ2YzJiNTk5MGNiN2EwNzc4NWUzNTM2ZTliMzk1MmI4NzFhYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9","sha":"f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9"}],"sha":"a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a5b46c2b5990cb7a07785e3536e9b3952b871ac1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T03:29:41Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T03:29:41Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Flatten nested dashboard card hierarchy\n\nReplace bordered section wrappers around metric tiles with responsive Salt section headings, and make empty states surface-neutral so tables and panels never frame another card. The graph, health, usage, and analytics views now match the reference hierarchy while retaining peer metric surfaces and the resizable rail.\\n\\nAdd a built-route sweep that rejects any nested Salt Card. Verified ci:static, 604 unit/component tests, 68 mocked end-to-end tests, bundle budgets, API code generation, production secret scans, and responsive light/dark visual checks.","tree":{"sha":"dd80781424a7d8749f1841e71f32afed30bbabde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/dd80781424a7d8749f1841e71f32afed30bbabde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGYyODhkMTQxZTQyYjc1MTJhNjlmNDhiOWMxN2U5YWVjZTEwN2IyYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7","sha":"dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7"}],"sha":"f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f288d141e42b7512a69f48b9c17e9aece107b2c9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:59:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:59:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Remove the shell header border and edge inset\n\nPlace the borderless Salt Toolbar on an opaque primary Panel and offset the default viewport inset with Salt spacing so the full shell and navigation rail begin at the left edge without horizontal overflow. Add browser assertions for zero edge offset, no Toolbar border, and an opaque header surface.\n\nVerified with 604 unit/component tests, 67 mocked browser tests, accessibility sweeps, static guards, responsive screenshots, and bundle budgets.","tree":{"sha":"9a0e67cc27a825a603c485c2f6c38b36c06b0374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/9a0e67cc27a825a603c485c2f6c38b36c06b0374"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGRiZDg0OTcwY2VmNGIxNDVlMzA2MzdmMmY2N2MzZmJkNzM0M2YzYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626","sha":"16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626"}],"sha":"dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dbd84970cef4b145e30637f2f67c3fbd7343f3b7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:53:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:53:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Pin opaque shell chrome during page scroll\n\nCompose the header with an opaque Salt Toolbar, measure its responsive height, and keep the desktop rail fixed beneath it with independent viewport overflow. Render the dashboard header destinations as Salt action buttons and cover page scrolling, rail scrolling, opacity, and non-overlap in the mocked browser suite.\n\nVerified with 604 unit/component tests, 67 mocked browser tests, accessibility sweeps, light/dark visual checks, static guards, and bundle budgets.","tree":{"sha":"e4c737195962491f97f453e434232528933139cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/e4c737195962491f97f453e434232528933139cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDE2YmM1YTQ1ZGJmOTNmNGMyNjkxZTY0MjUxNzVkN2U0NTc3Y2Y2MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf","sha":"c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf"}],"sha":"16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/16bc5a45dbf93f4c2691e6425175d7e4577cf626"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:40:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:40:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Align the console shell with the reference harness\n\nMove product identity into a full-width sticky header, add a global provenance footer, and make the Salt SidePanel width draggable and persistent. Restore the dashboard greeting hierarchy and align its actions while removing top-accent borders from shared card treatments.\n\nVerified with 604 unit/component tests, 67 mocked browser tests, light/dark responsive screenshots, static guards, production builds, credential scans, and bundle budgets.","tree":{"sha":"0dd632e86ef8146a605491a3114f1dea0385a14c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/0dd632e86ef8146a605491a3114f1dea0385a14c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM1MmViZTI0NDVhNWZhMDE5M2NhZmI5MzAzOWMwMjAyNDg0ZjdlYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4","sha":"8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4"}],"sha":"c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c52ebe2445a5fa0193cafb93039c0202484f7ebf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:06:03Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T02:06:03Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Name the product DE Context Plane for Agents\n\nApply the official name to shell chrome, browser titles, standalone remotes, primary documentation, and vendored API metadata while preserving stable internal package identifiers.\\n\\nVerified with 601 unit and component tests, 66 mocked end-to-end tests, accessibility sweeps, lint, type checks, formatting, policy guards, and desktop, tablet, and mobile visual review.","tree":{"sha":"c0a33eb38cac3c6eb1fd1b6c853a0e3e98130fbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/c0a33eb38cac3c6eb1fd1b6c853a0e3e98130fbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDhlZTU1ZGI0ZDE5Y2Y3MDBiZGRjY2RlMTc2MGY3MzQ5Mjg4MTMyYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f","sha":"0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f"}],"sha":"8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8ee55db4d19cf700bddccde1760f7349288132c4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:40:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:40:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Rework the console around Salt composition\n\nReplace application CSS and raw presentation markup with Salt components, then rebuild the shell and dashboard around a branded responsive rail, stronger hierarchy, honest metrics, and consistent domain context.\\n\\nValidated across desktop, tablet, mobile, and dark mode with 601 unit and component tests, 65 mocked end-to-end tests, accessibility sweeps, production builds, bundle budgets, formatting, secret scans, and repository guards.","tree":{"sha":"d221330c707ef2688075a142333cca057cb84e9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/d221330c707ef2688075a142333cca057cb84e9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDBiMzcxMTliNDBiZmQ2NDQyNjVhOGEyZDE1MjNiNDc5MDQ3ZjMzNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491","sha":"2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491"}],"sha":"0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0b37119b40bfd644265a8a2d1523b479047f334f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:39:54Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T18:39:54Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Refresh the contextplane API contract\n\nRegenerate the vendored OpenAPI paths and TypeScript client from the current service contract so the UI tracks all 218 live operations.\\n\\nVerified with the spec-freshness guard and the complete UI quality suite.","tree":{"sha":"5f64ec35bab5bb762e979a7ee6225ff2e2f58591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/5f64ec35bab5bb762e979a7ee6225ff2e2f58591"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDJlYTIzMmIxM2ExNjk0MjZhNzk4YTU0ODIzZjliYWM2MTc2ODc0OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009","sha":"33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009"}],"sha":"2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2ea232b13a169426a798a54823f9bac617687491"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:55:18Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:55:18Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Give the charts an axis, the pages a window, and the waits a shape\n\nThree threads that kept arriving at the same files, so they land together.\n\n**The chart was a bar of colour, not a reading.** `BarSeries` and `Sparkline`\ndrew proportional divs, which is the smallest thing that shows relative\nmagnitude and stops there: no value axis, so six columns looked identical\nwhether the peak was fifty calls or fifty thousand; no gridlines, so two columns\nof similar height could not be ranked; no hover, so reading one day meant\nfinding its row in the table. `ColumnChart` is recharts, and all three are one\nprop each.\n\nThe cost was measured rather than estimated — ~112 KB gz with React external,\nagainst 6 KB of headroom on catalog and 12.5 KB on operations. It is paid behind\n`LazyColumnChart`, a dynamic import that puts the library in its own chunk\noutside the exposed module''s graph, which is what the budget script measures.\nFederation made a share the wrong answer: each remote fetches its own copy of\nevery shared fallback, so a share duplicates the bytes and deduplicates only the\ninstance. Colours stay `var(--kui-chart-*)` in `theme-fixups.css` — the library\ntakes them as props, and `check-salt-tokens` only reads stylesheets, so a\nliteral here would be invisible to the guard that exists because two of three\nseries once rendered transparent. The mark is still hidden from assistive\ntechnology and still paired with the table that carries the same numbers.\n\n**The window a page reports on now has one definition.** `dateRange` holds the\npresets and their arithmetic — trailing N days, to-date, and completed periods —\nlifted out of the usage screen because more than one panel shows the active\nrange and any of them can change it. Two panels disagreeing about where a\nquarter starts look identical until someone reconciles two exports. Fiscal\nperiods are the calendar''s, stated in the option labels and in the module,\nbecause it is the assumption a reader imports from their own organisation.\n\n**Loading shows the shape of the answer.** `StatTile` and `DescriptionList` take\n`isLoading` and draw bars only where the reading will be, keeping every label\nand term — a row of tiles that says what it is about to measure is more\ninformative than a row of spinners, and nothing moves when the number lands.\nPages that returned a `LoadingPanel` branch instead of their table lost it: that\nbranch replaced the content with a centred glyph and then jumped the page.\n\nThat change broke ten tests on one page with the same unhelpful message.\n`DataTable` renders its column-derived skeleton under the same `table` role, so\n`findByRole(''table'')` now resolves before the data exists and every \"find the\ntable, then read a cell\" assertion started reading placeholders.\n`findLoadedTable` waits for the region to stop being `aria-busy`, which is what\na reader waits for, and lives in the testing package so the loading contract has\none place to change.\n\n`SectionCard` gained plural `actions` in a row, because headers commonly carry\nmore than one and callers were composing their own `FlexLayout` for each; and it\nnow renders a header for a description or an action alone, where it previously\nrequired a title and silently dropped both.\n\nGates: 601 unit, 67 end-to-end, bundle within budget (shell 403.1/440, catalog\n354.3/360, operations 349.1/360), lint, stylelint, types, format.\n\n`check-spec-freshness` fails on eleven ARC paths the backend serves and this\nrepo has not vendored. It fails identically on the untouched base — nothing here\ntouches the client — and clears when the API document is re-exported.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb39af4871de640e7700b8fd6d7cf1e869fb4f7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/eb39af4871de640e7700b8fd6d7cf1e869fb4f7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDMzZGNmMzVlYzY0OTRiNWJiYTZhOWNmMGY4NzIwNjYzMmFlMTYwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8","sha":"c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8"}],"sha":"33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/33dcf35ec6494b5bba6a9cf0f87206632ae16009"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T02:35:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T02:35:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Restore the package registry the rename swept away\n\n`npm ci` failed in CI on every job that runs it, while every gate passed\nlocally. The cause was in the lockfile: the sweep that renamed the backend\nreplaced the word \"registry\" inside 654 package download URLs, pointing them at\n`https://contextplane.npmjs.org/`, a host that does not exist. It also renamed a\nreal dependency, `language-subtag-registry`, to a package nobody publishes.\n\nLocal runs could not see it. `npm ci` served every one of those packages from\nthe on-disk cache and never resolved a URL; CI starts cold, so the first fetch\nfailed and both jobs died before reaching a single check.\n\nThe two `contextplane` strings left in the manifests are correct — the\ndescription and the codegen path refer to the renamed backend.\n\nThis is the third distinct class of damage from that sweep, after the imports\nthat pointed at files which were never renamed and the prose that changed\nmeaning. The pattern is the same each time: \"registry\" is a common English word\nand a common infrastructure term, and replacing it without discriminating hits\nthings that have nothing to do with the product.\n\nGates after the repair: 585 unit, codegen deterministic, lint, types, format.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9032ea1ad042d05a9d3545a166ec3417bd5d2ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/9032ea1ad042d05a9d3545a166ec3417bd5d2ada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM4ZjBmNjM5MTkxOTU1MTkyNTliMzY0NWQzMzJjMTUwOWFkMGEyZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518","sha":"2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518"}],"sha":"c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8f0f63919195519259b3645d332c1509ad0a2d8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T02:30:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T02:30:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Follow the backend''s rename, and undo it where the word meant something else\n\nThe backend repository became `contextplane`, and a sweep across this repo\nreplaced the word everywhere it appeared. That left the workspace broken:\ntypecheck reported twelve errors and lint failed, because imports had been\nrepointed at `./generated/contextplane` and `../../tooling/vite/contextplane-proxy`\nwhile both files were still named after the old product.\n\nTwo of those renames were right and are completed here — the generated client\nand the vendored API document describe the backend, and the dev proxy exists to\nreach it. The export moved with the module, `registryProxy` to\n`contextplaneProxy`.\n\nThe rest were the same word meaning something else. `apps/shell/src/remotes/registry.ts`\nis the registry of *remotes* — the table of mount points and navigation sections\nthis host owns — and has nothing to do with the backend. Its imports had been\nrepointed at a file that does not exist, and the README had been rewritten to\ncite `remotes/contextplane.ts`, a path no reader could follow. Those are back to\n`registry`, and the layout tables say \"remote registry\" again.\n\nProse was corrected where the substitution produced something untrue rather than\nmerely awkward: the service table said \"Registry API\" beside prose that no longer\nused the word, and one orientation table described the shell as owning a \"remote\ncontextplane\".\n\nNote for whoever re-vendors the API document: the sweep also edited the\ndescription text inside `contextplane.openapi.json`, so its prose now differs\nfrom what the service serves — including one sentence where \"the\nentity_external_ids registry\" became \"the entity_external_ids contextplane\",\nwhich is the word meaning an index. The path and method sets are untouched, which\nis all the freshness gate compares, so this will correct itself when the backend\nrename lands and the document is re-exported.\n\nGates: 585 unit, 67 end-to-end, bundle within budget, production build clean of\nthe dev roster, lint, types, format and guards. The spec-freshness gate reports\nthe same pre-existing drift as before — a dev backend serving eleven endpoints\nthat exist only in another repository''s uncommitted tree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"482dd5331c9104f4fb4b6762d49ceb9232058769","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/482dd5331c9104f4fb4b6762d49ceb9232058769"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDJiMTkwY2E0Zjg2N2JlZjYxZmU5YjBiZTRhZmM4NDYzZTJmNWY1MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5","sha":"c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5"}],"sha":"2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2b190ca4f867bef61fe9b0be4afc8463e2f5f518"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:38:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:38:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Clear every advisory that a patch release can reach\n\nThe dependency audit reported thirteen. Four are now gone with the js-yaml\noverride that preceded this; nine remained, and all but two of those had a fix\ninside the current major version:\n\n  concurrently          9.2.1  -> 9.2.4   (critical, via shell-quote)\n  react-router          6.30.1 -> 6.30.4  (high)\n  react-router-dom      6.30.1 -> 6.30.4  (high)\n  @module-federation/vite 1.20.1 -> 1.20.5 (moderate, via undici)\n  vite                  7.1.9  -> 7.3.6   (high)\n\nMinimum fixing versions rather than latest, deliberately: the registry this\nmust install from does not carry everything on the public one, and asking for\nless is asking for something more likely to be there.\n\nThe routers are federated singletons, so the pin table moved with them. Two\ncopies of react-router is not a version warning — it is `useParams()` returning\nan empty object inside a remote, which is why parity is a build gate rather\nthan a convention.\n\nThe two that remain are moderate, and their fix is a major version: react-router\n8 or react-router-dom 7.18. Both are unreachable here as written. One is\narbitrary constructor injection during server-side hydration, and nothing in\nthis repo renders on a server — there is no `hydrateRoot`, no `StaticRouter`,\nno server entry. The other is an open redirect through a backslash, and that\none is worth more than an argument, because link targets here are assembled\nfrom values the registry served and the registry ingests from sync connectors:\na capability''s name is upstream content, not a value this app chose.\n\nSo the vector is closed at the link layer rather than argued away. `KLink` is\nthe single component every anchor in the app already routes through, and it now\nescapes backslashes and neutralises a protocol-relative target before either\nreaches the router. Encoded rather than rejected — a name is data, and refusing\nto render a row because of a character in it is a worse failure than linking to\nan escaped version of it. Applied there rather than at the twelve call sites\nthat build a path from served content, because a rule about what may reach the\nrouter belongs where every link passes.\n\nAdvisories: thirteen to two, no high and no critical, and neither survivor is\nreachable through this application.\n\nVerified with the routers rebuilt across the federation boundary, which is the\nonly lane that would show a singleton breaking: 585 unit, 67 end-to-end, four\nof them new and covering the escape, bundles slightly smaller than before,\ngenerated client byte-identical, `npm ci` accepts the lockfile, production build\nclean of the dev roster, lint, types, format and guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c30b01b8f582f1a5641587925215127c4d4266da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/c30b01b8f582f1a5641587925215127c4d4266da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM4ZTI4YTBkOGZhMWQ4MjA2ODdmMGQyZjBiMjkzZWEzOTA1YmYwZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709","sha":"774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709"}],"sha":"c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c8e28a0d8fa1d820687f0d2f0b293ea3905bf0f5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:26:37Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:26:37Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Force the patched js-yaml under the OpenAPI generator\n\n`npm audit` reported a high advisory in the codegen toolchain:\nCVE-2026-59870, quadratic CPU consumption parsing `!!omap`, in js-yaml\nbefore 4.3.1. It arrives through @redocly/openapi-core, which\nopenapi-typescript has depended on since its 7.0.0.\n\nDowngrading the generator does not fix it, which is worth recording because it\nis the obvious move and it is wrong twice over. Every 7.x carries redocly, so\nonly a major step back to 6.x sheds it — and that rewrites the generated\nclient. More decisively, each 7.x declares redocly with a caret, so npm\nresolves every one of them to the same 1.34.18 regardless of which is named.\nThe version in package.json would change and the installed tree would not.\n\nThe pin is redocly''s: 1.34.18 asks for js-yaml at exactly 4.3.0, where earlier\nreleases used a caret that floats to the fix on its own. An override is\ntherefore the only lever that reaches it.\n\nNothing here ships. The generator runs during codegen and the linter''s copy\nruns during lint; the production bundles contain neither, which the secrets\ngate already proves. The exposure is a denial of service against whoever parses\nhostile YAML, and the only document this repo parses is its own vendored API\ndescription, which is JSON. So this is hygiene rather than a live risk — but it\ncosts one line.\n\nThe lockfile is regenerated rather than patched, because npm applies an\noverride during resolution and kept rebuilding the tree from the existing\nnode_modules instead. That floated 44 transitive dependencies by a patch level\neach — rollup, babel, browserslist data, postcss, ws — and cleared two further\nadvisories along the way, in fast-uri and nanoid. Thirteen advisories become\nnine. No federated share moved: react and react-dom are pinned by the\noverrides beside this one, and shared-parity passes.\n\n`msw.workerDirectory` now names all three public directories, so the tool that\ngenerates the interceptors updates every copy rather than only the shell''s —\nthe drift the worker-parity guard was added to catch.\n\nVerified: the generated client is byte-identical under the new js-yaml\n(`ci:codegen` regenerates and fails on any diff), `npm ci` accepts the\nlockfile, 581 unit, 67 end-to-end, bundle within budget, production build clean\nof the dev roster, lint, types, format and guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0d218e4fa2751a2119fccac2105621b0972ff82a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/0d218e4fa2751a2119fccac2105621b0972ff82a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDc3NGRlOGNiNGRlNzUyMzU2MmM0NmQyMTY2YWE5OTZiOGMzMmY3MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7","sha":"0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7"}],"sha":"774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/774de8cb4de7523562c46d2166aa996b8c32f709"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:05:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:05:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Intercept on every origin, so the whole app runs with no backend\n\nThe mocked dev lane covered the shell and stopped there. Each remote''s\nstandalone page is its own document on its own port, and a service worker''s\nscope is the origin that served it — so the shell''s copy could never cover them\nand those two pages still needed a registry, an identity provider and an\nentitlement service. \"The app runs without a backend\" was true of the part most\npeople open and false of the rest, which is the kind of half-truth a README\nsentence papers over.\n\nEach remote now carries its own worker and starts it before render, for the same\nreason the shell does: the standalone harness mints a token on mount, and a\nrequest that escapes before the worker is ready reaches for the identity\nprovider this lane exists not to need.\n\nThree copies of a generated file is duplication that cannot be designed away, so\nit is guarded instead. `check-worker-parity` compares all three against the\ninstalled library rather than only against each other, because three identically\nstale copies are still stale — agreement is not currency. It caught the first\none immediately: the shell''s copy had been run through the formatter despite the\nignore rule that says the generating tool owns it. Same version, same integrity\nchecksum, semicolons added. Now all three are the tool''s own output.\n\nVerified with the proxy pointed at a dead port, so anything escaping would fail\nrather than quietly succeed against the backend that happens to be running:\nacross the shell and both standalone pages, twenty-four API responses, all\ntwenty-four served by a worker, none reaching the network, no failed requests\nand no page errors, every route rendering its own heading over fixture data.\n\nGates: 581 unit, 67 end-to-end, bundle within budget, production build clean of\nthe dev roster, lint, types, format and guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afa8a268e878faeeb056d9b93c35148bd6719b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/afa8a268e878faeeb056d9b93c35148bd6719b8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDBlYjM1MmZkNTZmMTdhMWUwOThmNDRhNDg0OGI5Y2IxODU2MDJhYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8","sha":"de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8"}],"sha":"0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0eb352fd56f17a1e098f44a4848b9cb185602aa7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:45:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:45:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Start the app with no backend at all\n\nThe mocked lane could be tested but not used. `build:e2e` compiles the request\nhandlers into the artefacts for CI, and the README''s \"if you have no backend\"\nsection answered a question nobody was asking — how to run the *tests* without\none — while the only documented way to open the app still needed a registry, a\nmock identity provider and an entitlement service, plus a seeding step whose\nabsence looks exactly like a broken permission.\n\n`npm run dev:mock` runs the same three dev servers behind the same handlers the\ntests assert against. Hot reloading is unaffected: the handlers are a service\nworker in front of the network, not a different build. The token endpoint is\namong them, which is why the persona switcher works with no identity provider\nanywhere and refusals behave as they do against a real registry.\n\nA script rather than an inline environment prefix, because that is POSIX syntax\nand the setup instructions do not claim a shell. It prints the lane, says the\ndata is fixture data, and names the one hole: the standalone remote harnesses\nare separate documents and are not intercepted.\n\nVerified rather than assumed, against a proxy pointed at a dead port so anything\nescaping the interceptor would fail outright: all ten primary routes render\ntheir own heading, every one of twenty-one API responses is served by the worker\nwith none reaching the network, `/readyz` answers 200 and the rail reports the\nAPI ready, and the data on screen is the fixture set rather than the local seed.\nThe service worker outliving the run that registered it was also tested, since\nthat is the trap this shape has — the same browser profile switched back to\n`npm run dev` served zero responses from the worker and showed live data.\n\nGates: 581 unit, 67 end-to-end, bundle within budget, lint, types, format and\nguards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e01479296ebc256ed91b4d074ea47c01612669de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/e01479296ebc256ed91b4d074ea47c01612669de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGRlMmE4YTFkODRhMzU2ZGVlNTQ0YzY2MzFmYzY2YjJiMDM5ZGUxZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2","sha":"a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2"}],"sha":"de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/de2a8a1d84a356dee544c6631fc66b2b039de1e8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:25:25Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:25:25Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Open graph analytics on a root the walk actually reaches\n\nThe default root was whichever entity the catalog listed first, which is\ncreation order and says nothing about connectedness. Against the local seed\nthat is a leaf, so the page opened on four zeros and an empty state and read\nas a broken screen rather than as an honest measurement of a leaf.\n\nAn edge''s destination is the depended-upon side, so the first destination the\npage can name is a root with at least one dependent. The server''s own edge\nlist chooses the default; nothing is counted, sorted or scored in the browser,\nand the catalog''s first entry remains the fallback. The panel now waits for\nthe edge list too, so it opens once rather than measuring a leaf and visibly\nre-measuring.\n\nNames resolve from the projection''s own nodes before the catalog''s. That is\nbetter practice — one response is internally consistent, two joined by id are\nonly as good as their agreement — and here the agreement does not exist: the\nmocked catalog derives ids from a counter and the mocked graph from the\nentry''s name, so a cross-endpoint join resolves against the real service and\nnever under test. That trap is now written down beside the other fixture\nrules, because the next screen to join those two responses will hit it and the\nfailure points at the change rather than at the mock.\n\nVerified both ways: the mocked lane opens on a root with dependents rather\nthan the catalog''s first row, and against the live registry the page opens on\none dependent, one edge and a populated relationship table where it previously\nshowed four zeros.\n\nGates: 581 unit, 67 end-to-end both colour modes, bundle within budget, all\nguards but the spec-freshness one already recorded as reporting a dev backend\nthat runs ahead of its own repository''s committed contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8260f3eeb72d6c6b15a32254264bcf1b22ba1cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/c8260f3eeb72d6c6b15a32254264bcf1b22ba1cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE5ZWFjOTFiMTRjZDFhYjU1NjU4YzhkYTZhMzVmNDBhMmRjYmFhZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8","sha":"a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8"}],"sha":"a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a9eac91b14cd1ab55658c8da6a35f40a2dcbaaf2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:13:50Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:13:50Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Name the class of defect that is correct in the DOM and absent from the screen\n\nAlignment was written up as a one-off cautionary tale. It was not one: a\nwalkthrough of the built console found three more of exactly its shape in a\nsingle pass — a wrapping column that did not wrap, a link cell rendering in\nbody colour, and a floating panel clipped out of existence by an ancestor.\n\nEach had the right markup, the right class and the right intent, and no\nreader could see any of them. The standard now names the shape, states the\nrule it implies — assert the effect, not the form, when a change depends on a\ndeclaration winning, an element escaping, or a value crossing a component\nboundary — and lists the four gates that now exist because each one was\nwritten after watching it fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60d221fb251aff374e3fbc1561de6ab1d332b3dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/60d221fb251aff374e3fbc1561de6ab1d332b3dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE3YTk1OTIxM2U4NzEyNmI5MDY1ZDA4OWUyMjQzOTI2ZGYwYmI2Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966","sha":"79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966"}],"sha":"a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a7a959213e87126b9065d089e2243926df0bb6b8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:12:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T21:12:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Fix what the walkthrough found, including three fixes that never reached the screen\n\nA nine-judge walkthrough of the built console — every route, five personas,\nboth colour modes — returned thirteen verified defects. Implementing them\nsurfaced a fourth category the judges could not see from screenshots alone:\nchanges that were correct in the DOM and invisible to the reader.\n\nThree of those were shipped-broken and are fixed here at the source:\n\n  - `Column.wrap` never wrapped. `.wrap` alone loses to the compound\n    `.table:global(.saltTable) td` rule beside it, so the class landed and\n    nothing moved. The claims table measured 1841px against a 1198px column\n    and hid four of its eight columns; it now measures 1369px and scrolls the\n    remainder. All three columns that had opted in were affected.\n  - A link''s colour stopped at its content. A column supplies its own\n    `render`, and Salt `Text` sets its own foreground, so every link cell was\n    a teal anchor wrapping black text. Fixed as the cell''s rule rather than\n    each column''s.\n  - The search suggestion panel had never been visible at all. The top bar\n    clips its children so a long breadcrumb cannot spill across the field, and\n    an absolutely-positioned panel cannot escape an ancestor''s overflow\n    whatever its z-index says. It renders through Salt''s floating layer now,\n    which also brings the collision handling the hand-positioned version could\n    not do. No direct floating-library import: it resolves only through Salt\n    today, so Salt''s own default middleware is used instead.\n\njsdom computes no styles and stylelint checks form rather than effect, so\nnone of these could fail a test. Four end-to-end assertions now cover them by\nmeasured effect — the same lane, and the same reason, as numeric alignment.\n\nThe rest, by what the reader sees: links carry the accent register and inert\ntags stop competing with them; the catalog no longer claims every row is\ninactive while the record says otherwise; ?as_of is honoured on the list;\nthe Interface tab renders the recorded attribute it was denying; the audit log\nnames the actor and opens each diff beneath its own row; served numbers are\nrounded, given units, and no longer report a queue age as a queue depth;\nrefusals name a role and offer the persona that holds it. Copy across twelve\npages drops the implementation voice.\n\nTwo gates were red before this branch and are fixed rather than carried:\nthree files failed `format:check`, and `check-no-dev-secrets` failed because\na comment quoted a development client id — the exact trap the file that\ndefines the guard warns about, since sourcemaps carry comment text.\n\nThe vendored API document is deliberately not re-vendored. The dev backend\nruns eleven endpoints ahead of it, but they exist only in another repository''s\nuncommitted tree: our copy matches that repository''s committed spec exactly,\n185 operations, no difference in either direction. `check-spec-freshness`\nreports drift while that dev process is up; it skips where no service is\nreachable, which is every CI run.\n\nGates: 580 unit, 67 end-to-end across both colour modes, bundle within budget\n(shell 403.3/440, catalog 354.6/360, operations 347.1/360), codegen\ndeterministic, all guards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c5e8bb4bc0611750136f972057491d9fe6b0f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/7c5e8bb4bc0611750136f972057491d9fe6b0f39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDc5YmQ5ZWE1YzIwODJmNzE3Y2FkYzRkZjJkMzIyZjliNDdjMGI5NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69","sha":"e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69"}],"sha":"79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/79bd9ea5c2082f717cadc4df2d322f9b47c0b966"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:31:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:31:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Wait for the lazy chunk instead of assuming it mounted\n\nThe probe-conversation tests queried content rendered inside the\nlazily-imported ContextProbeResults synchronously. The transcript heading\ncommits in the same pass as the Suspense fallback, so under full-suite\nworker contention the assertion could run while the chunk was still\nloading — the intermittent failure showed the \"Preparing probe results\"\nfallback, not wrong content. findBy* observes the import actually\nsettling; the assertions themselves are unchanged. The one other in-page\nlazy boundary (ArcReceiptDetails) already awaits its chunk before any\nsynchronous query.\n\nReproduced twice in 20 shuffled runs before the change; 35/35 green\nafter, full suite 465/465.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73983ad0461758a2a1c65c48e4bd2bd505bf8dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/73983ad0461758a2a1c65c48e4bd2bd505bf8dfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGU5YWUxNGZkNzllNDFhNjcwYjhmNTc5ZGU0ODE3ZDc5MGYzZGNkNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e","sha":"59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e"}],"sha":"e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e9ae14fd79e41a670b8f579de4817d790f3dcd69"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T18:24:03Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T18:24:03Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Rebuild the experience the audit condemned: hierarchy, voice, anatomy\n\nA user walked the app and rated it 2 out of 10, with fourteen specific\nfrictions. Four senior-UX judge passes over the real screenshots and the\ncode traced them to four systemic causes, and this commit lands the fix\nlist their synthesis produced.\n\nRoot causes, honestly stated. The kit''s as/styleAs split let every compact\ncomponent quiet its own title independently, so card titles rendered at 12px\nunder 14px body and stat values inherited body size - the hierarchy was\ninverted, and no rule required it to be monotonic. Docstring culture leaked\ninto UI copy: honesty rules were satisfied by explaining the implementation\n- cursors, /v1/admin, walks, precedence - when they only required naming the\nabsence. Notices were designed for correctness rather than calm, and placed\nwhere the author finished thinking rather than where the reader needed them.\nAnd navigation was styled as decoration: real child-page links were\nflattened into inert Tag pills because anchors cannot nest, and the\nconstraint was answered by faking the links instead of restructuring the\ncard.\n\nThe type contract is now baked into the kit: page title 32, description 16\nregular, section heading 20, card title 20, nav-card title 16, stat value\n24 as the only display number. SectionHeading is promoted into the kit so\npages stop re-choosing.\n\nEvery navigation is an anchor. LinkButton is a KLink wearing button chrome\nbuilt from Salt''s own actionable tokens - Salt''s Button cannot become an\nanchor and card CTAs rendered as bare text. The first cut used the subtle\nfamily, which is transparent at rest, and the user caught it live within\nthe hour: the bordered look is the unsuffixed actionable family, and the\nselectors are double-class on purpose because Salt''s Link sets color at\nsingle-class specificity and import order was deciding who won.\n\nNavCard is a plain Card with a stretched title anchor and pill links raised\nabove the overlay - the pills navigate to the pages they always named.\n\nThe dashboard leads with Learn the registry, then Explore; \"Your access\" is\ngone (the rail badge and Session Details carry it); the empty at-a-glance is\none line. Graph analytics renames its sections to plain nouns, moves the\nwindow control to the sections it actually governs, lifts caveats above the\nnumbers they qualify, and turns three essays into three quiet lines. The\nContext Lab leads with the composer, fans \"All Sources\" out as one call per\nsource with separately labeled turns, renames and explains Saved Cases and\nhides them when empty, and folds its banner into the description. Health\nand Operational Health are one page - gating is a section concern, not a\nnavigation concern - with /ops/metrics surviving as a redirect. Workspaces''\nread-only banner became a disabled Create button whose tooltip says who can.\nEdge tables resolve names three tiers deep and cells hold their line, with\nper-column wrap for sentence-shaped values.\n\nSidebar children share their parents'' text column - Salt indents by 36px\nsteps while parent text sits an icon-plus-gap in, and the near-miss read as\nmisalignment - and the icon baseline nudge that double-corrected under flex\ncentring is cancelled.\n\nTests that pinned the condemned copy moved to the new strings; the\nworkspaces test now asserts aria-disabled, which is what keeps the refusal\ntooltip reachable by keyboard. 63 end-to-end across both colour modes, 465\nunit, all gates green. One known pre-existing flake in a context-lab test\nremains intermittent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"477ba45f07cbd5e46a46206b598242ff4e46bd28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/477ba45f07cbd5e46a46206b598242ff4e46bd28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDU5YjU0OTQ5N2E0NTcyNmMzNDA1YTdhZjM0ZjRlMzNlZmM0YjVhNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b","sha":"e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b"}],"sha":"59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/59b549497a45726c3405a7af34f4e33efc4b5a5e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:39:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:39:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Move the dashboard toward the reference console''s shape\n\nSix patterns from the console this app is modelled on, applied where they\nsurvive contact with a product that cannot invent numbers.\n\nA greeting instead of the product''s own name. The page opened \"Capability\nRegistry\" to a reader who had just clicked its logo to get there. A console\nis somewhere a person returns to during a working day, and naming them is\nthe cheapest thing it can do to read as somewhere they work.\n\nGreeting by name only when the server gave one a person would answer to.\nUnder client-credentials the actor''s display name is the client id, so this\nfirst rendered \"Good morning, knowledge-ui-consumer\" - worse than no\ngreeting, because the whole value of addressing someone is that it reads as\naddressed rather than generated. The test is shape rather than a list, and\nerrs toward dropping the name.\n\nOne primary action, top right. A landing surface should have exactly one\nobvious next move, and for every role here that is the catalog - the only\ndestination no role is refused.\n\nStat tiles gained the reference''s full anatomy: a badge opposite the label\nfor the qualifier read in the same glance as the number, a small mark beside\nthe value for direction of travel, and one action. The mark carries no axis\nand no labels, because at that size it cannot carry them legibly - anything\na reader needs to compare still belongs in a figure with its data table,\nwhich is a hard rule here and not a preference.\n\nDestination cards list what is in them, taken from each section''s own\nchildren rather than written again - so a card cannot drift from the rail\nbeside it, and adding a page adds its own tag.\n\nSection headings take one link, as the reference pairs every section with\nthe place to go when the summary is not enough. One, never two: two makes it\na toolbar and the eye stops reading either.\n\nA resources row and a quiet footer, both below the sections someone came to\nuse. Every one is a destination this app already serves; nothing links to a\nfeature that does not exist.\n\nWhat did not carry over is the metric density, and that is not a shortfall\nto fix later. The reference can put a number in every card because its API\nserves totals. The list endpoints here serve a page and a cursor, so the\nsame layout filled with counts would be a layout of numbers that mean \"as\nmany as fit on one page\".\n\n63 end-to-end, 465 unit, all gates green. Shell at 402.1 KB against 440.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a38ebbccdace3b87c88fb152c6dd6450b9ac21b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/a38ebbccdace3b87c88fb152c6dd6450b9ac21b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGUxM2I5OWZmZmYwYjA1ODFhNTYwMWVmNjc5YWM3MTE3ZGUzYjNmOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf","sha":"563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf"}],"sha":"e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e13b99ffff0b0581a5601ef679ac7117de3b3f8b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:39:15Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:39:15Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Names instead of ids, an editable entry, and a dashboard that says something\n\nFour pieces of feedback from using the app, which found things the mocked\nlane could not.\n\nNames. EntityLink shipped without the resolver that gives it something to\nshow, so it fell back to a short id nearly everywhere - which is a smaller\nversion of the same defect it was built to fix. useEntityNames resolves the\nids visible on the current page, prefers a name the server already sent,\nshares the detail page''s cache so opening a row it named is warm, and\nleaves an unreadable reference as an id rather than an error, because a\ncross-tenant edge is a fact about visibility. Wired into the impact panel,\nthe claims browser and the usage ranking - the three tables whose own\nendpoints answer with ids and no names. Verified against the live registry:\nthe claims table reads \"Memory Loop Demo\" and a shortened claim id, and no\ncell carries a bare UUID.\n\nTwo unit tests moved, and it is worth being clear that they were asserting\nthe old behaviour rather than being wrong: both demanded the slug where the\ndisplay name now appears, which is the change that was asked for.\n\nReceipts cannot be browsed, and now say so. The inspector asked for a UUID\nthat nothing in the console produces, and the registry publishes no index\nof receipts - only read-by-id. There is no lookup to build. So the page\nnames the absence and says where an id actually comes from, rather than\nleaving a reader hunting for a link that does not exist. This one needs an\nAPI change to fix properly; it is recorded here as a product gap.\n\nWorkspace entries are editable. The endpoint has existed the whole time\nwith no client, so an entry could be created and deleted and never\ncorrected - fixing a typo in a decision record meant deleting it and\nwriting it again, losing the entry''s identity and its place in the feed. A\nworkspace is the one surface in this console a reader owns outright.\n\nThe dashboard says something to the reader who can be told no numbers. A\nconsumer holds none of the aggregate reads, so the summary row was empty\nfor the most common reader on the most-visited page, which is most of why\nit read as plain. It now shows their own recent searches - which claims\nnothing about the tenant, and is the only honest \"at a glance\" available\nwhen the list endpoints serve pages rather than totals.\n\n63 end-to-end, 465 unit, all gates green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b54486b4c49a4294fd5f88d73b7006a3d2710e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/3b54486b4c49a4294fd5f88d73b7006a3d2710e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDU2M2RjYmUzNmRmYjJlMjFkM2VlMDMzYjFiYzliYzkzMWNhN2E3Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3","sha":"566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3"}],"sha":"563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/563dcbe36dfb2e21d3ee033b1bc9bc931ca7a7cf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:30:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:30:58Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Rows are links, verified against a live registry\n\nRunning the app against the real backend found the gap: DataTable had\ngained hasError and skeletons but never the Column.href half, so the main\ncapability list was still a row-level click handler. \"A destination is a\nlink, not a click handler\" was written into the standard and the ADR while\nthe busiest table in the app did not follow it.\n\nColumn.href renders a real anchor in the cell; onRowClick is deleted rather\nthan kept beside it, because two ways to activate a row - one of them a\nfocusable div wrapping an anchor - is the accessibility trap the old\ndocstring was already circling. The hover treatment stays, keyed on the\ntable having a linked column at all.\n\nVerified live: 20 linked cells on /catalog, href=\"/catalog/memory-loop-demo\",\nclick navigates, the four tabs render, and the interface tab routes and\nreports honestly that the capability declares no canonical contract.\n\nWorth recording that the mocked lane could not have caught this. It asserts\ncopy, landmarks, headings and identifiers - all of which passed - because a\nclick handler and a link produce the same rendered text. Only using the app\nshowed it.\n\n63 end-to-end, 465 unit, all gates green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02034d940abbd9ce7007a1e618150a47984fe44b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/02034d940abbd9ce7007a1e618150a47984fe44b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDU2NmVjZDliNTBkZDRmMDgwYWRiYzY1NGQ4ODQ0YjlkZTliYTExYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c","sha":"659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c"}],"sha":"566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/566ecd9b50dd4f080adbc654d8844b9de9ba11a3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:15:11Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:15:11Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Search that answers before you leave the box\n\nThe global search was a navigation form: type, submit, land on the catalog\nlist. Its own docstring said so - \"it is a link, not a live search\" - and\nthat was the right call at the time, because a popover reimplementing the\ncatalog view would hand back a result nobody could link to.\n\nIt still submits to that URL. What it adds is a preview: five hits while\nyou type, each a real link, plus recent searches when the field is empty.\nThe distinction that keeps this from being a second idiom is that the panel\nnever answers - it offers destinations, and the full answer stays one\nkeystroke away at a URL a colleague can be sent.\n\nDeliberately no command palette. It was the obvious thing to build and\nwould have been a second idiom for one job, find a capability, which is the\nrule this repo records having broken twice. The command shortcut focuses\nthis same field instead. One control, two keystrokes.\n\nRecents are per-persona and per-browser: no endpoint stores them, and\nswitching identity changes what a reader can see, so a recent search that\nnow returns nothing is worse than no recent at all.\n\nThe panel claims no listbox semantics, and the accessibility sweep is why.\nThe first version put aria-expanded on the input; an input has the textbox\nrole, which does not support it, and axe called it critical on the first\nrun in both modes. Implementing half a combobox by hand claims semantics\nthat are not delivered, which is worse for a screen reader than a plain\nfield followed by a short list of links. If it ever needs selection, it\nshould become Salt''s ComboBox rather than grow one.\n\nThe floating panel lives in the kit, because that is the only workspace\npermitted a stylesheet. Its offset is a transform rather than a top: inset\nis on the token allow-list and admits no percentage, top happens not to be\nmatched by that rule, and using top would be dodging the constraint rather\nthan working within it.\n\nKnown flake, not introduced here: one context-lab test fails intermittently\nand passes in isolation and on every re-run - four times across this work,\nthree consecutive clean full runs after the last. It is in an untracked\nfile that arrived with the in-flight work, and it looks like cross-test\nstate rather than a product defect.\n\n63 end-to-end across both colour modes, 465 unit, all gates green. Shell at\n401.4 KB against 440, catalog 352.9 against 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80a356c8fc434aa78ceded4823e07b02c25bc37c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/80a356c8fc434aa78ceded4823e07b02c25bc37c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDY1OTExMGRmZjVkZDg0YjIwNDRlMDFkYzA1MTE2M2E0NmU4YWZjNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6","sha":"c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6"}],"sha":"659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/659110dff5dd84b2044e01dc051163a46e8afc6c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:08:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:08:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Three surfaces the API had and the console did not\n\nTwo of these were orphan hooks: typed, exported, and rendered by no route.\nThat pattern is worth naming, because it is what a coverage gap looks like\nfrom the inside - the client layer knew about the endpoint, so nothing\nreported it missing, and only a reader trying to click found out.\n\nClaim detail. useClaim''s own docstring says it exists \"for the citation\ndrill-in\", and there was no page to drill into: the claims browser listed\nevidence counts that could not be opened. The whole point of the page is\nthe citations, and its empty state says the right thing - a served claim is\nrequired to carry evidence, so a claim rendering none here is a contract\nviolation worth reporting rather than an ordinary absence.\n\nSync run detail. The runs table listed failures with a truncated summary\nand no destination, so reading what a connector actually reported meant\ngoing to the server logs. The failure text is rendered verbatim, not\nsummarised - a paraphrased error is one an operator cannot search for. This\nis also the operations remote''s first detail route of any kind; every page\nthere was a list that terminated in itself.\n\nCuration queue, read-only. The registry ships a full curation runbook and\nnone of it had a surface, so the memory-steward persona - whose stated\nquestion is \"is curation producing claims owners accept\" - was served by\none read-only claims list. The queue can now be seen.\n\nIt says read-only rather than implying it. Linking, discarding and\nadjudicating are writes against untrusted observations; each needs a\ncapability entry read from the router and a confirmation naming the effect,\nand inventing either is the guess this repo''s authorization rules exist to\nprevent. Absent and explained beats offered and refused by the server.\n\nTwo ordering traps, both the same shape as one the routes already\ndocumented: claims/queue must precede claims/:claimId or the queue is\nmatched as a claim id, and the curation MSW handler must precede the\nclaim-by-id handler for the same reason. The second cost three sweep\ntimeouts before it was found - with no handler the request never settles,\nso networkidle never fires and the failure looks like a hang rather than a\n404.\n\n63 end-to-end across both colour modes, 465 unit, all gates green, catalog\nat 352.9 KB against 360 with the queue behind a lazy import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"742d7409150ebc479daa63c59493d72f57e82ef9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/742d7409150ebc479daa63c59493d72f57e82ef9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM3OWJmYjQ5NjcwNDYzN2U1MzRkMGMzZDQxZTBjMGFlZjNlMTYwYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52","sha":"53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52"}],"sha":"c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c79bfb496704637e534d0c3d41e0c0aef3e160a6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:59:43Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:59:43Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"A summary row that shrinks by role, and a past view that refuses to write\n\nThe dashboard carried no tiles, and the reasoning behind that still holds\nin full: the catalog list endpoints serve a page and a cursor rather than a\ntotal, so a tile reading \"42 capabilities\" could only ever mean \"42 on the\nfirst page\". Nothing added here counts a list.\n\nWhat was missed is that four endpoints do serve aggregates - the usage\nsummary, owned-capability usage, operational health - and none of them was\non the landing page, so a reader arriving cold met navigation cards and two\nfive-row teasers.\n\nThe row draws only on those, states its window inline, and shrinks by role\nrather than showing zeros: a tile whose source this identity cannot read is\nabsent, and the row says once, in a sentence, that it is. For a consumer or\nan auditor that means no tiles at all, and that is the honest answer -\ntheir dashboard is a dispatch page, and what fixes it is destinations,\nlinks and search rather than invented numbers.\n\nOne derived figure, and it is defensible only for a stated reason: the\nowned-capability list is complete and uncursored, so summing it is\nreporting the response rather than deriving a metric the API did not serve.\nThe tile''s own hint says so.\n\nTime travel. Four endpoints accept as_of and three hooks already took the\nparameter; no page passed it, so a capability''s history was reachable by\nthe API and by nobody reading the console. It lives in the query string,\nbecause a past view is exactly the kind of thing a colleague is sent a link\nto.\n\nThe rule that makes it safe: no writing against a past view. The adoption\ncontrol is hidden rather than disabled under as_of, and a persistent note\nsays why - a decision recorded against a state that is not current would\nnot say that it was, and offering that write is worse than not offering\ntime travel at all. The historical view is in the accessibility sweep.\n\n61 end-to-end across both colour modes, 465 unit, all gates green, catalog\nat 352.3 KB against 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14cfe4f2c2729e26891532b5f7ec5283e1974a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/14cfe4f2c2729e26891532b5f7ec5283e1974a59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDUzOTg4ZTM5YjI5MjM0MDhkODQ5YmZlYmI1ZjlhZGNjZGJjYTVjNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4","sha":"e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4"}],"sha":"53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/53988e39b2923408d849bfebb5f9adccdbca5c52"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:56:11Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:56:11Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Tabs on a capability, and the contract it declares\n\nThe busiest page in the app was one column running impact, then attributes,\nthen every fact, then subscriptions, then optionally record fields - so\n\"what is its contract\" and \"who depends on it\" were separated by a table\nthat can run to hundreds of rows.\n\nViews of one capability are now routed tabs. A path segment rather than\nclick state, for the same reason the rail derives from the route: a tab a\ncolleague cannot be sent a link to is a tab that does not exist for them,\nand it means the accessibility and copy sweeps can visit each one. All\nthree new routes are in both sweeps.\n\nThe interface tab is the largest promised-but-missing surface in the\nproduct. The orientation document tells a consuming team this console shows\n\"what its contract is\"; the endpoint has existed the whole time with no\nclient and no page, so the one question a team asks before depending on\nsomething was the one the app could not answer. It distinguishes three\nstates rather than collapsing them - no contract declared, which is normal\nand true of most capabilities; not readable by this role; and a failed\nread. A 404 here means the capability declares nothing, because the\ncapability itself is on screen.\n\nThe record fields were a toggle that revealed a panel further down the same\npage. That is a second idiom for what tabs already do, and it made the\nreader''s position depend on state no link could carry. It is a tab.\n\nBack to Catalog dropped the query, the lifecycle filter and the type filter,\nso a reader who arrived from a filtered search returned to an unfiltered\nbrowse and rebuilt it by hand. The list now writes its own state into the\nlink and the detail page hands it back.\n\n53 end-to-end across both colour modes plus the three new tab routes, 465\nunit, all gates green, catalog at 352.1 KB against 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2fa3f1ece62902e1e474cc45cd855007c49b733","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/b2fa3f1ece62902e1e474cc45cd855007c49b733"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGU3MjJjYWE5YmMyNDhjZDE3NWQ5Y2UxZTQwNWUxNTVhYzNiNWNlYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a","sha":"c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a"}],"sha":"e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e722caa9bc248cd175d9ce1e405e155ac3b5cec4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:16:07Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T02:16:07Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Every reference is a name and a destination, or a short id and a copy\n\nNine surfaces answered \"which one\" with a bare thirty-six-character UUID\nthat went nowhere: the impact panel''s related-entity column, every claim''s\nsubject, the usage and audit tables, graph analytics, a workspace entry''s\nreferences, and a probe result whose link text was the id while the name\nsat in the card title directly above it. Those are the places a reader is\nmost likely to want to go next. A reader could not tell two rows apart,\ncould not click through, and could not search for what they were looking\nat.\n\nEntityLink renders a name and a link where both are known, a name where\nonly that is, and otherwise the first eight characters in the code face\nwith the whole value in a tooltip and a copy control beside it. Eight is\nenough to tell two rows apart at a glance, which the full id is not, and\nthe whole value stays one keystroke from a support ticket.\n\nA reference the caller cannot resolve stays an id and says why rather than\nrendering as an error. Cross-tenant edges are real - the impact panel''s own\nempty state argues this - so an unreadable reference is a fact about\nvisibility, not a failure.\n\nThe unit tests caught a genuine flaw and were right to. Truncation was by\nlength, and a capability''s handle is its slug, so salt-design-system became\nsalt-des - strictly worse than what it replaced. The rule is now shape: a\nUUID carries nothing in its first eight characters beyond distinguishing\nrows, and anything else is left whole because it may well be the name.\nFixed in the component; not one assertion was changed to accommodate it.\n\nThe operations remote emitted no links at all. It now emits its first, and\nthat needed a contract change: navigateAbsolute can move a reader across\nthe federation boundary but cannot produce an href, so a cross-remote\nreference could only ever be a click handler. The host now supplies\nhrefForRemote, resolved from the same descriptor the rail reads, so a\nremote builds a real anchor into another one without knowing or hard-coding\nwhere it is mounted.\n\nOnly a capability target links from the audit log. The others keep the\nshort id and its copy control rather than pretending to a destination that\ndoes not exist.\n\nAn end-to-end sweep asserts no table cell renders a bare identifier, which\nis the shape of the regression rather than a list of the nine places it\nhappened to be.\n\n53 end-to-end across both colour modes, 465 unit, all gates and the budget\ngreen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"871909335dccf683d87e0af5daf702d00d31d318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/871909335dccf683d87e0af5daf702d00d31d318"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM0NmU2M2MxZTVlNThlZWRjNDE3ZTVmMmVhOTFlYjA4MDA3M2MzN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4","sha":"400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4"}],"sha":"c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c46e63c1e5e58eedc417e5f2ea91eb080073c37a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:57:30Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:57:30Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Re-vendor the API document, and make its drift visible\n\nThe vendored document was forty-two paths behind the running service - 97\nagainst 139 - and nothing could report it. The codegen lane proves the\ngenerated types match the vendored copy; it says nothing about whether that\ncopy matches the service. So whole domains were unreachable by\nconstruction: memory curation, the promotion proposals, claim history, ARC\nauthoring, the capability interface. A client cannot be generated against\nan endpoint it cannot see, and no check went red.\n\nRe-vendored at 139 paths, 185 operations. Types regenerate clean and the\nexisting suite passes unchanged, which is the useful signal here - the\ndrift was additive, so nothing was depending on a shape that moved.\n\nTwo guards, because the failure had two halves.\n\npaths.json is a committed manifest of every method and path, written by\ncodegen and diffed by ci:codegen. The document is forty thousand lines, so\nits diff is one no reviewer reads, which is how it drifted this far in the\nfirst place. The manifest is the same information at a size a person can\ncheck: an added endpoint is one added line.\n\ncheck-spec-freshness compares the vendored document against a running\nservice, on method and path only - a whole-document comparison fails on\nevery description the service words differently, and a guard that cries\nwolf gets switched off. It skips with a notice when nothing is reachable,\nbecause this workflow provisions no backend and a guard that cannot run\nwhere it runs most often is not a guard. Same trade the live end-to-end\nlane already makes.\n\nBoth were verified against a served document with one path added and one\nremoved: the check reports both directions and exits non-zero. A guard\nasserted only in the passing direction is how the last one got here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4700975fafb657325787294d21acd3e0f4a0d924","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/4700975fafb657325787294d21acd3e0f4a0d924"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDQwMGQ1OWUzMzI5MjQ1YzExMjllYTAwYzJlYjNjYmM4ODMxYTFjYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c","sha":"c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c"}],"sha":"400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/400d59e3329245c1129ea00c2eb3cbc8831a1cc4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:54:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:54:05Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Skeletons that cannot drift, a dark accessibility sweep, and named absences\n\nThird UX pass. Four of these are defects rather than polish.\n\nThe receipt inspector rendered a permanent spinner. useArcReceipt is\nenabled on a receipt id, and a disabled query in react-query v5 reports\nisPending true - pending in the sense of having no data, not in the sense\nof a request being in flight. So a top-level rail destination showed its\nempty state and a spinner labelled \"Reading ARC receipt\", forever, with\nnothing asked for. The unit test asserted the empty state and the absence\nof an error, which is exactly the pair that leaves this invisible; it now\nasserts the spinner is absent too.\n\nFour pages rendered an error banner and, directly beneath it, \"nothing has\nbeen published in this tenant yet\". Those are different facts calling for\ndifferent actions - retry, versus publish something - and the second was\nnot known. DataTable takes hasError and stops falling through.\n\nSeven tables took DataTable''s generic \"Nothing to show\" with no\ndescription, against this repo''s own rule that an absence says what is\nabsent and why. Each now names its own.\n\nThe workspace detail page replaced its whole header with a spinner, losing\nits title and heading for the length of the read. The capability detail\npage already kept its header through every state.\n\nThe context lab used an error panel for a role refusal where the rest of\nthe app uses an unavailable notice. Two idioms for one state is what makes\na console read as assembled rather than designed.\n\nSkeletons. This kit refused them, and the reasoning was sound: a skeleton\nmust mirror its content, and a mirror that drifts is worse than an honest\nspinner. What made that decisive was an assumed shape of the answer - a\ncomponent exported to pages, each hand-composing a wireframe. The drift is\na property of hand-composition, not of skeletons. So the bar is internal\nand unreachable from any page, and DataTable generates its placeholder from\nthe same columns array that builds the real header and cells. There is no\nsecond description of the shape to drift. Ships with the repo''s first\nprefers-reduced-motion block.\n\nThe empty state has the icon the standard has specified since it was\nwritten and which the component never rendered. Fixed rather than passed\nin: thirty empty states with thirty icons is a second vocabulary nobody\nagreed to, and the state is always the same state.\n\nThe accessibility sweep now runs light and dark over every route, and\nasserts the mode took before trusting the result - a dark run that silently\nrendered light is a green result for a check that never happened. The\nstandard claimed this gate for a long time without having it, which had a\nlive cost: unstyled anchors are worst in exactly the mode nothing checked.\nThat row is now true, and says so.\n\nLayout gained three width tiers and a two-column primitive built on Salt''s\nGridLayout and GridItem, neither of which was used. Every page was a\nvertical stack inside a 1200px cap, which is most of what made the console\nread as sparse - the cap was right for prose and for a page of one table,\nand never right for a page with an aside.\n\nBundle. The additions took remotes/catalog to 360.5 KB gz against a 360\nbudget, so the five largest routes - the graph area, the context lab, the\nreceipt inspector - moved behind lazy imports, which brought it to 351.0.\nWorth recording for the next person: deleting dead exports buys nothing\nhere, because unused exports were already tree-shaken. SidebarBack''s\nremoval moved the number by zero. A lazy route boundary is the only lever\nmanualChunks cannot replace under Module Federation.\n\n52 end-to-end pass across both colour modes, 465 unit, all static gates and\nthe budget green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8377983a5759109a84978530347618b1fdc8b518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/8377983a5759109a84978530347618b1fdc8b518"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM3YmNjNWQ4YWU2ZTU2Mzc5MzNhMzk3MjVmMGQ1NTI5MDVkZmJlNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519","sha":"9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519"}],"sha":"c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7bcc5d8ae6e5637933a39725f0d552905dfbe6c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:39:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:39:47Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Style every anchor, and make the rail nest instead of drill\n\nTwo UX passes, plus the in-flight work that was already in the tree when\nthey started. That mixing is not ideal and is called out here rather than\nhidden: the Graph pages, Context Lab, the workspaces surfaces, the\nHomePage-to-DashboardPage rename and their tests were uncommitted and\ninterleave with these changes in App.tsx, DashboardPage.tsx, registry.ts\nand the end-to-end specs, so they could not be separated by hunk without\nguessing at intent.\n\nAnchors. Nothing in this repo styled an <a>. Not Salt''s global.css, which\nis thirty-nine lines and touches no anchor; not the next theme; not the one\nglobal sheet here. So seventeen inline links across ten files rendered at\nthe user agent''s default - blue, underlined, purple once visited, and very\nnearly black on black in dark mode. Salt ships a Link that handles all four\nstates plus the visited token and the external-link screen-reader text, and\nit had zero consumers.\n\nKLink is that component with a routing seam. The adapter is installed three\ntimes - shell, catalog, operations - because workspace packages are excluded\nfrom the share contract, so each remote carries its own copy of the kit and a\nReact context is identified by object identity. A provider mounted only in\nthe shell would be invisible to every component in a remote, and every link\nover there would silently become a full page load. Each installation says so\nin a docstring, because deleting two of the three as duplication is the\nobvious next mistake.\n\nA restricted-import rule now bans the bare router Link in pages and\ncomponents, exempting the three installations and the app frame, where a\nLink handed to Salt''s render prop is the anchor Salt renders rather than an\nunstyled one. Verified by reintroducing one and watching lint fail.\n\nNavigation. The rail replaced its own contents on entering a section, with a\nback link to the dashboard as the only exit, so a lateral move cost three\nnavigations. No reader of this product works inside one section for a\nsession: a producer''s loop crosses into the other remote and back, an\nauditor''s crosses all three sections. Salt''s NavigationItem has published\nparent, expanded, level and blurActive the whole time - the replace-the-panel\nbehaviour was never a constraint of the component.\n\nSections are now disclosures owning no route, which also dissolved a\nduplicate: every section''s href was its own first child''s, so two rows went\nto the same place and only the child could carry aria-current. Collapse state\npersists beside the rail width, and a collapsed section holding the current\npage is marked rather than left inert.\n\nNesting then exposed a latent naming bug it is worth recording the shape of:\nthe app home and Graph''s index were both labelled Dashboard. Under the\ndrill-down they were never on screen together, so nothing could see it. Five\nlabel-to-title mismatches are reconciled. The general rule now sits in the\nstandard - a name only has to be unique among the things visible at the same\ntime, and nesting changes what those are.\n\nThe breadcrumb went from two segments to four, entity-aware, built from the\npath because the pages that would report it live in remotes and a context\ndoes not cross that boundary. It deliberately carries no aria-current: the\nrail already marks the current page, and an end-to-end invariant asserts no\ntwo elements claim it. That invariant caught this on the first run.\n\nAlso corrected: the standard claimed accessibility was enforced \"light and\ndark\". There is no dark sweep anywhere in the end-to-end specs. The row is\nnow split and marked honestly until the sweep is built, because a table\nclaiming a gate it does not have is the same defect as a number claiming a\nstrength it cannot bear - and this one had a live cost, since unstyled\nanchors are worst in the mode it never ran.\n\nSidebarBack deleted, now unreachable. Worth knowing for later: removing it\nmoved the bundle by zero, because unused exports were already tree-shaken.\nremotes/catalog sits at 359.8 KB gz against a 360 budget, so surfaces added\nlater need route-level lazy loading rather than dead-code removal.\n\n39 end-to-end pass across the built artefacts, 465 unit, lint, stylelint,\ntypecheck, all four guards and the bundle budget green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bce6558ffff5db89029596ba86648b58c2d3cee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/bce6558ffff5db89029596ba86648b58c2d3cee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDkyNDhjZTkyMzU3MGMxYjI3OGI3ZjMyZmRjMDM3YjA3YTUyYmY1MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217","sha":"637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217"}],"sha":"9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9248ce923570c1b278b7f32fdc037b07a52bf519"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:30:13Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:30:13Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Correct two documents that now claim less enforcement than exists\n\n`CLAUDE.md` said \"No guard checks idiom\" and the design standard listed button and\nheader case as agreed-only. Both were true when written and are not now.\n\nA document that understates its gates is a smaller problem than one that overstates\nthem, but it is the same defect: the next person writing a label does not know\nwhether anything will catch them, and the reviewer does not know what is already\ncovered. The standard''s own rule about this is that a rule claiming a gate it does\nnot have is the same defect as a number claiming a strength it cannot bear — which\ncuts both ways.\n\nThree rows moved out of the agreed-only gap, and the note records *how*, because\nthat is the reusable part: each was a rule about what reaches the screen, so none of\nthem was ever going to be a lint rule, and each became an assertion in the\nend-to-end lane — the only one that sees rendered output across a host and two\nremotes.\n\nNumeric alignment gets written down as the cautionary example. It was declared for\nevery numeric column in the app and never once took effect, and no gate saw it,\nbecause jsdom computes no styles, stylelint checks form rather than effect, and the\ntoken guard checks that a token resolves rather than that the declaration wins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95b3218d25e4be1749769177c8fee1c60e4b598f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/95b3218d25e4be1749769177c8fee1c60e4b598f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDYzN2E0NGMzYzE0OTkyNDRhZDU4Nzg1ZDEzM2JhMWM5MTU2ZjEyMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f","sha":"83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f"}],"sha":"637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/637a44c3c1499244ad58785d133ba1c9156f1217"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:29:28Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:29:28Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Make the two checkable copy rules a gate, and fix the two labels that broke them\n\nThe design standard is mostly agreement — no rule can judge whether a button''s\nnoun is the *right* noun. But two of its rules are shape rather than judgement: a\nbutton label is Title Case, and a table header is a Title Case noun rather than a\nsentence. Both had drifted twice, in both directions, on pages nobody reopened.\n\nThe stragglers this time were \"Add a source\" and \"Run now\" on the sync connectors\npage, sitting two clicks from \"Adopt Capability\", \"Mark Read\" and \"Subscribe to\nChanges\". A sweep of every button in the app across twelve routes as an admin found\nexactly those two out of fourteen distinct labels — which is the argument for\nautomating it rather than looking again: fourteen is small enough that a human pass\nfinds most of them and reliably misses the last two.\n\nSo `e2e/specs/copy.spec.ts`. This is the only lane that can check it: the labels are\nstrings scattered across a host and two remotes, some conditional on a role or on\nform state, and the rule is about what reaches the screen — which no lint rule sees\nand no component test enumerates.\n\nDeliberately narrow. It checks capitalisation, minor-word exceptions, and stray\narticles, and nothing else, because everything past that is taste and a guard that\noverreaches gets disabled. `p95` is exempted by name: it is a statistical notation\nand \"P95\" would be wrong rather than tidier.\n\nVerified in both directions rather than assumed, which is the part that matters for\na new guard. With \"Add Source\" reverted to \"Add a source\" the spec fails and names\nthe label and the reason; restored, it passes. A gate never seen to fail is a gate\nnobody should trust — and this one had a near miss during verification, when a\n`git checkout` used to undo the probe silently reverted the real fix along with it.\n\nGates: lint, stylelint, typecheck, four guards, prettier, 385 unit tests, 33 mocked\nend-to-end tests, bundle budget.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ddd8bbde718821df084e995f04b372b714822d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/6ddd8bbde718821df084e995f04b372b714822d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDgzYjhlY2UzNDk3NTYwYjM0OGYwMjU4YzRlYjhiOTY0ZDdkMTgzMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6","sha":"9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6"}],"sha":"83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/83b8ece3497560b348f0258c4eb8b964d7d1832f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:24:21Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:24:21Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Render a timestamp the same way everywhere, and say why a date differs\n\nThree spellings of \"put a moment on screen\" had accumulated: a raw\n`2026-08-01T10:00:00Z` printed verbatim into the notifications inbox, and\n`new Date(x).toLocaleString()` written out twice. The raw one is the defect — a\nreader has to convert it in their head before it answers the only question the\ncolumn is there to answer.\n\nOne `instantText` helper, and the interesting part is that it deliberately does\nthe opposite of `isoDay`:\n\nA **date** is rendered as served, in UTC. Localising moves it — a UTC midnight\nwest of Greenwich lands on the previous day — so a value the server was precise\nabout would disagree with the API by one.\n\nAn **instant** is rendered locally. It carries a time of day, so there is no\nmidnight to fall off, and \"how long ago was this, for me\" is the question being\nasked of it.\n\nTwo functions rather than one with a flag, because the choice follows from what the\nvalue *is*, and a caller passing the wrong flag would get a plausible answer. The\ntests assert the boundary in both directions, so whoever adds the next timestamp\ncolumn has to pick.\n\nAlso: the notifications table showed a visible caption reading \"Notifications\",\ndirectly under a page heading reading \"Notifications\", in a third size.\n\nGates: lint, stylelint, typecheck, four guards, prettier, 385 unit tests, 31\nmocked end-to-end tests. Browser: 22 route loads light and dark, zero console\nerrors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40399c80559ae5a6c9fa7db781930e8eea93c241","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/40399c80559ae5a6c9fa7db781930e8eea93c241"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDlmOGE4MzliYmM3NjhiNWQ3MmE5YmY2YTE1MjY5M2Q0NjI5ZWMwZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45","sha":"b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45"}],"sha":"9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/9f8a839bbc768b5d72a9bf6a152693d4629ec0d6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:21:10Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:21:10Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Give a refused route the heading its page would have had\n\nEvery capability-gated route rendered a document with no headings at all. The\nguard replaces the whole screen, including the `PageHeader` the screen would have\nrendered, so `/ops/audit` and `/ops/sync` had no `h1`, no `h2` and no outline.\n\nA sighted reader could at least read the banner. A screen-reader user landed on a\nheading-less document that never said which page had refused them — and the\nrefusal is the one state where knowing the destination matters most, because for\nthe audit log being refused is correct rather than broken: the registry collapses\na principal to one role and guards that endpoint on auditor specifically, so an\nadmin is turned away by design and the fix is to authenticate as someone else.\n\nNothing caught it. axe is right not to object — a document with no headings breaks\nno success criterion it checks — and the spec that would have caught it asserted\nthe heading outline on the home route only, which was already correct.\n\nSo `RequireCapability` takes the destination''s name and renders it as the heading,\nand each of the four call sites supplies one: the two remote sections read theirs\nfrom the same descriptor the navigation rail reads, so a refused section is titled\nexactly as its nav entry. `GuardedAdmin` gained the prop rather than inferring it,\nbecause it wraps two different pages and cannot know which one it replaced.\n\nTwo test changes, and the second is the more interesting one:\n\nThe heading assertion now runs over every route rather than the home page. That is\nthe gap, not a nicety — a check that only visits the route already passing cannot\nfail.\n\nAnd `admin.spec.ts` was asserting the *absence of the heading* as its proxy for\n\"the page did not render\". That proxy is now invalid by construction, so it asserts\nthe connector table instead — which is what actually separates a refusal from the\npage, and was the real intent all along.\n\nGates: lint, stylelint, typecheck, four guards, prettier, 381 unit tests, 31\nmocked end-to-end tests, bundle budget. Verified in a browser: `/ops/audit` and\n`/ops/sync` each report exactly one `h1`, as a consumer and as an admin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14c11e210461ad453c15f473d2b610fdb8843a86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/14c11e210461ad453c15f473d2b610fdb8843a86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGI3OWU0NzA0MmIxY2U2MmJkZjQyOTIwM2VjZTM3NDc1MDUwMzVhNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8","sha":"a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8"}],"sha":"b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b79e47042b1ce62bdf429203ece3747505035a45"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:16:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T11:16:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Fix eight defects a browser found and the test suite could not\n\nEvery gate was green before this commit and every one of these was visible on\nscreen. Worth recording, because it is an argument about what the gates are for:\naxe, stylelint and a token allow-list check that a rule is *well formed*, not\nthat it *takes effect*, and jsdom computes no stylesheets at all. So the whole\nclass of \"declared, overridden, silently dead\" is invisible to all of them.\n\n**Colour mode ignored the reader''s operating system and did not survive a\nreload.** `useState(''light'')`, hardcoded, unpersisted. A machine configured for\ndark got a bright white console, and a reader who toggled it got light again on\nthe next hard navigation — while the same component tree already persists the\nnavigation rail''s width. Now seeded from `prefers-color-scheme`, stored, and read\nback in an effect rather than a state initialiser so the standalone harnesses''\nbuild-time render still has no `window`.\n\n**Numeric alignment had never once worked, in two different ways.** It was\ndeclared and not read; then read, and the CSS module class it resolved to was\noutranked by Salt''s own `table.saltTable td { text-align: start }` — an element\nplus a class beats a lone hashed class. `text-align: right` was set and lost, and\nthe comment above the prop claimed a fix that had not landed. Salt''s `TD`/`TH`\ntake a `textAlign` prop that emits the class its own rule is keyed on; alignment\ngoes through that now and figures stay a class, safely, because Salt sets no\n`font-variant-numeric` anywhere. Measured after: the header and all three totals\nof a column share a text right edge at 1027px. `align`''s union lost `''left''` and\n`''center''` — Salt''s cells accept neither, and a member that resolves to \"do\nnothing\" invites writing it and expecting something.\n\n**A table caption was centred by the browser''s default stylesheet**, so the two\ntables that show one put a centred line above a left-aligned grid — the only\ncentred text on either page.\n\n**Four queue tiles rendered as three at 262px and one at 775px.** `FlowLayout`\nsizes each child to its content, and the wide one was wide because it was the tile\nwith a non-zero count and therefore the one carrying a sentence explaining the\nconsequence: the tile that mattered most looked like a mistake. A `TileGrid`\nprimitive in the kit fixes the column ramp once for the three surfaces that need\nit, rather than leaving them to disagree.\n\n**A raw `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z`** in the impact table, beside `2026-07-01`\neverywhere else — and a `toLocaleDateString` in the capability list that is worse\nthan untidy: a UTC date parsed and rendered locally lands on the previous day for\nevery reader behind Greenwich. One `isoDay` helper, deliberately unlocalised,\nbecause these are provenance values a reader reconciles against an API response.\n\n**Two identical amber \"Partial Answer\" boxes, stacked**, when a traversal reports\ntwo caveats — the exact shape this repo''s own rules say a caveat must never reach.\nOne note, both sentences.\n\n**A filter labelled \"Depth\" that lists personas**, two clicks from an impact panel\nwhose \"Depth\" genuinely holds the traversal depths 1 to 5. Now \"Persona\".\n\n**A fixture that contradicted itself**: `lifecycle: ''ga''` at the top level and\n`attributes.lifecycle = {state: ''beta''}` beneath, rendering a `ga` tag beside the\ntitle and a `beta` row in the attributes list. The registry''s own capability\nschema says the top-level value derives from the attribute, so the disagreement\nwas not a harder case — it was one the API cannot produce.\n\nTests for what is now testable: `isoDay` including the timezone shift it exists to\navoid, and a `DataTable` suite asserting Salt''s alignment classes reach the header\nand every cell — the mechanism, since jsdom cannot see the pixels.\n\nGates: lint at `--max-warnings 0`, stylelint, typecheck across five projects,\nfour guards, prettier, 381 unit tests, 30 mocked end-to-end tests including axe on\n11 routes, bundle budget (396/342/344 KB gz against 440/360/360).\n\nBrowser: 22 route loads across light and dark as admin, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"828da9461baad414d205153dfffb141eece7dff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/828da9461baad414d205153dfffb141eece7dff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE5NTUzODAwNGEzNjEzZDE3NTljZDkyMTQxOWUzZTBmYjYxMzQ3Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38","sha":"7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38"}],"sha":"a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a95538004a3613d1759cd921419e3e0fb61347f8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T10:01:20Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T10:01:20Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Turn on type-aware and a11y linting, and fix what it found\n\nThree plugins the repo should have had from the start: `@typescript-eslint`''s\ntype-checked rules, `jsx-a11y`, and `no-only-tests`. A heavily async React app\nwith no `no-floating-promises` and no edit-time accessibility check was relying\non review to catch two classes of defect that a compiler already knows about.\n\nTurning them on cost one configuration decision and found 17 real problems.\n\n**Configuration.** `parserOptions.projectService` is the modern spelling and the\nwrong one here: it only auto-discovers files named `tsconfig.json`, and the tier\nholding the e2e specs, the test setup and the Vite configs is deliberately\ncovered by `tsconfig.tooling.json` — those files ship in no package. The service\nreported all seven as \"not found\", which is true and unhelpful. An explicit\nproject list, globbed per workspace so a new workspace needs no edit here.\n\n`jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-tabindex` is widened to admit `separator`. The\nplugin''s role table is right in general and wrong for a window splitter: ARIA\ndefines a focusable separator as a widget, and the rule''s only other satisfying\nanswer is a resize handle no keyboard can reach — the outcome it exists to\nprevent. Named in the config rather than disabled at the call site, so the next\nresizable surface inherits the judgement.\n\n**Six `[object Object]` sites.** Five in a table cell, a page title, a `Tag` and\na row key; one in the message a failed form submit renders. `String(value)` on an\nobject produces a string a reader cannot act on *and* cannot distinguish from\ndata, so the field it replaced is silently gone and nobody reports it — the same\nclass of defect as rendering zero for an absent number. One `displayText` helper\nin the kit, serialising rather than summarising, and `describeThrown` in the\nclient for the thrown-value case. Both narrow positively, because TypeScript does\nnot narrow `unknown` on the negative side of a `typeof` test and the natural\nspelling leaves the hazard in place.\n\n**Three promise misuses.** `authRef.current?.getToken() ?? Promise.resolve(null)`\nput a promise on the left of a nullish test in the shell and both standalone\nharnesses — correct by accident, and indistinguishable from the mistake it looks\nlike. Awaiting first tests the value. `CopyButton` handed an async function to\n`onClick`, which discards the promise silently; it now says `void`, which records\nthat the rejection is handled rather than leaving it to be inferred.\n\n**A `<button role=\"separator\">`** in the navigation rail. The roles a `<button>`\nmay take are an enumerated list and `separator` is not on it, so the element and\nthe role described two different things. Now a `div` with `tabindex`, which is\nthe documented splitter pattern — and needed three fewer CSS declarations, since\nthere is no button chrome left to reset.\n\nPlus: `switchTo` declared `async` while awaiting nothing (the interface promises a\npromise because credential swapping is I/O in general; this implementation says\nso explicitly), a stubbed `fetch` doing the same, an untyped ESLint config API\nconfined to one line, a redundant assertion, and `Element.prototype.scrollIntoView`\ntested by descriptor — the two obvious spellings are a detached method reference\nand a narrowing to `never`, since the DOM lib declares a method jsdom lacks.\n\nGates: lint clean at `--max-warnings 0`, stylelint, typecheck across five\nprojects, four guards, prettier, 372 tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18ba43c0b3beccfd1a0a67a82c816ca21d050205","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/18ba43c0b3beccfd1a0a67a82c816ca21d050205"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDczODc5MTRiNTI3MDIwMTE4YTZiNDMyNDJjMTA4NmIxZmJiNTBjMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044","sha":"445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044"}],"sha":"7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7387914b527020118a6b43242c1086b1fbb50c38"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:43:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:43:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Make the app match the design standard, and correct the standard where it was wrong\n\nThe standard described an app that did not exist. Buttons read \"Back\", \"Adopt\",\n\"Show bitemporal fields\"; several table headers were sentence case; heading tracking\nwas applied to exactly one component. Closing that is the work here — and checking it\nagainst the rendered screen rather than the tests turned up a defect I had introduced\nmyself.\n\n**Copy.** Every button is Title Case with a noun where the verb alone left the reader\nguessing what: \"Adopt Capability\", \"Unadopt Capability\", \"Subscribe to Changes\",\n\"Save Connector\", \"Reload Page\", \"Back to Catalog\", \"Mark Read\". Table headers are\nTitle Case nouns. Two deliberate exceptions, because applying a rule mechanically is\nhow a rule stops being right: the per-row Deactivate action keeps the bare verb —\nthe row already names the connector, and repeating it twelve times is noise — and\n`p95` stays lowercase, because it is the name of a statistic rather than a word.\n\n**Tabular figures, and the API needed splitting to do it.** Right alignment already\nimplied tabular figures, on the argument that counts want both. Timestamps want the\nfigures and not the alignment: their values are all the same length, so right-aligning\npulls them off the label beside them, while proportional digits make adjacent rows\ndisagree by a pixel per digit. So `align` decides where a column sits and `figures`\ndecides how its digits are cut. A real count in the metrics table also turned out to\nbe left-aligned with proportional digits, which is what the coupling was supposed to\nprevent.\n\n**Heading tracking** now applies to card headings as well as page titles, which\npreviously disagreed on a property the reference applies to both. Per component by\nnecessity: Salt defines two letter-spacing tokens, neither per style, and `Text`\npublishes no variable for it.\n\n**The screenshot found what the tests could not.** The claims table had nine columns\nand broke `salt-design-system` across three lines — a density problem I created while\nfixing a judge''s blocker that demanded every served field be rendered. Nine columns\nwas the wrong reading of that: the requirement is that a field reaches the screen, not\nthat it gets a column. The category now sits with the predicate and the authority with\nthe evidence, each pair answering one question. Seven columns, every field still\nvisible, rows a third shorter. The test that guarded this was updated to assert the two\nmoved fields by value rather than by header, so it still fails if either disappears.\n\n**And the standard itself was wrong about four components.** It listed `Toast`,\n`EntityRow`, `Skeleton` and `Tabs` as still to build. Salt ships the whole Tabs family;\n`LinkCard` and `InteractableCard` *are* a descriptive row with one action; a skeleton\nis not in Salt and is not worth custom CSS when `Spinner` exists. Only the toast\ndecision survives, and for a behavioural reason rather than a technical one. A standard\nthat lists components without checking the design system first grows a parallel kit —\nthe answer was \"Salt has this\" three times out of four.\n\nAlso fixes a live wrong instruction: the unadopt dialog told readers to cancel the\nsubscription \"from Subscriptions\", which is nowhere. There is no such destination and\nthere cannot easily be one, since subscriptions are readable per capability with no\nendpoint listing a tenant''s own across all of them. It now names the panel further\ndown the same page, which is where the subscription can actually be cancelled.\n\n363 tests, full pipeline green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca86b2dbdbd25604d3094ba05547cbe02950c59b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/ca86b2dbdbd25604d3094ba05547cbe02950c59b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDQ0NWFjZjIwNGZlNjFlYzJjZDNkZjBiNzY1ZjliMTM1YzIwNTEwNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f","sha":"a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f"}],"sha":"445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/445acf204fe61ec2cd3df0b765f9b135c2051044"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:21:21Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:21:21Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Audit the whole kit against the Salt-first rule, and record what survives it\n\nThe rule applies to the repo, not only to what was added under it, so I went\nlooking. The result is mostly reassuring and worth writing down so the four\nlegitimate cases are not \"fixed\" by the next reader.\n\nAcross pages and components there are exactly four raw elements outside the kit, all\n`strong` for inline emphasis — and Salt''s text components have no emphasis variant\n(`Text`, `Label`, `Code`, `Display`, `Headings`, `TextAction`, `TextNotation`), so\nthere is nothing to compose instead.\n\nInside the kit, which is the sanctioned place for gap-filling, the three\nnon-layout elements each hold up: the resize handle is a real `button` carrying\n`role=\"separator\"` and a width value, which Salt''s `Button` would fight on both\nstyling and role; the rail is a `nav` landmark, and Salt ships no landmark wrapper;\nthe chart mark is an `svg`, and Salt ships no chart primitive. All three are now\nnamed in the conventions file so the reasoning is available before someone tries to\nremove them.\n\nAlso drops a constant I exported from the request mocks and never used — added while\nmoving the silent-surface fixture into the scenarios file, and dead the moment that\nmove finished.\n\n363 tests, full pipeline green: coverage 65.3% / 57.8% / 65.1% / 67.6%, bundles at\n395.4 / 341.6 / 343.9 KB gz against 440 / 360 / 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca60a6bf859faab435405bf60562e1243f784f0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/ca60a6bf859faab435405bf60562e1243f784f0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE2MGY4ZTE5NDczNTU4OTdlMjNjOTM3NzM0MGEzYTY5YmZjYmUwOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917","sha":"f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917"}],"sha":"a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a60f8e1947355897e23c9377340a3a69bfcbe09f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:19:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:19:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Fix four defects a second defect hunt found, including my own documented trap\n\n**The fixture invented a surface the API cannot emit.** The summary handler returned\na third surface, `webhook`, carrying the \"a real zero is not an absence\" case. The\nendpoint declares `Literal[\"rest\", \"mcp\"]` and the vendored schema closes the enum to\nthose two — so the load-bearing invariant of the whole page was only ever exercised\nagainst a value production can never produce. This is verbatim the trap written into\nthis repo''s own conventions a few commits earlier: a fixture must never be richer\nthan the endpoint it stands for. I wrote that rule and then broke it.\n\nNothing caught it, and the reason is worth recording: a handler passes a plain object\nliteral to `HttpResponse.json`, so no generic ties it to the response schema.\nTypeScript infers a type *from* the fixture and checks the fixture against it, which\nis a tautology. The typecheck was clean throughout.\n\nSo the real zero moved to a scenario override — which is where per-test overrides\nbelong, and gives that file another caller — and a new parity test reads the vendored\ndocument and fails on any surface literal outside the enum. Two closed vocabularies\nare now checked, and the test also asserts the enum is still closed at all, so opening\nit becomes a deliberate decision rather than a silent widening.\n\n**A date was truncated rather than parsed.** `toDay` sliced the first ten characters\noff a string, which is a no-op on anything shorter — so `2026-8-4`, the same calendar\nday without zero padding, survived intact, compared unequal to the server''s\n`2026-08-04`, and rendered a false \"this is not the window you asked for\" on the one\npage whose entire purpose is not overstating anything. It would also have been\nrejected by the endpoint, which binds these as real dates. Now parsed and re-emitted,\nthrowing on an unparseable value — the pattern `toApiTimestamp` beside it already had.\n\n**Nothing checked the outgoing query parameters.** The response schema uses\n`start`/`end` while the query takes `from`/`to`, so renaming one to match the other is\na natural slip that every existing test would have survived, because the request mocks\nanswer the same payload regardless of what they are asked for. That discipline was\nadded for the impact traversal after a parameter turned out wrong on the wire, and it\nwas never extended here. It is now.\n\n**The fifth read was rendered nowhere.** The commit adding the console said five\nendpoints served it; the page had four panels. The capability ranking was wired end to\nend — hook, key, export, cache-key test — with no reader-visible surface. It answers a\ndistinct question from the tool ranking, so it is now a panel: which capabilities\ncallers asked about, which is demand rather than catalogue.\n\nAlso confirmed by that hunt, and worth recording as checked rather than assumed: the\ndate walk handles month, year and leap boundaries and cannot loop on a reversed range;\nrecomputing the window every render does not thrash the cache, because keys are hashed\nstructurally; the shell''s test alias does not pick up the remotes'' own tests or double\ncount coverage; and the two usage capabilities match their routers exactly.\n\n363 tests, coverage 65.4%, ratchet raised to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bf1ce80950f476302950373fef64cf6c6bece6a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/1bf1ce80950f476302950373fef64cf6c6bece6a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGY0ZTNhYjY4NjRkMWU1NGRiODYxNWQ0OTdlYTI5NmNhNmVjNTc5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc","sha":"35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc"}],"sha":"f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f4e3ab6864d1e54db8615d497ea296ca6ec57917"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:12:35Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:12:35Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Rebuild both new primitives on Salt, and drop three stylesheets\n\nSalt components are the default here, and custom markup or CSS needs a reason. The\ntwo primitives added a few commits ago did not have one.\n\n**The note was a hand-rolled `div` with a CSS module** — a leading rule, four colour\nvariants, its own padding — to reproduce the margin-note look the reference uses.\nSalt ships this component: `status` carries exactly those four states, `variant`\ncarries emphasis, `BannerActions` is the action slot. So the custom version bought an\nappearance and gave up the accessibility, keyboard and theming work Salt maintains,\nand put a second idiom for \"tell the reader something\" into a repo whose standard is\nlargely about not having those. It is now composition on `Banner`, contributing the\ncopy discipline and the two structural constraints — no dismiss, one action — and\nnothing visual.\n\n**The metadata block was raw `dl`/`dt`/`dd` with a CSS grid.** Semantic markup is a\nreal argument and it lost to a simpler one: a bespoke stylesheet for a two-column\nblock is a layout Salt''s primitives already do. `FlexLayout` with a fixed-basis first\ncolumn gives the same alignment, wraps the same way, and inherits the spacing scale\ninstead of restating it. The labelled region is kept, so the block still says what it\ndescribes.\n\n**The dialog radius moved out of a component stylesheet** into the one global sheet\nthat exists for filling Salt gaps, set through `--saltDialog-borderRadius` — Salt''s\npublished variable for it. A component should not need a stylesheet to be the right\nshape.\n\nNet effect: fifteen stylesheets where there were eighteen, and two components with\nbehaviour maintained upstream rather than by us.\n\nThe rule is now written down in both places it belongs — the conventions file an\nagent reads first, and the design standard — including where the escape hatch is,\nbecause \"the reference looks slightly different\" is not on its own a reason to write\nCSS.\n\n354 tests, full pipeline green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f94f310746663496e4d5d8fe8850d59ea5ec249e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/f94f310746663496e4d5d8fe8850d59ea5ec249e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDM1YTE5ZmI1N2E3YmM0NjFiMDBmNDJlNGQzN2ZiMDg5YjNmMGY2ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f","sha":"c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f"}],"sha":"35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/35a19fb57a7bc461b00f42e4d37fb089b3f0f6fc"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:06:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:06:52Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Build the Note primitive, and retire five hand-rolled versions of it\n\nThe standard called for an inline note and the app did not have one, so five\ncaveats had been built out of whatever was nearby: a card with prose for the recall\nwarning, a card for the usage page''s closing caveat, bare secondary text for the\ntraversal caveats and the omitted-days notice. Five spellings of one idea, which is\nprecisely how a console starts reading as assembled rather than designed.\n\n`Note` has four variants chosen by meaning, and two properties that are structural\nrather than conventional:\n\n**No dismiss, ever.** Not an omission — a reader who closes a caveat to clear the\nscreen has removed it while it still applies, and on the claims page that caveat is\na content-trust boundary. Where a caveat is uniform across every row, it belongs\nhere once rather than per row, because an identical marker repeated becomes chrome\nthe eye stops seeing.\n\n**One action slot, not children.** Two buttons make a note a decision point, and a\ndecision belongs in a dialog or a form.\n\nThe docstring spends most of its length on when *not* to use it, because there are\nnow three ways to tell a reader something and the difference is load-bearing: a note\nqualifies data on the panel, an unavailable notice says the data cannot be fetched,\nan empty state says the query found nothing and will fill later. Reaching for the\nwrong one is the failure this component could easily become.\n\n**The bridge got a guard rather than an exemption.** Styling the variants needed\nnamed colour roles, and permitting `var(--kui-*)` in the stylelint allow-list would\nhave opened a hole straight through the token rule — `--kui-notePalette-accent:\n#ff00ff` would have satisfied every check. So `check-salt-tokens` now proves every\nnamed role is defined as one Salt token and nothing else. Verified by writing that\nexact magic value and watching it fail. Thirteen named roles, all checked.\n\n354 tests, full pipeline green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b2ba5a69096a204f02f9c9b069ad0e3eddfb7f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/7b2ba5a69096a204f02f9c9b069ad0e3eddfb7f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM5MmMzYjUyZjI0NDBiYzE2MmM4YWY2NGMzZmVhYjUzNzdhY2QzMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719","sha":"5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719"}],"sha":"c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c92c3b52f2440bc162c8af64c3feab5377acd31f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:02:02Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T09:02:02Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Build the radius ladder, and make the bridge that names it checkable\n\nEvery corner in this app was 6px. That is right for the base tier and wrong above\nit: the reference distinguishes surfaces by radius, and a modal at card radius does\nnot read as lifted off the page — matching the cards behind it flattens the\ndistinction elevation is supposed to carry.\n\nThe ladder is five named roles in the global stylesheet, each mapping to a real Salt\ncurve step, measured at this app''s density: 6px for base surfaces and floating ones,\n12px for large surfaces and modals, 15px for fullscreen. A component now picks\n`--kui-radius-modal` because it *is* a modal, rather than picking 6px because 6px is\nwhat its neighbour used — which is how one value ends up on everything in the first\nplace.\n\n**A bridge like this is a hole unless something polices it**, and that is the part\nworth the effort. Permitting `var(--kui-*)` in the stylelint allow-list would\notherwise let `--kui-radius-modal: 13px` satisfy every check while being exactly the\nmagic value the token rule exists to forbid. So `check-salt-tokens` gained a third\nclass of failure: a named role must be defined as one Salt token and nothing else.\nThe bridge can rename a token; it cannot invent a value. It now reports 72 token\nreferences and 5 named roles.\n\nApplied to the modal through `--saltDialog-borderRadius`, Salt''s own published\nvariable, rather than reaching past it — the same reasoning as the button\nproperties beside it.\n\nFullscreen is 15px where the reference is 16px, because the curve scale has no 16 at\nthis density. Recorded in the stylesheet and in the standard rather than rounded\nquietly: a value that is close is fine, and a value that is close while claiming to\nbe exact is not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19ed2951821e77a9116821ed8d6b56391b654743","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/19ed2951821e77a9116821ed8d6b56391b654743"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDU1NDlmNGY4MTA5MDY3YWMxMjEyNGQ1NmZhZDA2MjNmZjYzYWE3MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca","sha":"09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca"}],"sha":"5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5549f4f8109067ac12124d56fad0623ff63aa719"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:57:51Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:57:51Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Document the usage surface and the guard that guards the guards\n\nThe operations README, the root layout listing and the orientation table all\ndescribed a section that now has another destination. The operations README also\ngets the two things about usage that are easiest to get wrong: why it has two gates\nrather than one, and that most of the page''s job is not undoing the service''s own\ncare about its numbers.\n\nAlso records the resolved-config test in the guards reference. It is a test rather\nthan a script so it was not in the table, but it belongs in that family — and it\nhas now caught the replace-not-merge trap three separate times: on the raw-hex ban,\non the package bans, and on the chart-mark ban hiding inside the stylesheet\nexemption. Reading the config cannot tell you what survived; only resolving it per\nfile can, which is why it is the mechanism that actually works.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e0dba16b9025fcd0ec7e220f52280db213fcc20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/0e0dba16b9025fcd0ec7e220f52280db213fcc20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDA5ZDhiYzBjNTM3YWEyNWRjNjFiNDZhNWFjZWMxYzZjMWY1ZWM2Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a","sha":"ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a"}],"sha":"09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/09d8bc0c537aa25dc61b46a5acec1c6c1f5ec6ca"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:56:36Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:56:36Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Alias the federation boundary, and mount it for real\n\n`lazy.ts` and the root test config both said the federated specifiers were aliased\nat test time so the host mounted a remote''s actual source. No alias existed\nanywhere. The claim described a test nobody had written, and the boundary''s only\ncoverage was the built end-to-end lane.\n\nThe alias exists now, and it buys the half that lane does not. Playwright proves a\nremote entry can be fetched and mounted from another origin; it does not cheaply\nprove the props the host passes are the props the remote accepts, because a\nmismatch there produces a blank region or an unhelpful runtime error rather than a\nfailed navigation. That is the question the contract package exists to answer, and\nit is now answered at the value level rather than only by types.\n\nFive tests. A remote mounts and renders its own route from the host''s props. Its\nroutes resolve relative to wherever it was mounted, which is the property that lets\none bundle serve more than one prefix. A child route needing more than its section\nrefuses and explains itself — checked here because that gate lives inside the\nremote, where the host cannot enforce it and a type cannot express it. And both\nremotes mount on one page without either capturing the other''s context, which is\nthe subtle one: two context objects exist, each subtree reads its own, and if one\ncaptured the other the second would render with the first''s identity. That is the\nshape of a cross-tenant leak, not a layout bug.\n\nBoth comments that made the false claim now describe what is actually there,\nincluding that it was absent and what the two lanes each prove.\n\n**The coverage threshold went down, and that is the honest direction.** Aliasing\nthe boundary means the host loads the remotes'' whole route tree, and the tool\nreports files it saw — so about two hundred statements that were previously\ninvisible to the report entered the denominator, mostly pages the mount reaches\nthrough a router without exercising. Nothing became less covered; the measurement\nstopped flattering itself by only counting what it happened to import. The\nthresholds are reset from the wider figure and the reasoning is in the config, so\nthe next reader does not mistake it for a regression.\n\nAlso adds the jest-dom types to the host''s tsconfig, which the remotes already had\nand the host did not need until it had tests.\n\n354 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6cd3cdfc23c6128df6e04be3691ba9fdcb197ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/f6cd3cdfc23c6128df6e04be3691ba9fdcb197ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGVmODFlMWI0MGIxYmVlMTA5Njg4NjkxMWMzNDNlNGFlODVhNDdiMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac","sha":"ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac"}],"sha":"ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ef81e1b40b1bee1096886911c343e4ae85a47b0a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:53:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:53:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Test the host workspace, starting with the config that made it possible\n\n`apps/shell` had twelve source files and no tests, and the reason it stayed that\nway is worth naming: it was globbed as a vitest project with no config of its own.\nBoth remote configs spend a paragraph warning about exactly this — a workspace\nwithout one resolves against its `vite.config.ts`, **with the Module Federation\nplugin loaded**, and inherits the default `node` environment. So the first test\nanybody added would have failed inside federation machinery for reasons that name\nnothing about the component, and the cheapest response to that is to stop.\n\nThe config comes first for that reason, before any test. Verified by removing it\nand watching the run die inside Vite server construction rather than in a test —\nwhich is what the sibling configs predicted and what nobody had confirmed.\n\nThen the three modules where a mistake is least visible:\n\n**The remote descriptor table**, which decides what the navigation offers. This is\nthe highest-consequence pure module in the host: it either hides a screen a reader\nis entitled to, or offers a link that leads to a guaranteed refusal — and the\nsecond is worse, because the reader believes they should have been able to. The\nassertions are mostly about its relationship with the capability table, which\nnothing checked: every referenced capability exists, no child is reachable through\na section its role cannot enter, child paths stay relative so a remote can be\nremounted, and the audit log stays auditor-only even against an admin. The helper\nis typed as the capability union rather than `string`, because that narrowing is\nthe thing turning a typo into a compile error instead of a nav entry that silently\nnever appears.\n\n**The basename resolver**, where every failure wears another failure''s costume. A\nwrong basename produces routes that do not resolve, which reads as a router bug; an\nun-substituted template placeholder produces the same symptom and is a deploy bug.\nThe resolver exists to tell those apart and nothing checked that it did.\n\n**The query defaults**, which include an invariant that is easy to lose. `retry: 0`\non mutations is not a preference: the write helpers mint an idempotency key inside\nthe mutation function, so a retry mints a second key, and a second key is a second\noperation as far as the server is concerned. Raising it to \"harden\" the write path\nwould silently convert idempotent retries into duplicate writes. That now fails a\ntest.\n\n349 tests, up from 311. Coverage 66.4% statements and 68.6% lines, and the ratchet\nis raised to match — the first raise, earned by a workspace going from nothing to\ncovered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f658e4624cf1a08442ecab537da297182e99dfcf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/f658e4624cf1a08442ecab537da297182e99dfcf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGVlNDk4OWNlNjgzMDQ3ZDVkYWQ3Zjk5ZjFmNGYwZGY3YTI2MzFkYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7","sha":"94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7"}],"sha":"ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ee4989ce683047d5dad7f99f1f4f0df7a2631dac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:48:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:48:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"The usage console, and the chart components it made usable\n\n\"Is any of this used, and by whom\" is the question the product turns on, and\nnothing in the console could answer it — the aggregate API did not exist when\nthese screens were built. Five endpoints serve it now.\n\nAlmost every decision here is about not undoing the service''s own care. It is\nunusually disciplined about its numbers, and each discipline is one a dashboard\ndestroys by default:\n\n**A day with no traffic is absent, not zero** — the API says why, in the series''\nown description: \"so a caller can tell an outage from a quiet weekend\". Every\ncharting default fills that gap and erases the distinction. The page counts the\ngaps and names the dates above the chart instead of drawing through them.\n\n**Distinct actors can be genuinely unknown**, when the window reaches past raw\nretention, and the response carries the reason expressly \"so a caller can render\nthe reason rather than a zero\" — a zero there reports an unused platform on the\npage read to decide whether the platform is used. A surface with a *real* zero\nrenders the zero, which is why the two are distinguished by null and not by\nfalsiness. I wrote that check as a truthiness test first; both fixtures exist so\nthat version fails.\n\n**`actor_days` is not a headcount** — an actor active on ten days counts ten\ntimes, so for a month it runs up to thirty times high. It is shown, because it is\nthe only reach figure available when the distinct count is not, and labelled as\nday-counts.\n\n**The worst daily p95 is not the window''s p95**, because percentiles cannot be\naveraged. The column says which one it is and the caveat says why.\n\nThe page also states what it refuses to say: no rates, no percentage this page\ncomputed, and no strength badges — the API classifies none of its fields, so a\nbadge would be a claim the response does not make. That absence is stated rather\nthan filled in.\n\nTwo capabilities, not one, because the server has two gates: the four aggregate\nreads are admin-only and describe the deployment, while the owner-scoped read\nadmits producer and returns only what their tenant owns. A producer sees their own\nsection and is told, once, why the deployment panels are absent.\n\n**The chart primitives finally have a consumer, and the reason they had none turns\nout to be structural.** `Figure` takes its mark as a prop, and the marks are\nunimportable outside the component kit — both correct, and together they made\n`Figure` unusable from a remote, since building a mark requires importing one. I\nfirst worked around it with a scoped lint exemption, which reopens exactly the\nhole the rule closes. The fix is `BarFigure`: a composite inside the package that\nalready holds the marks, taking bars and rows, with no prop that omits the table.\n\n31 new tests, all on the awkward cases rather than the easy ones. 311 total,\ncoverage 66.1% (up from 63.8%), usage route in the accessibility gate, bundle\n343.7 KB gz for operations against a 360 budget.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dde8ea9917438365f8b734cad7776646cfbcd867","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/dde8ea9917438365f8b734cad7776646cfbcd867"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDk0YzI1NTM0NTUyOWNlMTE3OWRiYjY4NjI4ODYzZTgzMDgwNWNlYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e","sha":"707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e"}],"sha":"94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/94c255345529ce1179dbb68628863e830805ceb7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:36:37Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:36:37Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Fix seven defects an adversarial review and a defect hunt found\n\nTwo independent judges went at this branch. Both earned their keep, and two of\nthe findings were wrong in a way only the wire could show.\n\n**`edge_types` was sent as a repeated parameter; the API declares a\ncomma-separated string.** My own comment asserted the opposite — against a spec\nsitting in this repo. A server binding a single string reads the first occurrence\nonly, so selecting three relationship types silently filtered on one, with no\nerror and nothing on screen to suggest it. Confirmed on the wire, fixed, and now\nasserted by a test that inspects the outgoing URL.\n\n**`direction` used `upstream`/`downstream`, values the server does not define.**\nIt documents `forward` and `reverse` and defaults to `reverse`. An unrecognised\nstring falls back to that default, so asking for one direction could silently\nreturn the other — broken by construction for every value the type admitted. It\nnow spells the parameter the way the API spells it, rather than translating a\nfriendlier vocabulary at one more place that can be wrong. The request fixtures\nhad been reinforcing the wrong words; they match now.\n\nAlso from that read: `depth` caps at 5 server-side, and offering 1–3 hid reach\nthat was available. And `/dependencies` accepts neither `edge_types` nor\n`direction`, so it no longer sends them — a no-op that still varied the cache key\nand split one answer across two entries.\n\n**The dev-secret guard passed on an empty-but-present output directory.** Exactly\nthe false negative it was written to remove, one layer in: `existsSync` is true\nfor an empty directory, so it sailed past the missing check and then found nothing\nin nothing. Reachable in practice — the bundler clears the directory at the start\nof a build, so a build that dies immediately after leaves this. It also silently\ndropped the secret from its needle set if the env key were renamed, while failing\nloudly for the same condition on the roster. Both fixed, both verified against the\nreproducers that demonstrated them.\n\n**The capability parity test checked only the first path an entry named.** One gate\nnames two probes; the second was never validated while the entry read as covered —\nwhich is the \"verified coverage that gates nothing\" failure the test exists to\nprevent. It now checks every path, and a wildcard family must cover something\nbeyond its own carve-out.\n\n**`recallCaveat` trusted an invariant its neighbour re-verifies.** Every served\nclaim carries the same note, so one is shown for the set — but nothing checked\nthat they agreed, on the one surface whose purpose is not showing a caveat that\nis stale for part of what is on screen. It now returns nothing rather than\nguessing.\n\n**The stylesheet exemption was still dropping the chart ban.** Three entry files\nwere the only ones in the app free to import a mark directly — a narrower instance\nof the replace-not-merge bug this composition exists to prevent. The ban is now\nhoisted and shared, and the resolved-config test asserts it there too.\n\n**The role-literal rule missed a `switch`.** Added, and verified by writing one.\nThe destructured and aliased forms need scope analysis this rule does not have;\nthat limit is now written into the rule rather than left as an impression of\ncoverage.\n\n**Three factual errors in the design standard**, each checked against the live\nreference: modal radius is 12px and only fullscreen is 16px; the two\ndiscouraged-label lists belong to different components and are now attributed\nseparately; and a destructive button pairs with a result toast, with the\ndestructive modal being its own pattern rather than the same one.\n\n**The blocker: the claims page dropped four fields it claimed to render.** The\nmodule docstring promised the whole envelope and the table omitted the subject,\ncategory, and both validity bounds — so a predicate and a value did not say what\nthey were about. Worse, the test named \"renders the whole trust envelope\" listed\nonly the columns that existed, shaping itself to the code and endorsing the gap it\nexisted to catch. The columns are there now, and the test is driven from the\nresponse fields so a served field with no column fails.\n\nOne thing the review flagged that turned into a design question: the search fired\nper keystroke. It is debounced now, but the control state is not — the predicate\nfield disables on the keystroke while the request waits, because a live control\nwhose value is being ignored is worse than one that greys out.\n\n279 tests, full pipeline green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a6c43a76ebea3cc6646344eadf488c965d221501","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/a6c43a76ebea3cc6646344eadf488c965d221501"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDcwN2JhYmU5NDczN2Y3NDhlMjhhNGNmMjI4YTJhYzJlNjc4ZTVlMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099","sha":"7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099"}],"sha":"707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/707babe94737f748e28a4cf228a2ac2e678e5e1e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:19:00Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:19:00Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"A README per workspace, saying what it owns and what it forbids\n\nEight packages, no statement anywhere of what any of them was for. The boundaries\nbetween them are the most load-bearing thing about this repo — which workspace may\nhold a stylesheet, which one may name a role, which one may not export a runtime\nvalue — and all of it was learnable only by reading the code and inferring the rule\nfrom its absence.\n\nEach file says what the workspace owns and, more usefully, what it refuses:\n\n- the client, where a new domain gets its own module and keys carry every\n  parameter that changes the answer\n- auth, where the capability table mirrors the API rather than implementing it,\n  and the two collapse traps are spelled out\n- the ui-kit, the only workspace permitted a stylesheet, and why screens compose\n  from it rather than from Salt directly\n- testing, where a fixture must never be richer than its endpoint and must encode\n  the server''s invariants\n- the remote contract, which exports no runtime value on purpose and is therefore\n  the only compile-time guard on the federation boundary\n- the shell, which owns the client and the nav, with the reason for each\n- the two remotes, including the two things each is easiest to get wrong\n\nLinks verified and the doc-reference guard passes, as with the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"050ad41db9304ed4b87d4e1c5008d176fc318165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/050ad41db9304ed4b87d4e1c5008d176fc318165"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDcxNDNjZDZhYmFmNDNkOTUzYWYxOWIxMzE5MWFkMmM4MzZlMjcwOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04","sha":"dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04"}],"sha":"7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7143cd6abaf43d953af19b13191ad2c836e27099"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:17:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:17:38Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Put a number behind \"we have tests\"\n\nThe coverage tool was a devDependency with no threshold, no reporter and no step\nin CI — installed and never once run. So the claim was unfalsifiable, and the\nparts with no coverage at all were invisible: an entire workspace, and most of the\ncomponent kit.\n\nMeasured: 63.4% of statements, 58.2% of branches, 65.4% of lines. Thresholds are\nset a point below that and enforced in the unit lane.\n\nDeliberately unambitious, and that is the argument. A threshold set where the code\nactually is cannot be negotiated with and cannot be skipped. One set where the\ncode ought to be gets lowered to the ceiling by the first person it blocks, and\nthen it protects nothing. The point of headroom is so an unrelated change does not\nfail on rounding noise; the first run with no headroom passed by four hundredths.\n\nExcluded: the generated client, build output, config, the standalone development\nharnesses, and the end-to-end specs — those run against built artefacts, so\ncounting them here would credit source they never import.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45f86e6d91e8ae50f2a1ade8853be129fe9be4b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/45f86e6d91e8ae50f2a1ade8853be129fe9be4b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGRhYjRiOGY4NGUwNTlhY2NkOGVlZTBiYzkwMGI1NDUxYWQ2N2RhMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285","sha":"895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285"}],"sha":"dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/dab4b8f84e059accd8eee0bc900b5451ad67da04"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:14:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:14:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Documentation, for a repo that had none\n\n192 tracked files and not one markdown file. No README, no docs, no conventions\nfile. What substituted was genuinely good reasoning in header comments — but only\ndiscoverable by opening the right file, and much of it cross-cutting architecture\nthat belongs in one place.\n\nConcretely, none of this was written down anywhere: that local development needs a\nregistry, a mock identity provider and an entitlement service on three ports; that\n`doctor` has to run first and again after any restart, because the entitlement\nstore is in memory and a lost seed looks exactly like a broken permission; or that\nadding a remote requires nine files to agree, where missing any one fails in a way\nthat names something other than the cause.\n\nSix documents:\n\n**`README.md`** — what this is, who it serves, the three backing services, the\nquickstart, a commands table, and the handful of conventions that will bite a first\nchange. A who-you-are table routes readers rather than making them scan.\n\n**`CLAUDE.md`** — the rules that are enforced but not obvious, and the traps that\nhave already cost somebody a session: the six guards and what each exists to\ncatch, the two authorization constraints that have each caused a defect, the\nper-workspace test config trap, the fixture rules, and the bundle economics that\ndecide where a surface goes.\n\n**The design standard** — the current reference console expressed in Salt''s\nvocabulary, since the substrate stays Salt and its own packages and typefaces are\ndeliberately not adopted. Colour as a ramp read by role rather than by eye, a\nradius ladder instead of one constant, type as a named scale set as a unit, and\nthe button, table, empty-state and note rules. It reverses an earlier reading:\nbuttons are Title Case verb-plus-noun, and the noun is the useful half. It ends by\nstating precisely which properties are enforced and which are only agreed —\nbecause a rule claiming a gate it does not have is the same defect as a number\nclaiming a strength it cannot bear.\n\n**Orientation, add-a-screen, add-a-remote, and a guards reference.** The\nadd-a-remote guide opens by arguing you should not: a new remote starts about\n154 KB gz in debt, against 1.3 KB for the same surfaces inside an existing one.\n\nTwo things checked rather than assumed: every internal link resolves — a broken\nlink is the defect class this whole pass has been fixing — and all of it passes the\ndoc-reference guard, which scans markdown as well as code, so the documentation\ncannot lean on a planning repo that does not ship with it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8ee7093d080e17509cf6baa9bbbcd3878dccafc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/8ee7093d080e17509cf6baa9bbbcd3878dccafc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDg5NWU2MTQxZmFkMzNhNzkyMTFiNjczZDMzOGJhMGFkY2E5Y2UyODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6","sha":"d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6"}],"sha":"895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/895e6141fad33a79211b673d338ba0adca9ce285"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:10:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:10:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Claims, with the evidence and the confidence that make them usable\n\nThe vision asks for cited answers — \"every response returns its sources and\nconfidence, so an agent or engineer can verify and drill in\" — and for trust to\nbe explicit. The endpoints served all of it and nothing rendered any of it. A\nmemory whose trust signals are unreadable is a memory you cannot act on.\n\nA claim is an ontology-bound triple, and the triple is the least interesting\npart. The page renders the envelope: confidence, the source''s authority, whether\nan owner confirmed it, and the citations. Owner confirmation gets its own column\nrather than being folded into confidence, because they are different signals and\nthe human one is ground truth — a confirmed low-confidence claim outranks an\nunconfirmed high-confidence one.\n\nFour decisions that came out of reading the server rather than designing in the\nabstract:\n\n**The safety caveat renders once, above the table.** Every served claim is\nlabelled recalled and untrusted by construction; the service refuses to build one\notherwise, because a high-confidence extraction of a hostile statement is still\nhostile. That is a content-trust boundary, not a quality score, and it does not\nvary. A per-row badge would imply variance that does not exist, and an identical\nmarker on every row becomes chrome the eye stops seeing — the one state a safety\ncaveat must never reach. The wording is the server''s, including the part that\nmatters most on an agent-facing surface: this is not an instruction to follow.\n\n**Citations are always visible.** No disclosure, no click. A citation nobody\nopens is not evidence, and this whole surface exists so a claim can be checked.\n\n**Confidence is banded with the number beside it.** `0.82` invites a reader to\ntreat it as different from `0.79`. The band carries the decision; the number is\nstill there.\n\n**Every filter is server-side, and the state lives in the route.** Filtering in\nthe browser would hide how many claims were excluded, and a count that omits what\nit dropped is the kind of number that gets quoted. A filtered view being a\npasteable link is most of the point for a page about evidence.\n\nEmpty states name which kind of empty: excluded by your own threshold (which you\ncan reverse), versus nothing matching for this tenant (where the claim may exist\nand belong to an entity you cannot see).\n\nOne bug fixed on the way: the filtered read was being switched off with\n`limit: 0`, which still issues a request. The hook now takes an `enabled` option,\nbecause a page cannot call a hook conditionally and the two reads are\nalternatives.\n\nEleven component tests, and the route joins the accessibility gate — 14 axe\nchecks pass. 272 tests total. Bundle 341.2 KB gz for the catalog against a 360\nbudget.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8949f185006a2b398619d55255632e8ebadaded7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/8949f185006a2b398619d55255632e8ebadaded7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQ3MDQ5YWUyOTZlN2IxMDAxMDA3YzNkM2Y0YWRhZGNjOTdiYmYxYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0","sha":"add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0"}],"sha":"d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d7049ae296e7b1001007c3d3f4adadcc97bbf1a6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:05:55Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:05:55Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Impact and ownership, on the page where the decision is made\n\nThe product''s vision names \"dependency and blast-radius traversal before a\nchange\" as something the memory must enable. Three endpoints served it, open to\nevery role, and no screen called any of them.\n\nIt lands on the capability detail page rather than as its own destination,\nbecause the decision it supports is made while looking at the capability —\nsending a reader elsewhere to find out whether changing the thing in front of\nthem is safe is how a feature ends up unused. One panel with a question selector\nrather than three stacked cards: these are alternatives, not parts of one answer,\nand stacking would make the page long enough that the third is never seen.\n\nIt opens on **Used by**. A reader arriving here is more often deciding whether a\nchange is safe than deciding whether to build on something, and the other\nquestion is one selection away either way. Only the selected traversal is\nrequested, so opening a capability never costs a transitive closure.\n\nTwo properties are the reason this is worth trusting rather than just worth\nhaving:\n\n**A partial answer says so.** The traversal reports `cache_hit` and\n`version_satisfied`, and both are relayed above the table. A cached closure may\nbe missing an edge written moments ago; an unresolved version constraint means\nedges are reported without version agreement. The reader most likely to be here\nis deciding whether to ship a breaking change, and is the one person who must not\nbe told a partial answer is complete. The plain dependency endpoint reports\nneither, so nothing is relayed there — inventing a caveat is the mirror of\ndropping one.\n\n**An empty result does not claim isolation.** \"Nothing depends on this\" and\n\"nothing you can see depends on this\" are different facts, and the second is the\none a reader would act on wrongly. The copy names both and suggests a greater\ndepth. The mocked blast radius is empty on purpose so that path is reachable in a\ntest rather than only in theory.\n\nWritten first with two rows of toggle buttons, then rewritten as dropdowns in\nfilter fields. That is not taste: a row of toggles where every other selector in\nthis app is a bordered dropdown is the specific deviation this codebase has\nalready been corrected for once, and a second idiom for the same job is what\nmakes a console read as assembled rather than designed.\n\nNine component tests, and the request mocks encode the two server invariants\nthey rest on — every claim cited, every claim uniformly untrusted — so a fixture\ncannot quietly make a component right for the wrong reason. 261 tests pass.\nBundle 395.2 / 339.9 / 340.7 KB gz, against budgets of 440 / 360 / 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aefd1706f1d75092ebc9f0737efbe5aa6970f810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/aefd1706f1d75092ebc9f0737efbe5aa6970f810"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGFkZDY3NzUyY2YxMjIyMjAxMDc4MjcwOTUzODgwM2E1YmExMDgxZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167","sha":"8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167"}],"sha":"add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/add67752cf12222010782709538803a5ba1081e0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:01:10Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:01:10Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Typed reads for claims and impact, and refresh the vendored spec\n\nThe vendored OpenAPI document was six paths behind the registry, which is why\nthis comes first: writing client code against a stale contract is how the last\nregeneration ended up twenty-two paths behind. It is now current at 97 paths,\nand the generated bindings with it.\n\nTwo new domains, both of which the product''s own vision names as things the\nmemory must enable and neither of which had any client code:\n\n**Impact.** Dependencies, dependents and blast radius — \"dependency and\nblast-radius traversal before a change\". Three endpoints rather than one with a\nflag, because they answer three questions: what this needs, who needs this, and\nhow far a change travels. Depth, edge types and an as-of instant are all real\nparameters, so the bi-temporal lever is available rather than approximated, and\nall of them are in the cache key — a key holding only the root would serve a\ndepth-1 result under a depth-3 heading, which is wrong in a way that looks\nright. `cache_hit` and `version_satisfied` are surfaced as caveats rather than\ndropped: the reader deciding whether to ship a breaking change is the one person\nwho must not be told a partial answer is complete.\n\n**Memory.** Claims with the whole envelope around the triple — confidence,\nauthority, citations, human confirmation, and the bi-temporal interval.\n\nTwo things I got wrong by assumption and fixed by reading the server, both of\nwhich would have shipped as fiction:\n\nThe persona vocabulary is `l1_responder` / `l3_engineer` / `architect` / `agent`.\nI had written `l1` and `l3`. The server validates against a closed set and\nrefuses an unknown value, so those would have produced a 422 rather than a\ndegraded result.\n\nMore importantly, `trust` is **not** a per-claim quality signal, and I had built\na helper treating it as one. Every served claim is labelled recalled and\nuntrusted by construction, with an assertion refusing to serve one otherwise,\nbecause — in the server''s words — \"a high-confidence extraction of a hostile\nstatement is still hostile\". It is a content-trust boundary, not a data-quality\nscore. So a per-row badge would be misleading twice: it implies variance that\ndoes not exist, and an identical marker repeated on every row becomes chrome the\neye skips, which is the one state a safety caveat must not reach. It renders once\nper view instead, carrying the server''s own wording. Relatedly, a claim without\ncitations is never served at all, so that is an invariant the client checks\nrather than a case it designs a fallback for.\n\nConfidence bands rather than rendering two decimal places, which invite a reader\nto treat 0.82 and 0.79 as different. The number is still shown beside the band.\n\n252 tests pass, up from 229. No screens yet — these are the reads they will use.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe27253a486034e927af3b2f3e98beb088399231","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/fe27253a486034e927af3b2f3e98beb088399231"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDhmOGE1YmJjZTk4MDY1YTEwYjljNDFjMjBiYjM0YjIwZTg5MjUxNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171","sha":"18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171"}],"sha":"8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/8f8a5bbce98065a10b9c41c20bb34b20e8925167"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:55:14Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:55:14Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Ask the capability table, and make its claims checkable\n\nThe table exists so a screen asks `can(session, ''audit:read'')` and never names a\nrole — that is what lets a gate move without touching a component, and the table\nis the only place the server''s real gates are documented and tested. Two places\nhad gone around it. An adoption control compared the session role against\nproducer and admin directly, and the home page branched on \"not the auditor\nrole\". Both were correct, and both were invisible to the parity test that exists\nto catch exactly this.\n\nBoth now ask a capability. The home page''s condition is the more interesting\nrewrite: it renders a note explaining the audit log''s role gate, so the\ncondition worth writing is `!can(session, ''audit:read'')` — the reader lacks the\ncapability, which is *why* the note is there.\n\nSeven capabilities added for surfaces the API already serves: adoption read and\nwrite, subscriptions, notifications, impact traversal, and memory reads.\nAdoption is two entries rather than one because the gates are asymmetric —\nlisting admits every role while adopting is producer-or-admin and excludes\nconsumer, so a single entry could only be as permissive as its narrowest use and\nwould either hide state from consumers who may see it, or offer them a button\nguaranteed to 403.\n\nA lint rule now catches the class rather than the two instances. It matches a\ncomparison between `.role` and a role literal, is exempt inside the package that\nowns roles, and is registered for both components and plain modules — the\n`.tsx`-only block could not reach a hook or a route guard, which is where such a\ncomparison would otherwise hide. Verified by writing one and watching it fail,\nafter a first attempt with a sibling combinator that silently matched nothing.\n\nThe parity test''s weakest assertion is also fixed. It checked that each gate''s\nendpoint string was non-empty, which any typo passes; it now resolves the path\nagainst the vendored OpenAPI document, so a capability mirroring a renamed or\nimaginary route fails instead of reading as verified coverage. That found a bug\nin its own first implementation: `POST/PATCH /v1/capabilities` parsed to\n`/PATCH`, because \"starts with a slash\" is not how you find a path.\n\n229 tests pass, up from 219.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18af9883c195248d0282f02fdee4c3c88b97a443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/18af9883c195248d0282f02fdee4c3c88b97a443"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDE4YzJmMjZhN2U5ZDU3ODRkMTgyNGEyODg5M2I3YWRmZjFhZjkxNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85","sha":"e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85"}],"sha":"18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/18c2f26a7e9d5784d1824a28893b7adff1af9171"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:50:25Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:50:25Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Split the API client by domain, and correct a docstring that had it backwards\n\nTwo modules held eight unrelated domains between them. `hooks.ts` was catalog,\nsearch, audit, identity and operational health at 282 lines, under a name three\nof its siblings also deserved — `mutations.ts` had to open by explaining it was\n\"separate from hooks.ts and admin.ts, which are reads\", which is a file name\napologising for itself. `consumer.ts` was adoption, subscriptions and the inbox\nat 357 lines.\n\nNow one module per domain: identity, catalog, search, audit, operationalHealth,\nadoptions, subscriptions, notifications, adminSync. Nothing downstream changed —\nall 21 import sites go through the barrel, and no file deep-imports these — so\nthis is a rearrangement with a rewritten barrel, grouped transport / plumbing /\ndomains so a new domain has an obvious place to go instead of joining whichever\nfile is nearest.\n\nTwo things folded in along the way. `readings.ts` merges into\n`operationalHealth.ts`: it held the wording rules for the values that module\nserves, its name was a near-homograph of two neighbours, and a rule kept apart\nfrom what it governs is a rule that drifts. And `LIST_OPTIONS` was defined\nidentically in two modules — now one, because two copies of a caching policy\ndiverge toward whichever was edited while debugging one screen.\n\n**The find worth the whole exercise.** The old `consumer.ts` opened by stating\nthat \"adopting does not silently subscribe\". The server does exactly that: the\nadoption service is constructed with an auto-subscribe hook, and unadopting\nsoft-deletes only the adoption row, so the subscription it created survives and\nkeeps delivering. The unadopt dialog two files away already told users this\ncorrectly. So the module docstring — the thing a developer reads first — asserted\nthe opposite of both the server''s behaviour and the app''s own copy. It now\ndescribes what happens, and says which claim it replaced.\n\nAlso noted while reading: `/v1/graph/consumer` is named in that docstring but\nnever called. It is uncovered surface, not covered surface, which matters for\nwhat the consumer projection needs next.\n\nVerified: typecheck, 219 tests, 28 end-to-end, bundle budget unchanged at\n395.1 / 338.5 / 340.6 KB gz.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3042bf8c58b02eba0b001c9f40331132cca2442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/e3042bf8c58b02eba0b001c9f40331132cca2442"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGUzMDBjYjYxNTZlZjM4OTkxMzA2ZmVlZjE4OGRhNWE4N2MzN2RkODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30","sha":"5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30"}],"sha":"e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/e300cb6156ef38991306feef188da5a87c37dd85"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:44:31Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:44:46Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Move the two root modules into tooling/, named for what they do\n\n`mf.shared.ts` and `dev-proxy.ts` sat at the repo root, which is where a reader\nlooks last and where neither had a neighbourhood. Both names were also working\nagainst them.\n\n`mf` was an unexpanded abbreviation appearing nowhere else in the repo, and the\ndot separator was unique to that one filename. Worse, its export was named\n`shared`, a bare noun, so all three import sites read `shared` with no\nindication of what was being shared or with whom. Now\n`tooling/federation/shared-modules.ts` exporting `sharedModules`.\n\n`dev-proxy` was actively misleading rather than merely vague. The same table\nserves all three `preview` servers as well as the dev ones, and the built\nend-to-end lane runs entirely through preview — so it is in the path of every\nrequest the test suite makes against a real backend, not just a developer''s.\nNow `tooling/vite/registry-proxy.ts` exporting `registryProxy`, with the\ndocstring saying so.\n\nThe interesting part is `check-shared-parity`, which reads the share contract by\npath and regex rather than importing it, precisely so it needs no TypeScript\nloader — which makes it the thing a move breaks silently. Its path is updated\nand it still resolves all seven pinned modules.\n\nVerified beyond typecheck, because the vite configs themselves changed: the\nbuild, 28 end-to-end tests, and the bundle budget all pass, with the three\nartefacts at 395.1 / 338.5 / 340.6 KB gz — byte-identical to before the move.\n\nAlso drops a dangling pointer to a deployment section of a README that has never\nexisted; the surrounding paragraph already says what to do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"823627c73d41e7eab3bef3ea0c2843b50a88e2e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/823627c73d41e7eab3bef3ea0c2843b50a88e2e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDVmOTk4NzU5NjdlN2EzNTRiYTEwNjY3YTExZjg5Yzk3MWQ5M2FkMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f","sha":"4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f"}],"sha":"5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5f99875967e7a354ba10667a11f89c971d93ad30"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:42:31Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:42:31Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Write the two files that other files have been pointing at\n\n`playwright.dev.config.ts` was referenced by the `e2e:dev` script and by the\nbuilt config''s own docstring, and did not exist, so `npm run e2e:dev` exited\nbefore running anything. It is the same failure the built config''s header\ndescribes having just fixed, one file over, left open. It now covers the lane it\nwas always meant to: the dev servers against a real registry, which is the half\nthe mocked lane cannot reach — real request shapes, the identity chain end to\nend, and the role gates as the API enforces them rather than as hand-written\nmocks describe them. Serial, because those specs mutate shared registry state.\nNot wired into CI, deliberately: the workflow provisions no registry, and a lane\nthat passes only when a backend happens to be up is a lane whose failures get\nignored.\n\n`.env.example` was called \"the tracked spec\" by `.gitignore`, which whitelisted\nit, and also did not exist. It now documents all sixteen variables the repo\nreads, split by whether they reach the browser bundle or stay in Node, each with\nwhat happens if you leave it alone. Checked both directions: every variable\ndocumented is read somewhere, and an exhaustive grep for `VITE_*`/`KUI_*` across\nthe tree finds exactly these sixteen and no more.\n\nAlso drops `openapi-fetch`, a declared runtime dependency of the API client that\nnothing imports. The client is a deliberate hand-rolled fetch wrapper — its own\nheader explains why a proxy over generated paths was rejected — so the package\nwas there to support an approach that was considered and not taken.\n\nTwo dependency findings I am *not* acting on, because looking at the manifests\nchanged my reading of them. The shell keeps `@knowledge-ui/testing` in\ndevDependencies, and the ui-kit continues to declare nothing for it. Both look\nwrong in isolation, but this repo has a consistent convention: internal packages\ndeclare runtime deps as peerDependencies and all test tooling lives at the root,\nwhich is why `packages/testing` declares neither `msw` nor `@testing-library/*`\neither. Moving the shell''s entry would imply production needs the request mocks\nand would pull `msw` into a production install. Both follow the convention\nrather than break it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68589000bb26dcc38f208cb2170afd3252855c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/68589000bb26dcc38f208cb2170afd3252855c5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDQzNDNjMTU0MmQwMDkzZjk4ZGQ3YWMxYmI2ZjgzMDgwZTFiZGY5NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61","sha":"1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61"}],"sha":"4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/4343c1542d0093f98dd7ac1bb6f83080e1bdf96f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:38:40Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:38:40Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Delete what nothing referenced, and load the env files that were inert\n\nFour categories, all verified rather than assumed.\n\n**Committed declaration output.** `dev-proxy.d.ts`, `mf.shared.d.ts` and their\ntwo sourcemaps were tracked. No tsconfig emits them — every project includes\n`src/**` and both sources sit at the repo root — so no build reproduced them and\nno gate compared them against their sources. They had already begun to rot: the\ndeclarations were a day newer than their own maps. `.gitignore` covered `dist/`\nand `dist-types/` but nothing root-level, which is how they got in; it now\ncovers root `*.d.ts`, anchored so the two hand-written declaration files inside\n`src/` directories are untouched.\n\n**Three env files nothing read.** Each app carried a byte-identical\n`.env.development` setting an empty API base URL and enabling the persona\nswitcher. All three vite configs point `envDir` at the repo root, so Vite never\nlooked in the app directories. The settings happened to match the code''s own\nfallbacks — `apiBaseUrl()` already returns the empty string, and the switcher is\nenabled by the build-time DEV flag in dev regardless — so nothing misbehaved,\nand nothing revealed the files were dead. Rather than drop them, both variables\nand their reasoning move into the root file, where they load.\n\n**A dead barrel.** `packages/testing/src/msw/index.ts` had no importer; the\npackage exports `.`, `./server` and `./browser`, and its own entry imports each\nsubmodule directly.\n\n**Three empty directories** left behind as scaffolding: a `state/` for a state\nlibrary that never arrived, an unused `components/`, and an `e2e/support/` that\nthe Playwright config does not reference.\n\nOne thing that looked dead and was not: `packages/remote-contract` had a vitest\nproject and no tests, and its source claimed `RemoteApp` was \"asserted by a\ntype-level test\" that did not exist. Deleting the config was the cheaper option\nand the wrong one — this package is the only compile-time check on a boundary\nModule Federation resolves at runtime, so a mistake inside these types disables\nthe one mechanism the boundary has. The test now exists, and it fails the\ntypecheck when the contract is broken: verified by widening `RemoteName` and\nwatching `tsc` reject it with the expected and actual values named.\n\n219 tests pass, up from 214.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"97eec350e4807cebbecdb45b2a4b22218762e573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/97eec350e4807cebbecdb45b2a4b22218762e573"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDFiMjhjZWY2ZWVkYWZmMzA4YjM5ZjBkNzg3MzhiYzM0MjAxZmNiNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324","sha":"5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324"}],"sha":"1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1b28cef6eedaff308b39f0d78738bc34201fcb61"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:35:54Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:35:54Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Typecheck the tier that was never typechecked, and order the packages\n\nEvery project in this repo included `src/**` and nothing else, so a whole tier\nwent unchecked: the three end-to-end specs, all seven test configs, the three\nVite configs, the shared test setup, and the two modules at the repo root that\nthe build and the shared-parity guard both read. An error in any of them\nsurfaced when the file ran, if it ran — and `mf.shared.ts` is parsed by a guard\nscript with a regex rather than imported, so an error there surfaced nowhere.\n\n`tsconfig.tooling.json` covers all of it: 38 files that `tsc` had never seen.\nIt is separate from the workspace projects because these files are not part of\nany package''s output — noEmit, no declarations, no composite build.\n\nAlso adds the project references the five packages were missing. All of them\nset `composite: true` and two import a third, but none declared a reference, so\ncorrect build order was implicit in the order of an array in the root config\nand `tsc -b` would not reorder on a cross-package change. `remote-contract` and\n`testing` both depend on `auth`; after the change both report as up to date\n\"with .d.ts files from its dependencies\", which is the form only a project with\nreferences gets.\n\nI tried extending this to the nine guard scripts under checkJs. It reports 46\nimplicit-any errors, which is annotation work rather than defects, so they stay\nout for now — but the experiment found one real bug and it is fixed here: an\nindexed lookup in the new dev-secrets check is `string | undefined` under\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess, and the shell output directory is now a named\nconstant instead.\n\nThe mocked-build branch of that check has now also fired for real rather than\nonly in a test: run against a tree still holding end-to-end artefacts, it\nrefused to draw a conclusion instead of reporting a false leak.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2be715623de7ee00fe842ed8bf08e288394c5b27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/2be715623de7ee00fe842ed8bf08e288394c5b27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDUxMDE2MDJhYTQwOWRiZDk5MmMxZDQ4OGZiODY0YzYyYjlmODYzMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a","sha":"949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a"}],"sha":"5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/5101602aa409dbd992c1d488fb864c62b9f86324"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:32:46Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:32:46Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Make the local pipeline the same pipeline CI runs\n\nThe workflow''s header claimed every step invoked an npm script so the gates\nwould run identically on a laptop, and that `npm run ci` was the whole\npipeline. Neither held. Four checks existed only inside the workflow file —\nformatting, codegen drift, the end-to-end lane, and the dev-secret assertion —\nso `npm run ci` could pass locally while CI failed on any of them, with nothing\nto warn you which.\n\nNow there are five named lanes, `ci:static` / `ci:codegen` / `ci:unit` /\n`ci:e2e` / `ci:secrets`, and `ci` runs all five in order. Each workflow job\ncalls one lane and adds nothing, so there is no step in CI that is not also a\ncommand you can run. The jobs stay separate because they parallelise and report\nindependently; only the composition moved.\n\nThree other things the audit turned up:\n\n`lint` gains --max-warnings 0. Without it a rule set to warn — including\nanything inherited from a recommended preset — cannot fail the build, so the\nseverity was decorative.\n\nThe dev-secret assertion becomes a script instead of four lines of shell, and\ngains the check the shell version was missing. `grep -rl … 2>/dev/null` over a\ndirectory that does not exist prints nothing and exits non-zero, which the `if`\nread as \"clean\" — so it passed whenever the build had not run, the one case\nwhere it proves nothing. It now fails on absent output, checks all five client\nids as well as the secret, reads the secret from the env file rather than\nhardcoding a needle that could go stale, and recognises the mocked build (which\nbakes the roster in deliberately) instead of reporting it as a leak.\n\nThe Playwright browser install is pinned to the installed runner version. A\nbrowser from a different version than the test runner is a failure that\nreproduces nowhere else.\n\nVerified by running all five lanes: static, codegen, unit (214 tests), e2e (28\ntests, bundle budget green at 395.1 / 338.5 / 340.6 KB gz), secrets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4aca0ace457e38f36c2fcfd0aed4b5b3377fc8b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/4aca0ace457e38f36c2fcfd0aed4b5b3377fc8b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDk0OWY1MjExMTZiMTZkN2NiMTA3MTEyM2UxNzI4MDU2Y2FkMDI3NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861","sha":"2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861"}],"sha":"949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/949f521116b16d7cb1071123e1728056cad0274a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:31:45Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:31:45Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Format the 23 files that were failing the formatting gate\n\n`npm run format:check` has been failing on main. It is a step in CI''s static\njob and was absent from the `ci` script, so a local run reported success while\nthe same check in CI did not — which is how 23 files drifted.\n\nThe diff is reflow only: joined import lines, corrected JSX indentation, and\none trailing blank. Typecheck and the whole suite pass unchanged, which is what\nmakes it safe to read quickly and skip in blame.\n\nAdds `.prettierignore`, which is what made this possible to separate from the\nwork around it. Without one, formatting rewrites the generated API client — and\n`ci:codegen` regenerates that file and fails on any diff, so the two gates\nwould have contradicted each other, each undoing the other''s output. The\nvendored OpenAPI document and the mock service worker are excluded for the same\nreason: nobody hand-edits them and their generators own their formatting.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26efc83d07c61156a26e6d3aa276337d60def989","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/26efc83d07c61156a26e6d3aa276337d60def989"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDJjMDQyZmE0ZTAzNjgyZWM2ODk0MWE0OTI4NmVlZmE5MTc5OTM4NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3","sha":"f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3"}],"sha":"2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/2c042fa4e03682ec68941a49286eefa917993861"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:27:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T07:27:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Restore the import bans that a narrower block had been deleting\n\n`no-restricted-imports` was set twice: once for every TypeScript file, with\nfive package bans and the global-stylesheet ban, and again for `apps/**` and\n`remotes/**` with a single chart rule. Flat config replaces a rule''s options\nrather than merging them, so the second one won everywhere it matched. The\nCSS-in-JS bans, the alpha-package ban and the stylesheet rule were enforced\nonly under `packages/` — the tree least likely to break them — and had been\nfor as long as the chart rule existed.\n\n`eslint --print-config` on any page returned exactly one banned path.\n\nThis is the second time the same trap fired. The first was\n`no-restricted-syntax`, where a block restated the intrinsic-element selectors\nand dropped the raw-hex ban with them; the fix then was to restate the\nuniversal entries by hand, which is what left the trap armed. So neither rule\nis written as a literal array any more. Both are built by a composer that\nalways includes the universal set, and there is no longer a spelling that\nomits it.\n\nThe three theme entries keep their exemption but no longer buy it by switching\nthe whole rule off — they lift the stylesheet pattern alone, so global CSS is\nstill importable there while CSS-in-JS is not.\n\nAlso drops `react/no-unknown-property: off`, which did nothing: the plugin it\nbelongs to is not installed.\n\nVerified two ways. Every resolved config now carries all five bans, and the\nnew test fails with six errors when the old spelling is put back — checked by\nreintroducing it, not by assuming.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4892b054166d4043bad46053081a034f97a4d888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/4892b054166d4043bad46053081a034f97a4d888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGY2YTA2YmY3ZWZlZGRmM2VkYTQ4NTM1NTZkNDJlOTBjYzZlYjNhYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb","sha":"c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb"}],"sha":"f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6a06bf7efeddf3eda4853556d42e90cc6eb3ac3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T05:44:46Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T05:44:46Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Follow the catalog''s response shapes, and stop faking the ones it never sent\n\nSearch results now cite the artifacts that made them match instead of carrying\ntheir bodies, and the client types say so: citations are always present, while\nthe tenant and the inline artifacts are audit-only.\n\nThe audit panel on the capability page was reading four storage-prefixed\nbitemporal keys off the capability response. It has never returned them under any\nview — bitemporal intervals belong to facts and edges, the rows that assert\nsomething which can later stop being true, and an entity has a creation time and\nan active flag instead. So the panel was permanently empty, and said so in copy\ngentle enough to look deliberate: \"No bitemporal fields returned\".\n\nIt looked fine in tests because the mock invented the missing keys. That is the\npart worth fixing first: a fixture returning a shape the server does not produce\nturns the test suite from a check into a second source of truth, and here it hid\na dead panel for as long as the panel existed. The mock now returns the fields\nthe server actually adds, and the panel reads those.\n\nThe superseded-fact fixture keeps its prefixed names on purpose — the admin\nschema it mirrors genuinely still uses them.\n\n183 tests, typecheck, and lint pass. Client regenerated against a spec where the\nview parameter is an enum, so the hand-written union no longer restates it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"214310163e3835f65f6904e34ce13e1f400802f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/214310163e3835f65f6904e34ce13e1f400802f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGMxZGNiYzk5OWVjNWM3OGY3YWZlYTMwMmFlOGZhYTU2OGNjMTgwZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826","sha":"97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826"}],"sha":"c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c1dcbc999ec5c78f7afea302ae8faa568cc180eb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:30:48Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:30:48Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Regenerate the client: private_annotation entry kind removed\n\nThe kind existed only to contrast with the capability annotations removed\nearlier today, and carried no behaviour of its own — every entry kind\nalready has reference_ids. Generated types and the vendored spec only; no\nhand-written code referenced it.\n\n183 tests pass; lint, typecheck, guards and the bundle budget are clean.","tree":{"sha":"927a5cb3673ba003fee1e02130cb6a5a2bd85363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/927a5cb3673ba003fee1e02130cb6a5a2bd85363"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDk3Y2Q0NzVkM2Q3NDM0Njg4ZDM4YTY2ZDc1NDg5ZGFhNjFhZWQ4MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457","sha":"333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457"}],"sha":"97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/97cd475d3d7434688d38a66d75489daa61aed826"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:08:53Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:08:53Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"Regenerate the typed client after annotations were removed\n\nThe API no longer publishes the annotation endpoints, so the generated\ntypes no longer describe them. No hand-written UI code changes: the\nfeature never had a page, hook, or capability entry — the generated\nclient was its only trace here.\n\n`private_annotation` survives in the generated types as a workspace entry\nkind. That is a different feature and is unaffected.\n\n183 tests pass; lint, typecheck, guards and the bundle budget are clean.","tree":{"sha":"8e26a65897553e9462924b86c1096d6fb53506ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/8e26a65897553e9462924b86c1096d6fb53506ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDMzM2IwOWNkNmFhZGRlNTI3ZmRmMDZiOTU5OTE5ZjdkOGI0NDc0NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1","sha":"1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1"}],"sha":"333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/333b09cd6aadde527fdf06b959919f7d8b447457"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:07:39Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:07:39Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI Phase 4: close the chart, capability, and honesty gaps\n\n**F4.5 — charts are marks in the UI kit, not a library.** Measured rather\nthan argued: a `Figure` (mark + its data table) in use costs 0.4 KB gz,\nagainst 19.4 KB of headroom in operations and 21.6 KB in catalog. Module\nFederation makes that headroom the real ceiling — a library not in the\nshared set is re-fetched per remote that mounts a chart, and one added to\nthe shared set grows the fallback chunk every remote already re-fetches.\nThe library figure is not measured; installing one to measure it would\nmutate the lockfile for a decision the headroom already settles, and that\nis recorded as an assumption rather than a measurement.\n\n`Figure` pairs a chart with the table it was drawn from, and the pairing\nis in the type: `rows` and `columns` are required and no prop suppresses\nthe table. The table is visible rather than alt text because the reader\nwho needs an exact figure, the one checking a number before quoting it,\nand the one whose SVG failed to paint are all served by the same rows —\nand a table cannot drift from the chart, because it is the same array.\n\nThe component alone would have been a convention, and a convention is\nwhat the next page under deadline skips. An eslint rule makes the marks\nunimportable outside ui-kit, so the only route to a chart carries its data\nwith it. Mutation-tested: importing `BarSeries` in a remote fails lint.\n\n**F4.3 — the capability table is checked against the API.** Its docstring\nalready said it mirrors server authorisation and that the API is right\nwhen they disagree; that was a comment, and a comment cannot notice a\ncapability granted to three roles for an endpoint admitting one. Each\ncapability now declares the gate it mirrors in the server''s own terms,\nand the roles must match. Mutation-tested in both directions — a widened\ngrant and an ungated capability each fail.\n\n**F4.4 — the cumulative qualifier is single-sourced.** The wording is the\nsafeguard, so `describeScope` and `processScopeCaveat` live beside the\ntype that carries `kind`. Stated plainly in that module: this is a\nconvention with a helper, not a guarantee, because no static check can\nrecognise a number rendered without its caption.\n\nTwo latent traps fixed on the way. `packages/ui-kit` ran under\n`environment: ''node''` — true while its only test covered a pure function,\nand a trap for whoever wrote the first component test, which failed with\n`document is not defined` for a reason unrelated to the component. It now\nmatches `remotes/operations` exactly. Its tsconfig also lacked the\njest-dom types, so `toBeInTheDocument` failed typecheck while working at\nruntime.\n\nThe a11y sweep visited /ops/metrics as a consumer, which renders the\nrole refusal — so the populated state, with four tiles and a table, had\nnever been axe-checked. It is now, after a persona switch.\n\n183 unit tests and 28 e2e pass; lint, typecheck, guards and the bundle\nbudget all pass. Operations 340.6 KB gz against a 360 budget.","tree":{"sha":"7b8da2f24f349c2dd4c9c67c370da2ca8c031368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/7b8da2f24f349c2dd4c9c67c370da2ca8c031368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDE2NDUyNTNjNDliNGQ5NDJmNTk5M2FiNmNiYmNkZGEzNTA1ODdmZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6","sha":"470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6"}],"sha":"1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/1645253c49b4d942f5993ab6cbbcdda350587ff1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:50:15Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:50:15Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI: read operational health from the service, not from a dashboard tool\n\nThe telemetry page depended on Grafana. That is wrong: Grafana is\ndeployment infrastructure, optional and frequently absent, and this\nproduct does not ship it — so the page was a set of dead links wherever\nit was not installed. A console that only works next to something it does\nnot ship is not a console.\n\nIt now reads one first-party endpoint the service serves for itself, and\nworks with Grafana and Prometheus both stopped. Verified that way rather\nthan assumed: both containers were stopped for the screenshots.\n\nBrowser-side parsing of the Prometheus exposition stays retired, for\nreasons independent of the above — per-replica, cumulative since process\nstart, and the endpoint is credentialed now. The parser module,\nfetchMetricsText, useMetrics, and queryKeys.metrics are gone.\n\nThe page''s organising idea is that every number states how far to trust\nit. Queue depths are counted from the database at read time and are\ncorrect under any replica count; data-quality counters come from the\nreplica that answered and are cumulative since it started. Rendered side\nby side these are the same shape, so the qualifier is the only thing\nbetween a reader and a wrong conclusion. Rates and percentiles render as\na named absence — this console holds no history and says so, rather than\nderiving a rate from a single reading or sending the reader elsewhere.\n\nTwo things the first draft got wrong, found by looking at it rendered:\n\nA tile showed \"these deliveries will never arrive\" against a value of\nzero, stating a live failure that was not happening. The consequence text\nnow appears only when the count is non-zero; an operator who learns to\nignore that caption would ignore the real one too.\n\nThe per-row provenance column repeated one identical sentence four times,\nwrapping three lines each, because every row in that table shares a\nscope. It is stated once beneath the table instead, and the column\nreturns by itself if a reading with a different scope ever joins.\n\nThe guard is renamed check-operational-data-sources and now bans external\ndashboard references and deep-link URL shapes as well as exposition\nparsing — mutation-tested on both rules. `ops:operate` is admin-only,\nmirroring the server; deliberately not `ops:view`, which all four roles\nhold because the endpoints behind it are unauthenticated probes.\n\n11 page tests; 165 tests pass. lint, typecheck, guards, and the bundle\nbudget all pass; operations is 340.6 KB gz against a 360 budget.","tree":{"sha":"cbd7343122839437c0e994e4b1d54a40e6fb804b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/cbd7343122839437c0e994e4b1d54a40e6fb804b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDQ3MGRkZjgzYjg2YmJmZjJlZTcwMWE0Mjk5MDU0NTFhMmU3MTBiYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17","sha":"c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17"}],"sha":"470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/470ddf83b86bbff2ee701a429905451a2e710bb6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:57:55Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:57:55Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T09: the consumer surfaces enter the accessibility gate\n\nBoth new routes added to the axe lane: the notifications inbox, and the\ncapability detail page now that it carries the adopt control and the\nsubscriptions card. Zero critical violations on either, alongside the four\nthings axe cannot see that the spec already asserts by hand -- one main\nlandmark, a skip link that is genuinely first, a single aria-current, and a real\nheading outline.\n\n27 e2e specs pass. Full CI green.\n\nMeasured bundle, which is the number T04''s placement decision was made against\nand which now has an outcome rather than a projection:\n\n  catalog  336.3 -> 338.4 KB gz  (budget 360)\n\n2.1 KB for adopt, subscriptions, the inbox, bulk mark-read, two unavailability\nnotices and a new ui-kit primitive. The alternative the TDD assumed -- a third\nfederated remote -- would have cost roughly 340 KB, because each remote\nre-fetches its own copy of the shared-fallback chunk. Recording the number so\nthe next placement decision compares against a measurement rather than\nrepeating the reasoning.\n\nThe doc-refs guard rejected the first version of this commit for writing\n\"Phase 7''s consumer surfaces\" in a comment: a delivery-phase label says when\ncode was written rather than what it does, and it rots the moment the phase\nends. Second time this guard has been right today.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d854bd78ccd61273af0e594007bce4520ce3a3af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/d854bd78ccd61273af0e594007bce4520ce3a3af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGM3ZWI1MGUwZmM4MDhhOWFiZDcxYWYxZjRlMGYwMTZmMTdkYzNlMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb","sha":"ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb"}],"sha":"c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/c7eb50e0fc808a9abd71af1f4e0f016f17dc3e17"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:56:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:56:04Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T07: bulk mark-read, as a fan-out that admits it is one\n\nNo bulk endpoint exists, so this is one call per notification. Two consequences\nthe UI surfaces rather than hides.\n\nIt is not atomic. A failure partway through leaves earlier items read and later\nones unread -- a legitimate outcome, since the ones that succeeded really are\nread, but not what \"mark all read\" implies. So the hook collects failures\ninstead of throwing on the first, and the page reports the split: \"2 of 7 could\nnot be marked read\", with the reason. Reporting only success would leave a\nreader believing rows cleared that are still listed.\n\nConcurrency is bounded at 4. An unbounded fan-out at a rate-limited API turns a\nconvenience into a 429 storm that leaves more undone than doing nothing would\nhave.\n\nThe control names its own count -- \"Mark 2 read\" -- so the size of the action is\nvisible before it is taken, and it disappears at zero rather than sitting there\ndisabled. A control that can never do anything is noise on the header row.\n\n3 new tests, 177 total. Full CI green; catalog at 338.4 KB gz against 360.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"06dd845be3ce1082884dad413c55f2da3859fe08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/06dd845be3ce1082884dad413c55f2da3859fe08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGFjNTQyYjAzNGQwNWJhNWU0MzMxMWZlOTA4NzE2Zjk2MWUzNTViZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6","sha":"d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6"}],"sha":"ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/ac542b034d05ba5e43311fe908716f961e355bdb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:54:49Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:54:49Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T08: name the two absences instead of rendering hollow panels\n\nTwo surfaces this phase promised are not backed by any endpoint. Both now say\nso, in the place a reader would look for them.\n\nUnavailableNotice is a new ui-kit primitive, generalised out of the metrics\npage which made this argument first. It is deliberately distinct from\nEmptyState, and the distinction is the point: an empty state means the query ran\nand found nothing, so it will fill when data arrives. This means the data does\nnot exist to fetch, so no amount of waiting will populate it.\n\nRendering the second as the first is a lie the panel tells on its own. A reader\nseeing \"No delivery attempts\" concludes deliveries are working and none have\nfailed; the truth is that nothing measures them. `reason` is a required prop for\nthe same reason -- a notice saying only \"unavailable\" moves the question off the\nscreen and back to a person.\n\nDelivery health, on the subscriptions panel: per-attempt outcomes are recorded\nserver-side and no endpoint reads them back. The notice states explicitly that\nthe panel does not infer health from the enabled flag, because an enabled\nsubscription that has failed every delivery looks identical to one that has\nsucceeded.\n\nCross-capability adoptions, on the notifications page: adoption reads one\ncapability at a time, and the consumer graph projection returns connections\nwithout a version pin or behind-status. Assembling a list would mean asserting a\nstatus the server never did. Placed here because this is the only\ncross-capability consumer surface, so it is where the question gets asked.\n\nPer ADR 001 the primitive went into the ui-kit rather than into the remote --\na control invented inside a remote is invisible to the next screen that needs\nit, which is how a second idiom starts.\n\n2 new tests, 174 total. Lint, typecheck, guards, bundle budget all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"13a6b42b686efb23d216a632677622bfa51dc529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/13a6b42b686efb23d216a632677622bfa51dc529"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQ3NzFjZmFkMWVmNDQxNWNjNTJlZmQ2ZTJkNTQ0MjA0ZGUyMWU1YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57","sha":"7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57"}],"sha":"d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d771cfad1ef4415cc52efd6e2d544204de21e5b6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:49:43Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:49:43Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7: conform the new surfaces to the established design baseline\n\nI built these against Salt''s primitives directly instead of against the\nbaseline KUI-P2 established by measuring the reference console. Three concrete\ndeviations, all now corrected.\n\nThe notifications status filter was a row of toggle buttons. Every other filter\nin this app is a bordered Dropdown with Options inside a FilterField, with\npopoverOverlayProps -- the capability list page is the reference and it does\nexactly that three times. A second filter idiom in the same app is the kind of\ndrift that makes a console feel assembled rather than designed.\n\nThe subscriptions panel stacked a table, a form and a note in the card body.\nSectionCard already publishes the slots for this: `description` for what the\nrows are, and `footer` for a tinted strip holding \"a hint on the left, its\naction on the right\". Using the body for all three gave one card two competing\naction zones and put the disclosure after the rows it explains rather than\nbefore them. Now: disclosure in the description, subscribe control in the\nfooter band, table flush so its dividers run to the card edges as one\nseparation mechanism rather than two.\n\nThe adoption control rendered a sentence -- \"Not adopted, a producer or admin\ncan adopt\" -- into the page header''s action slot. That slot holds controls, and\nprose there sits at a different weight and baseline from the buttons beside it.\nReplaced with a disabled Adopt button carrying a tooltip, which keeps the row\nreading as a row of actions while still refusing the affordance visibly.\n\nAlso added zebra to both new tables, which is what the baseline chose as the\nsingle separation mechanism.\n\nTests updated to drive the real controls rather than the ones I had invented:\nthe filter through its combobox and option, and the refused adopt through a\ndisabled button rather than a string. 172 tests, full CI green, bundle\nunchanged at 337.6 KB gz.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"433c7521364f5d7560a3295b17f753a1c78504b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/433c7521364f5d7560a3295b17f753a1c78504b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDdhN2I0MjhhOWViMmZhNGVkYjEyMjRmY2M4M2UxOTQzNTEyZTZiNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c","sha":"6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c"}],"sha":"7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/7a7b428a9eb2fa4edb1224fcc83e1943512e6b57"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:35:31Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:35:31Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T06: the notifications inbox\n\nThe surface the app had no equivalent of. Lists what changed in the\ncapabilities your tenant subscribes to, filterable by unread/read/all, with\nper-item mark-read and a link out to the capability.\n\nIt does not summarise, and that is deliberate. The server minimizes notification\npayloads on purpose -- it withholds the change body so a webhook recipient\ncannot leak it -- so what arrives is a kind, a classification, a version\ntransition, a timestamp and a URL. Composing those into a sentence would read\nlike a description of the change and invite trust in a summary the API never\nsent. The fields render as fields; the link is how you find out what happened.\n\nRead state is a filter, not a field. NotificationItem carries no read flag, so\nmark-read is a call plus an invalidation of the notifications root key, and the\nrow leaves the view because the server stopped returning it. Two tests pin that\ndistinction: one asserts the marked row disappears while its sibling remains --\nproving a refetch rather than a cache clear -- and one asserts it reappears\nunder `all`, which only passes because the invalidation covers every status\nfilter rather than the active one.\n\nRouted ahead of :handle, or /notifications would match as a capability slug and\n404 against the detail endpoint.\n\nThe doc-refs guard caught a requirement ID in the module docstring and refused\nthe commit until the reasoning was written in the code''s own words. Working as\nintended -- shipped code should carry the argument, not a pointer to where the\nargument lives.\n\nBundle: catalog 336.3 -> 337.6 KB gz for both this and the subscriptions panel,\nagainst a 360 budget. 1.3 KB total for two surfaces the TDD had assumed needed a\nthird federated remote costing ~340 KB. The measurement is the justification.\n\n6 new tests, 172 total. Lint, lint:css, typecheck, guards, and bundle budget all\npass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f52b2862ff4720fdf99c1f6e717fe33bc1e46996","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/f52b2862ff4720fdf99c1f6e717fe33bc1e46996"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDZhMWNiMTU4ODNiNzY0MDg0YTkxYTRlZTJiZTdhNDJjZDkxYmVjMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58","sha":"d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58"}],"sha":"6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/6a1cb15883b764084a91a4ee2be7a42cd91bec0c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:33:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:33:22Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T05: subscribe to a capability''s changes, from its own page\n\nCreate, list, and cancel subscriptions, with the event kinds drawn from the\nclosed EVENT_KINDS set. Subscribe is disabled when nothing is selected rather\nthan POSTing an empty event_kinds, which the server accepts and which then never\nfires -- the silent no-op that vocabulary exists to prevent.\n\nPlaced on the capability detail page rather than in a new remote, and the\nmeasurement is why. The TDD assumed a separate remotes/consumer. Measuring\nfirst: catalog was at 336.3 KB gz against a 360 budget, and each remote''s\nfetched total includes its own ~154 KB gz shared-fallback chunk that the budget\nscript documents as re-fetched per remote mount. So a third remoteEntry costs a\nfull duplicate of that for anyone visiting both.\n\nThis panel cost 0.6 KB gz -- 336.3 to 336.9. Roughly three orders of magnitude\ncheaper than the structure the TDD assumed, for a surface that is per-capability\nanyway: subscriptions are read per capability, exactly like adoptions, and there\nis no cross-capability subscription endpoint to build a separate screen against.\n\nThe empty state names the consequence rather than the row count. \"No\nsubscriptions\" states a fact about the table; \"you will not be told when this\ncapability changes\" states the thing the reader is deciding about.\n\nThe panel also discloses that adopting creates a subscription and unadopting\ndoes not remove it, so a reader who finds a row they never made does not\nconclude they subscribed and forgot. That disclosure is only here because the\nPhase 7 review caught my claim that adoption and subscription were independent\n-- they are not, in that direction.\n\n5 new tests, 166 total. Lint, typecheck, guards, and the bundle budget all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"baca9a58622dd04406b966450efd18a551224003","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/baca9a58622dd04406b966450efd18a551224003"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQ1Y2E0NzI2N2MxODk4Yzc3ZGQzM2JhMjFlZmYxYmFmODBhMGNmNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5","sha":"a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5"}],"sha":"d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d5ca47267c1898c77dd33ba21eff1baf80a0cf58"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:48:48Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:48:48Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T03 fix: the real role gate, and the subscription unadopt leaves behind\n\nA review of the Phase 7 spec found two claims I had made without reading the\ncode, and both were wrong in ways that reached the shipped component.\n\nThe role gate is asymmetric and I had it backwards. `_adopt_required` is\nrequire_roles([ROLE_PRODUCER, ROLE_ADMIN]) and excludes consumer outright;\n`_list_adoptions_required` admits all four roles. So every role may read\nadoption state and only producer or admin may change it -- the opposite of this\nfeature''s framing as something a consuming team does.\n\nWorse, the test I shipped rendered as `consumer` and asserted the Adopt button.\nIt passed against MSW and would have 403''d against the real service: a test\ncertifying a broken thing, which is worse than no test. It now defaults to\nproducer and adds two cases proving a consumer sees the state and no action,\nwith copy naming the role that could act. Offering a button guaranteed to 403 is\nworse than offering none, and the registry collapses a principal to one role so\na consumer cannot escalate by also holding producer.\n\nSecond: adopting DOES subscribe. AdoptionService is constructed with\nauto_subscribe=subscriptions.adoption_hook(), and main.py''s own comment says\nadoption \"transparently creates an inbox-only subscription\". `unadopt`\nsoft-deletes the adoption row and touches nothing else, so that subscription\nsurvives and keeps delivering. My unadopt dialog said the record was preserved\nin the audit log and stopped there, which described the action as cleaner than\nit is. It now states that notifications continue and points at Subscriptions.\n\nThis is the second time in this phase I asserted an API behaviour instead of\nreading it. The pattern is consistent: the claims that turn out false are always\nthe ones I found plausible enough not to check.\n\n161 tests. Lint, typecheck, guards green. PRD corrected at source as rev 6, with\nOQ-KUI-11 opened for whether CAP should cancel the subscription on unadopt --\nthe UI can disclose that asymmetry but cannot fix it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb86b4ec620f0f69c7d874ed7c6b4c25112c5bad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/eb86b4ec620f0f69c7d874ed7c6b4c25112c5bad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGE1M2ZhMTFlMzIzMmMzNDMyOTJkZWVkYjNmMTQwNjVmY2YwYzI4ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28","sha":"57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28"}],"sha":"a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a53fa11e3232c343292deedb3f14065fcf0c28e5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:45:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:45:16Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T03: adopt and unadopt from the capability detail page\n\nThe first consumer capability in the app. Adopt sits on the detail page rather\nthan in a consumer remote because the point is acting on the thing already in\nfront of you -- sending a reader elsewhere to declare a dependency on what they\nare currently reading would be worse than not offering it.\n\nState comes from the server, never from the last mutation. The button renders\nfrom a read of the adoption endpoint, and a successful write invalidates that\nread rather than seeding it, so a POST that succeeded and was then reversed by a\nteammate cannot leave the button claiming a state that no longer holds. The\ncomponent test drives a stateful MSW store precisely so this is provable: a\nfixed handler would pass for a component that merely guessed correctly.\n\nThree states are kept distinct because collapsing them is how this goes wrong:\nin-flight renders a disabled \"Checking adoption…\" rather than \"Adopt\", since\noffering an action that may be wrong a moment later and then flipping the label\nis what makes a reader stop trusting a page; a failed read reports the failure\nrather than degrading to \"not adopted\", which are different facts; and unadopt\nconfirms first, saying explicitly that the record is preserved in the audit log,\nbecause otherwise \"Unadopt\" reads as a deletion.\n\nCopy says \"your tenant\", never \"your team\" -- the API records adoption at tenant\ngranularity with team attribution as free text in `intent`, and implying\nper-team adoption would describe a distinction the server does not make.\n\nTwo infrastructure gaps surfaced and are fixed here:\n\n- remotes/catalog had no vitest.config.ts, so the first .test.tsx resolved\n  against vite.config.ts with the Module Federation plugin loaded and vitest''s\n  default node environment. It failed inside user-event''s prepareDocument with a\n  missing document symbol, which reads as a testing-library problem and is\n  actually a missing DOM. remotes/operations'' own config file predicted this\n  exact failure in its docstring; the new file records that it came true, since\n  the error names nothing that points at the config.\n- The same tsconfig lacked @testing-library/jest-dom in `types`, so the suite\n  passed while typecheck rejected every toBeInTheDocument.\n\nStateful MSW handlers added for adoption, subscriptions, and notifications. The\nnotification handler strips its internal `read` flag from responses, because the\nreal item carries no such field and a component must not start depending on\nsomething the API never sends.\n\n159 tests across 13 files. Lint, lint:css, typecheck, and all three guards green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"088cbc8bd59046633391de8ff1a54c6315f0b749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/088cbc8bd59046633391de8ff1a54c6315f0b749"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDU3Mzk4YWVkMDFiMTg0M2E5NTQ0ZDdiNDA2ZGQzNWZlMTM5YTZlMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859","sha":"b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859"}],"sha":"57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/57398aed01b1843a9544d7b406dd35fe139a6e28"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:41:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:41:08Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T02: typed hooks for adoption, subscriptions, and notifications\n\nThe data layer for the consumer surfaces. Three things that look related and\nare deliberately not coupled: adopting records that you depend on a capability,\nsubscribing says which changes you want to hear about, the inbox is where they\narrive. A team may watch something it has not adopted, and adopting does not\nsilently subscribe -- coupling them would be a policy this client invented\nrather than one the server expresses.\n\nShapes were read off the live OpenAPI rather than assumed, and two of them\nchanged the design:\n\n- GET /v1/capabilities/{id}/adoptions returns the CALLING TENANT''S OWN adoption\n  for one capability, not a roster of adopters. So useAdoption returns the first\n  item or null: more than one active adoption of the same capability by the same\n  tenant is not a state the server produces, and rendering a list would prepare\n  for a case that cannot arrive.\n- NotificationItem carries no read flag. Read state exists only as the list''s\n  `status` filter, defaulting to unread. So mark-read is a call plus an\n  invalidation of the notifications root, never a local edit -- and the root key\n  exists precisely so marking read in the default view does not leave the `all`\n  view showing the item as unread. A test asserts every status-filtered key is a\n  child of that root.\n\nNo optimistic updates, following the repo''s existing stance: adoption state is\nread back from the server, so a POST that succeeded and was then reversed\nelsewhere cannot leave the button claiming a state that no longer holds.\n\nEVENT_KINDS is enumerated because the server''s vocabulary is closed and a typo\nin event_kinds is accepted syntactically and then matches nothing -- a\nsubscription that exists and never fires is worse than one that was refused.\n\nPAGE_LIMITS gains a notifications entry at the API''s own default of 50, so an\nunspecified page size produces the same result whether the client sends it or\nomits it.\n\n8 new tests, 153 total. Lint, typecheck, and all three guards green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b6305ee992824f7e9c247397e9d4772ef934d2ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/b6305ee992824f7e9c247397e9d4772ef934d2ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGI5YjM2YzU0Mjc2M2Q0ZmZiM2Q1MDlhOGNjNmFhZjJiNTFlZGE4NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27","sha":"28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27"}],"sha":"b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b9b36c542763d4ffb3d509a8cc6aaf2b51eda859"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:38:33Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T21:38:33Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P7-T01: regenerate the typed client against the live API\n\nThe vendored OpenAPI snapshot was 22 paths behind the service -- 65 against\n87 -- so the client was typed off a contract that had moved. The six paths\nPhase 7 needs happened to be present, but building a consumer surface against\na stale snapshot is how a UI ends up bound to a shape that has since changed.\n\nCopied registry/openapi.json over the vendored snapshot and re-ran codegen.\nFormatted with prettier to match the committed style: openapi-typescript emits\n4-space double-quoted output and the repo''s committed generated file is\n2-space single-quoted, so skipping the format step would have shown the whole\nfile as changed and hidden the actual delta.\n\nGates green: typecheck, 145 tests across 11 files, and all three guards\n(no-doc-refs, shared-parity, salt-tokens).\n\nNo behaviour change -- types only. This is the prerequisite for the adoption,\nsubscription, and notification hooks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53d8ee60a24a76697f99ded8a3900989a92bef20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/53d8ee60a24a76697f99ded8a3900989a92bef20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDI4Y2ExYmY0NzIxNzkyYTU1NDZjYmZiNzcyZjgzNjEwZDRiNTljMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32","sha":"a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32"}],"sha":"28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/28ca1bf4721792a5546cbfb772f83610d4b59c27"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T15:08:32Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T15:08:32Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P3c: the deadline lost a race it had to win, and two bugs visible only on real data\n\nAsked to validate the spin fix with actual screenshots rather than text extraction.\nDoing that showed the previous claim was wrong in a way that mattered.\n\nThe deadline was never reached. Measured with the API forward wedged: Vite''s dev proxy\ngives up on a dead upstream at 15.33s and answers 500, so a 20s client deadline lost\nthe race every time. The reader got `internal_error · HTTP 500` — which names nothing\nthey can act on — after fifteen seconds of blank spinner. The fix was real but it was\nnot doing the work.\n\n- Default deadline 20s -> 10s, so the timeout wins and the message that names the\n  likely cause is the one shown. The number is now measured against the proxy rather\n  than picked, and `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS` is exported so a test asserts the real value\n  instead of a copy that would drift.\n- Reads should not wait for the worst-case write, so `RequestOptions.timeoutMs` allows\n  a per-request override and create takes 30s — it runs `connector.validate()`\n  server-side, an outbound round trip.\n\nTwo bugs found by looking at screenshots of real data\n- `lifecycle` rendered as the literal text \"[object Object]\" on every capability\n  detail page. `attributes` is `Record<string, unknown>` and the server means it: real\n  data carries `lifecycle: {\"state\": \"beta\"}`, and `String(value)` on a dict produces\n  that. The fixture had only string attributes, so no test could see it. Added\n  `AttributeValue`, which renders objects as compact JSON in the mono face, and gave\n  the fixture an object-valued attribute so it cannot regress.\n\nVerified visually, not by innerText, against the live registry\n- API wedged: spinner at 5s and 15s, error at 10.26s after the change, with the\n  timeout message and a sentence-case Try again.\n- Try again clicked after repairing the API: recovers to the loaded overview with\n  \"API ready\".\n- Every route screenshotted and read: home, catalog, search, detail, health, metrics,\n  audit (gated), sync, runs, plus dark mode with the create form open.\n- Zero console errors across the sweep. Full CI, 145 unit tests, 25 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aee05e7cecf65d2ff68115209f7f7c669f239b61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/aee05e7cecf65d2ff68115209f7f7c669f239b61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGEyNDI2Yzk3YTc2YTI4MjA2MTIyYjhlMzk1YmMxOTI5MDVhMDBlMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70","sha":"b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70"}],"sha":"a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/a2426c97a76a28206122b8e395bc192905a00e32"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:47:19Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:47:19Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P3b: a stalled request hung the whole app instead of failing\n\nReported as \"localhost:5170 just spins\". The cause was not the spinner: `fetch` has\nno default timeout, so a connection that is accepted and then never answered leaves\nits promise pending forever. React Query holds such a query `isPending`, and the\nsession bootstrap renders its spinner off exactly that — so the application sat on\n\"Resolving your session\" indefinitely with no error, no retry, and nothing on screen\nto explain it. The app already had good copy for this failure and could not reach it.\n\n- `client.request` now carries a 20s deadline, composed with the caller''s signal via\n  `AbortSignal.any` so React Query can still cancel on unmount. 20s is set against\n  the slowest legitimate call: creating a sync source runs `connector.validate()`\n  server-side, which is a round trip to whatever the credential points at.\n- A new `timeout` error code, distinct from `network_error`. The distinction is the\n  useful part: refused means nothing is listening, timeout means something accepted\n  the connection and went quiet — and the message names the likely cause.\n\nA precedence bug found while testing the fix: `isAbort` treats *any* AbortError as a\ncancellation, which was correct while the caller''s signal was the only one. With a\ndeadline aborting the same way, checking it first relabelled every timeout as a\ncancellation, React Query swallowed it as a cancelled query, and the spinner stayed\nput — the fix would have silently done nothing. Extracted `classify()` so the\ncaller''s signal is asked first, then ours, then anything else.\n\nTwo things the resulting screen exposed\n- `ErrorPanel` printed \"HTTP 0\". Status 0 is what a timeout and a network failure\n  carry and it means no HTTP response arrived; rendering it invites a reader to look\n  up a status code that does not exist. Now omitted.\n- The retry button read \"TRY AGAIN\". Button typography was scoped to `.shell`, and\n  the session bootstrap renders *before* `AppShell` exists — so pre-shell and\n  portalled buttons kept Salt''s uppercase while everything inside the frame was\n  sentence case. Moved to the theme root, which is what the scope should have been.\n\nVerified by holding a route open with no response: the app now shows the error and a\nworking retry at the deadline instead of spinning. Full CI, 143 unit tests, 25 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"14905150ab7edb7a52f4132258a95bcbd923ee7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/14905150ab7edb7a52f4132258a95bcbd923ee7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGI3NGJlNGIwNjdkNDYyMmEzNjc0MWVjNTk0NWJiNWVlNjI5MWVhNzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a","sha":"f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a"}],"sha":"b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/b74be4b067d4622a36741ec5945bb5ee6291ea70"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:38:56Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:38:56Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P3a: deactivation was a one-way door against the real registry\n\n`GET /v1/admin/sync-sources` is `active_only: bool = Query(True)` — it hides inactive\nsources unless asked. `SyncSourcesPage` omitted the parameter, so deactivating a\nsource removed it from the table, the Reactivate control became unreachable, and the\nconfirm dialog''s \"Reversible: the source can be reactivated from this table\" was\nsimply untrue.\n\nEvery one of the 140 tests passed, and that is the interesting part: the MSW handler\ndefaulted `active_only` to false — showing everything — so the mocked lane could not\nexpress the bug. The mock was wrong about a default and the wrongness was invisible\nbecause it was more generous than the server.\n\nFound by running the app against the live stack, not by reading code.\n\n- The page now asks for `activeOnly: false`, with a comment saying why it is\n  load-bearing rather than a default being restated.\n- The mock defaults to true, as the server does, so anything that needs a deactivated\n  source has to say so.\n- Three handler tests that silently depended on the old default now spell\n  `?active_only=false`, plus a new one pinning that the default hides inactive rows.\n- A component test asserts the round trip: an already-inactive source is listed with\n  Reactivate and a disabled Run now, and a source deactivated during the session\n  stays on screen.\n\nVerified against the live registry end to end: create -> 201, trigger -> 202 (whose\n`sync_run_id` is confirmed different from the run row that follows, exactly as the\nplan predicted), run appears, deactivate -> 200, source stays visible, reactivate\n-> 200. Plus full CI, 141 unit tests, 25 e2e specs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68038a9da529c0021210bd456894ad8835a16811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/68038a9da529c0021210bd456894ad8835a16811"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGY2Y2M1N2NkNDhmNmFkMGE1NmMyZTQ4NjA2ZmQxMDE2YTc0YTRjM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe","sha":"eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe"}],"sha":"f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/f6cc57cd48f6ad0a56c2e48606fd1016a74a4c3a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:25:28Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T03:25:28Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P3: admin console slice 1 — sync connectors and the write path\n\nThe app reached 8 of the registry''s 103 operations and every one was a GET. This\nadds the first write surface, and the conventions the ones after it inherit.\n\nFeature\nSync connectors under /ops/sync and /ops/sync/runs, admin-only: list sources,\ncreate one, deactivate and reactivate, trigger a run, and read the run history\nfiltered by source and status with the failure detail behind a per-row expander.\nNew capability `admin:manage` -> [''admin''], gating both routes via GuardedAdmin,\nthe same pattern the audit log already used one level less strict.\n\nWrite-path conventions, each with its reasoning in the code\n- Mutations live in api-client/src/mutations.ts and name RegistryError explicitly,\n  or error.items needs a cast at every call site.\n- The idempotency key is minted inside mutationFn. Not in the client, which knows\n  nothing about which endpoints declare the header; not at the call site, because a\n  caller who forgets gets an inert context server-side and loses protection with no\n  error. Correct only because `mutations: { retry: 0 }` is set — noted at the mint.\n- Invalidation is by prefix under a shared ''admin'' key segment, so the blunt option\n  is bounded and cannot reach catalog, search or ops.\n- Feedback is an inline ActionResult, not a toast: ui-kit is not a federation share,\n  so a ToastProvider inside a remote creates a context the host never sees.\n- ConfirmDialog owns the mutation''s error while open and closes only on success.\n  Deactivate gets one; Run now deliberately does not.\n- No optimistic updates, for three endpoint-specific reasons rather than taste.\n\nTwo bugs this shipped and then fixed, both found by running it\n- `fieldErrors`/`formErrors` used `instanceof RegistryError`. api-client is bundled\n  into the shell *and* each remote, so the client that throws and the page that maps\n  are different copies and the guard was always false: a 422 of field errors came out\n  as zero field errors and one form-level message, the exact inverse. Now duck-typed,\n  as ErrorPanel already was for the same reason. Regression tests at both the unit\n  level and — necessarily — across the real boundary in Playwright.\n- Salt renders a placeholder in the secondary *foreground* at full opacity, so an\n  empty required field showed \"platform-openapi\" and \"Field required\" at once.\n  Examples moved into helper text.\n\nTest lanes\nFirst jsdom project in the repo. remotes/operations had no vitest.config.ts, so it\nresolved against vite.config.ts with the federation plugin loaded and inherited\nenvironment: ''node'' — harmless only because it held no tests. Adding the config\nneeded two jsdom stubs Salt requires: ResizeObserver (ViewportProvider) and\nscrollIntoView (list controls).\n\n`renderWithProviders` and `scenarios` had been written and imported by nothing; both\nnow have callers. scenarios'' twelve factories were all `http.get`, so a write-path\ntest asking for forbidden() let its POST escape to the real network — now every\nmethod. adminSyncHandlers is the first stateful handler group, with resetAdminStore\nbecause resetHandlers does not clear module state.\n\nAlso fixed: a circular import between handlers.ts and adminSync.ts that left\nadminSyncHandlers undefined when spread, resolved by extracting the role resolver.\n\nKnown gap, left visible: Salt sets no aria-invalid on a field with\nvalidationStatus=\"error\" — it associates the message via aria-describedby only.\nDocumented in FormRow; the tests assert what Salt actually does.\n\nHousekeeping: RemoteDescriptor.need was typed `string`, so a capability typo was not\na compile error; now Capability, and App.tsx reads descriptor.need instead of\nrestating the literal beside a fallback path.\n\nVerified: full CI green, 139 unit tests (was 110), 25 e2e specs (was 18), zero\ncontrast failures across 440 text nodes in light and dark, no console errors, and\nevery flow driven in a real browser against the built federated artefacts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cec1df52a30efaa394af01cbf1eb77cc4932e14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/9cec1df52a30efaa394af01cbf1eb77cc4932e14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGVhYjc1YzRhM2RjNjQwZDdlNmVlZjJmNTY2ZGEyNWFmNjllMDk3ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e","sha":"14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e"}],"sha":"eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/eab75c4a3dc640d7e6eef2f566da25af69e097fe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:52:27Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:52:27Z","email":"martinmarzejon@Martins-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P2: application shell, federated remotes, and the design baseline\n\nEverything between the shared-package layer and a running application, plus the\npass that made it match the reference console. One commit because it is one\nunbroken piece of work: the intermediate states do not build independently, and\nsplitting it retroactively would produce commits that were never verified.\n\nApplication\n- apps/shell: route table, providers, session bootstrap against /v1/whoami with\n  the four outcomes (session, tenant_required, one auth re-mint, seed diagnostic),\n  persona switching with a full cache clear, remote error boundary, home page,\n  session debug, 404.\n- remotes/catalog: capability list with URL-held filter state and cursor paging,\n  and capability detail.\n- remotes/operations: health, metrics, audit log.\n- Federation: two remotes exposing ./App only, shared singletons pinned by\n  mf.shared.ts and enforced by check-shared-parity.\n\nui-kit\nAppShell, AppSidebar (resizable rail with route-derived drill-down), PageHeader,\nSectionCard, StatTile, NavCard, DataTable, FilterBar, CursorPager, ScopeSwitcher,\nScopeBreadcrumb, EmptyState, LoadingPanel, ErrorPanel, CopyButton, JsonDiff,\nSparkline, RetrievalArmsBar.\n\nDesign baseline\nMeasured against the reference rather than matched by eye. Page title now\n24/600/32 with -0.96px tracking; interface text at weight 500; hairlines from\n0.2 to 0.1 alpha; radius uniformly 6px; canvas tint on the document; tables on\nSalt''s own zebra + divider props with one separation mechanism instead of two;\nbuttons in sentence case via --saltButton-*, Salt''s own API rather than a token\nlayer.\n\nThree things found while measuring, each a real defect:\n- Salt''s Text resets no heading margin and neither theme resets the UA''s, so\n  every `as=\"h2\"` carried ~30px of phantom space -- a card header band measured\n  90px around 24px of text.\n- PageHeader branched on `typeof description === ''string''` to decide the prose\n  measure. A fragment skipped the wrapper and StackLayout''s flex column put each\n  child on its own line. Replaced with explicit description/metadata slots.\n- DataTable never passed the row index while a caller declared\n  `(row, index = 0)`, so every id-less fact collided on the key \"0\".\n\nGuards\ntheme-fixups.css was the one stylesheet neither stylelint nor check-salt-tokens\nlooked at -- the file that exists to repair dangling tokens. Both now cover all\n.css, with ignoreFiles for build output.\n\nVerified: full CI green, 110 unit tests, 18 e2e specs, zero contrast failures\nacross 480 text nodes in light and dark, no console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"21ccead51372d130253f4c7d554954ab66964aa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/21ccead51372d130253f4c7d554954ab66964aa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDE0NTI0YjcyYjc3ZTM3YjM3MTljMmEzMWE5ODViNGJmYzdiZmViMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237","sha":"0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237"}],"sha":"14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/14524b72b77e37b3719c2a31a985b4bfc7bfeb2e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:40:05Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:40:05Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P1-T02: ui-kit and testing packages complete the shared layer\n\n96 tests, typecheck clean, lint and stylelint clean, both guards passing.\n\nui-kit composes Salt and nothing else, with one exception. Three components have\nno Salt equivalent — a proportional multi-segment bar for search retrieval arms,\na before/after key diff for audit entries, and an inline trend line for metrics —\nand each gets a colocated CSS Module where every design value is a var(--salt-*)\ntoken. Verified the rule bites: a probe stylesheet with #ff0000 and 4px is\nrejected on both properties.\n\nThe pure logic inside those three is where the tests are, because that is where\nthis kind of component silently produces a wrong picture rather than an error.\nAn all-zero arm breakdown returns null instead of NaN segment widths. A flat\nseries sits on the midline instead of dividing by its zero range. A gap in the\nseries breaks the line into segments rather than drawing through it — a gap means\na counter reset, and joining across one would render a plunge and a climb that\nnever happened.\n\nCursorPager has no page number, deliberately: the list endpoints return items\nand next_cursor and no total, so a count would have to be invented, and a wrong\ncount is worse than an absent one because a reader acts on it.\n\ntesting ships fixtures shaped like the actual responses, and a test for the\nfixtures themselves. That is unusual but earns its place: makeEntityRef asserts\nit has NO lifecycle key, because the list endpoint does not return one, and a\nfixture richer than the server teaches every test written against it a shape\nthat only fails in production. The lifecycle vocabulary is asserted to be\nalpha/beta/ga/deprecated/retired — the sibling app''s fixtures use active and\ndraft, which do not exist.\n\nMSW handlers are origin-agnostic so the same set runs under jsdom, under the\nservice worker, and behind the dev proxy. They implement real cursor paging\nrather than faking it, and reproduce the two different invalid-cursor statuses\nthe server uses: 400 on the list endpoints, 422 on audit.\n\nrenderWithProviders wraps the same provider stack in the same order as the shell.\nThe sibling app has two stacks that have drifted apart, which means its tests\npass against a tree that does not exist at runtime.\n\nFour fixes worth noting, all found by the typechecker rather than by review:\nStackLayout has no justify prop (that is FlexLayout); CSS Modules need an ambient\ndeclaration or every import is unresolved; a comment containing a slash-star\nsequence closed itself and broke the file it documented; and packages/auth now\ntypes the build flags locally instead of borrowing Vite''s ambient globals, so it\ncompiles standalone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b96ad9bad15a972586c83904b7f23236647a69b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/b96ad9bad15a972586c83904b7f23236647a69b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKDBhZTIxM2NiMDRjY2Y0MDA2MjFlMGI0NTNlMTQ2MWY4NTk3YzIyMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332","sha":"d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332"}],"sha":"0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/0ae213cb04ccf400621e0b453e1461f8597c2237"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:23:05Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:23:05Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P1-T01: contract, auth and api-client packages\n\nThe three packages everything else is written against. 71 tests, typecheck clean.\n\nremote-contract is types only, deliberately. It is the host-to-remote handshake,\nand Module Federation resolves remotes at runtime — so this is how the check\ncomes back: both sides import the same props type and tsc catches a drift even\nthough the import is dynamic. A runtime export here would be duplicated into\nevery bundle and identity comparisons across the boundary would fail.\n\nauth owns identity and permissions. Two decisions worth naming:\n\nGating is by capability, not role. Components ask can(session, ''audit:read'') and\nonly the matrix knows which roles carry it. The matrix mirrors the server rather\nthan implementing it — ''audit:read'' is auditor-only and specifically NOT admin,\nbecause the API guards that endpoint with an exact auditor check while\ncollapsing a principal''s grants to one role by precedence. An admin+auditor\nprincipal therefore resolves to admin and is refused, so adding admin to the\ntable would not widen access, only produce a nav entry leading to a 403.\n\nsession.role always comes from whoami. The persona registry decides which token\nto mint and nothing else; a UI that derived permissions locally would offer\nactions the server rejects. toSession() throws on an unrecognised role rather\nthan defaulting, because every default is a guess about authorisation.\n\nThe persona roster lives behind a guarded dynamic import so the bundler can drop\nit — it carries dev client secrets, and CI greps dist/ for them.\n\napi-client hand-writes the error envelope instead of generating it. The OpenAPI\ndocument describes every failure as FastAPI''s HTTPValidationError, which is not\nwhat the server sends for any status the UI branches on. Notably\navailable_tenants arrives inside errors[0], not at the envelope root, so a\nreader looking at the wrong level silently never opens the tenant picker.\n\nThe Prometheus parser is tested against a verbatim capture from a running\nregistry rather than invented input, which is how the histogram-suffix and +Inf\ncases got covered. An all-zero histogram returns undefined, not 0 — a p95 of\nzero reads as \"very fast\" when the truth is \"no data\".\n\nAlso fixed: isUsable() is a type predicate, so callers can read .token after\nchecking it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d185706933dd521978ecfdcad8ebd2a89aad2e5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/d185706933dd521978ecfdcad8ebd2a89aad2e5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQwNWFhZWQyN2MyMGJiMDFkYTJjZDk1MDU2ZmRmNWZkMzI0MTkzMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7","sha":"d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7"}],"sha":"d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d05aaed27c20bb01da2cd95056fdf5fd32419332"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T06:01:48Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T06:01:48Z","email":"martin@local","name":"Martin Marzejon"},"message":"KUI-P0-T01: repo, workspaces and the guards that hold the design together\n\nScaffolds the monorepo: npm workspaces over apps/shell, remotes/{catalog,\noperations} and five packages, strict TypeScript project references, flat\nESLint, stylelint, and Prettier.\n\nThree pieces carry most of the weight:\n\nmf.shared.ts is the single declaration of what Module Federation shares. Every\nentry is a singleton with an exact version, and the load-bearing ones use\nstrictVersion so a drift throws at startup. The failure it prevents is the one\nworth preventing: two copies of a shared module is a console warning and then a\nhook error somewhere unrelated, or a Salt component rendering unthemed because\nthe theme context it reads is not the one the host populated. react-router is\nshared alongside react-router-dom because the router contexts live in the\nformer; sharing only the latter leaves useParams() returning {} inside a remote.\n\ndev-proxy.ts is the single proxy table. The API ships no CORS middleware, so a\nbrowser cannot call it cross-origin at all, and every dev and preview server\nproxies it from its own origin instead. The app builds relative URLs and never\nlearns the API''s real origin.\n\nTwo guard scripts, both negative-tested: check-shared-parity fails on any caret\nor mismatch against mf.shared.ts, and check-no-doc-refs keeps internal planning\nlabels out of shipped code.\n\nESLint enforces the Salt-only rule directly — Salt-covered intrinsics are\nbanned outside ui-kit, literal values in a style prop are an error, and\nCSS-in-JS and non-module stylesheets are blocked. stylelint restricts every\ndesign value in a *.module.css to a var(--salt-*) token.\n\nTwo upstream findings, both verified against the registry:\n\n- @salt-ds/core@1.68.0 is unresolvable as published. It depends on\n  @salt-ds/icons@^1.18.2, and 1.18.0 is the newest icons release that exists;\n  1.67.1 has the same problem against ^1.18.1. Pinned to 1.67.0, which asks for\n  ^1.18.0 and installs.\n- react resolved to 19.2.8 through testing-library''s peer range, because\n  nothing at the root pinned it. Overrides force 18.3.1 tree-wide, matching the\n  version Salt''s own CI runs. Verified: one hoisted copy of every shared module,\n  no nested duplicates.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c8824a8b44ab91b6f6b438b64f4a88eb4d863ea1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/trees/c8824a8b44ab91b6f6b438b64f4a88eb4d863ea1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/git/commits/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commit/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7","node_id":"C_kwDOTtVZdNoAKGQ5MzlmNzIzNGIyN2FlZGM1OGUyMTc5NzA5YWI1OGE4YzJhODg3ZTc","parents":[],"sha":"d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits/d939f7234b27aedc58e2179709ab58a8c2a887e7"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/knowledge-ui/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=3af597d547320e444da6583eb25c0dfab717386e&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A38%3A12.202Z"}');
