_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/commits/bcb434272f179d1b722656d3f9aecf1c0d187662/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T15:54:42Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T15:54:42Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"message":"chore: drop stale committed app build output, fix stale README note\n\npackages/searm-apps/public/customer-support/.twenty/output was build output\ncommitted before the rebrand. The CLI now emits .searm, so the old tree was\ndead weight that regenerated on every build and kept ''twenty'' appearing in\nsearch results. Removed and both paths gitignored.\n\nREADME no longer claims the CLI and SDK are unrenamed; they are searm-cli and\nsearm-sdk now.\n\nRemaining ''twenty'' in tracked source is 16 lines, all deliberate: AGPL-required\nattribution in README and LICENSE files, the English word in ERP-MVP-PLAN, and\nthe gitignore pattern itself.","tree":{"sha":"d9c6f167a4b9b64725a8ae8ab50b6e154fdaa64d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/trees/d9c6f167a4b9b64725a8ae8ab50b6e154fdaa64d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/commits/bcb434272f179d1b722656d3f9aecf1c0d187662","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123623531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vatsa10","id":123623531,"login":"Vatsa10","node_id":"U_kgDOB15Yaw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Vatsa10/Harbour/commit/bcb434272f179d1b722656d3f9aecf1c0d187662","node_id":"C_kwDOTtosW9oAKGJjYjQzNDI3MmYxNzlkMWI3MjI2NTZkM2Y5YWVjZjFjMGQxODc2NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Vatsa10/Harbour/commit/b909db6b62047aeb032ce3a8c0dd713c9a7b0ee7","sha":"b909db6b62047aeb032ce3a8c0dd713c9a7b0ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/commits/b909db6b62047aeb032ce3a8c0dd713c9a7b0ee7"}],"sha":"bcb434272f179d1b722656d3f9aecf1c0d187662","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/commits/bcb434272f179d1b722656d3f9aecf1c0d187662"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123623531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vatsa10","id":123623531,"login":"Vatsa10","node_id":"U_kgDOB15Yaw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/commits/b909db6b62047aeb032ce3a8c0dd713c9a7b0ee7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T15:52:25Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T15:52:25Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"message":"feat(ai-write-approval): attribute approved AI writes to the AI, not the approver\n\nCharter Principal contract: an AI-originated change must be distinguishable\nfrom a hand-typed one. It was not. buildApproverContext stamped\nFieldActorSource.MANUAL with the approving human''s name and an empty context,\nso an approved AI edit was indistinguishable from a human one in the record''s\nactor trail.\n\nAttribution now names the proposing actor, with the approver recorded in\ncontext as approvedByWorkspaceMemberId alongside the proposalId, so both\nparties to the change are recoverable. A proposal carrying no creator actor\nresolves to SYSTEM rather than MANUAL - we cannot name an author, and\ncrediting the approving human would assert authorship nobody claimed.\n\nPermissions are unchanged: the write still executes as the approver, so\nobject and field permissions are enforced by the ordinary ORM path.\n\nAlso adds the CREATE_AGENT_TASK workflow action type, and pins the spread in\nworkflow-validation to typeof step - widening the step union tipped it past\nTypeScript''s complexity limit (TS2590).\n\n37/37 proposal-execution tests pass. Server typecheck 0.","tree":{"sha":"fb8f73938c811c9f0fffda560cb40faa6e1a173e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/trees/fb8f73938c811c9f0fffda560cb40faa6e1a173e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/comm