"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/commits/56670cf64474e579c642cd797cbc3e30687cccd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T21:34:59Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T21:34:59Z","email":"vatsajoshi2@gmail.com","name":"Vatsa Joshi"},"message":"docs(clean-room): record a real breach - six auth/ Enterprise files read in full\n\nSSO agent batch-read six SAML/OIDC files without the grep pre-check because\nthey live in auth/ rather than sso/. Protected expression, not de minimis.\nAgent retired; nothing was written or committed.\n\nRoot cause is mine: scoping tasks by directory implied other directories were\nsafe to read. Enterprise files are scattered - SSO guards live under auth/,\nand all 12 workspace-migration Enterprise files are row-level-permission\nfiles. Location carries no license signal. Every file now needs the grep\ncheck before opening, consumer or not.","tree":{"sha":"1ae78d7b02aacda216cd325d492372971d13e9e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/trees/1ae78d7b02aacda216cd325d492372971d13e9e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vatsa10/Harbour/git/commits/56670cf64474e579c642cd797cbc3e30687cccd3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123623531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vatsa10/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Vatsa10","id"