rs.githubusercontent.com/u/3944034?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimou","id":3944034,"login":"guimou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NDQwMzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/quickstarts-manager/commits/2f1e708cfdaca24fd090f23f7d9b1469b758f999/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:43:20Z","email":"guimou@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Guillaume Moutier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:43:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add Helm values customization UI for install/upgrade (#18)\n\n* feat: add Helm values customization UI for install/upgrade\n\nAdd an author-curated deployment.configurableValues spec section that\ndrives a values form in the install dialog (behind a \"Show advanced\noptions\" toggle) and a new upgrade dialog pre-filled with the actually\ninstalled values.\n\n- spec/types: configurableValues (key, label, description, type,\n  default, required, optional options enum) on deployment\n- frontend: values utils (validation mirrors BFF flat-scalar\n  constraints), QuickstartValuesForm, install-dialog integration,\n  UpgradeQuickstartModal, getValues hook method, page wiring\n- bff: helmGetValues (helm get values -o json) + GET /:name/values\n- empty optional fields are omitted so chart defaults apply\n- docs: quickstart-spec + template configurableValues examples\n\nBackward compatible: quickstarts without configurableValues install\nand upgrade exactly as before.\n\nCloses #16\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: fix useQuickstartCatalog mock to match API response shape\n\nThe mount test mocked the /api/catalog response body as a bare array,\nbut the hook (and the BFF) use { quickstarts: [...] }, so data.quickstarts\nwas undefined and the assertion failed. Wrap the mock accordingly.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: explain Helm value precedence and when advanced options appear\n\nAdd a \"How Helm values are resolved\" subsection to the quickstart spec:\nthe three override layers (chart values.yaml < defaultValues <\nconfigurableValues), that the plugin overrides via --set rather than\nediting values.yaml, and that the \"Show advanced options\" toggle only\nappears when configurableValues is declared.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3039b0f2fced01255aefa24f97bf92bcac22029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/quickstarts-manager/git/trees/d3039b0f2fced01255aefa24f97bf92bcac22029"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rh-ai-community-plugins/quickstarts-manager/git/commits/2f1e708cfdaca24fd090f23f7d9b1469b758f999","verification":{"payload":"tree d3039b0f2fced01255aefa24f97bf92bcac22029\nparent c9710a97cac337ab0f41550993d6c2f33f32bff0\nauthor Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com> 1786135400 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786135400 -0400\n\nfeat: add Helm values customization UI for install/upgrade (#18)\n\n* feat: add Helm values customization UI for install/upgrade\n\nAdd an author-curated deployment.configurableValues spec section that\ndrives a values form in the install dialog (behind a \"Show advanced\noptions\" toggle) and a new upgrade dialog pre-filled with the actually\ninstalled values.\n\n- spec/types: configurableValues (key, label, description, type,\n  default, required, optional options enum) on deployment\n- frontend: values utils (validation mirrors BFF flat-scalar\n  constraints), QuickstartValuesForm, install-dialog integration,\n  UpgradeQuickstartModal, getValues hook method, page wiring\n- bff: helmGetValues (helm get values -o json) + GET /:name/values\n- empty optional fields are omitted so chart defaults apply\n- docs: quickstart-spec + template configurableValues examples\n\nBackward compatible: quickstarts without configurableValues install\nand upgrade exactly as before.\n\nCloses #16\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: fix useQuickstartCatalog mock to match API response shape\n\nThe mount test mocked the /api/catalog response body as a bare array,\nbut the hook (and the BFF) use { quickstarts: [...] }, so data.quickstarts\nwas undefined and the assertion failed. Wrap the mock accordingly.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier <guimou@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: explain Helm value precedence and when advanced options appear\n\nAdd a \"How Helm values are resolved\" subsection to the quickstart spec:\nthe three override layers (chart values.yaml < defaultValues <\nconfigurableValues), that the plugin overrides via --set rather than\nediting values.yaml, and that the \"Show advanced options\" toggle only\nappears when configurableValues is declared.\n\n---\nSigned-off-by: Guillaume Moutier 