/commit/48a8c18eb4c78f62cd007dd56a105c59a55491ef","sha":"48a8c18eb4c78f62cd007dd56a105c59a55491ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aregnaud-newforma/frontend-demo-app/commits/48a8c18eb4c78f62cd007dd56a105c59a55491ef"}],"sha":"071f0e9d8b3b668bf8d3b4f5d58b3f2a79396af3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aregnaud-newforma/frontend-demo-app/commits/071f0e9d8b3b668bf8d3b4f5d58b3f2a79396af3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/305502597?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/aregnaud-newforma","id":305502597,"login":"aregnaud-newforma","node_id":"U_kgDOEjWZhQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aregnaud-newforma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aregnaud-newforma/frontend-demo-app/commits/48a8c18eb4c78f62cd007dd56a105c59a55491ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:14:08Z","email":"aregnaud@newforma.com","name":"aregnaud-newforma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:14:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Datadog APM on the backend, and RUM on the mobile app (#24)\n\n* Add Datadog RUM, browser logs and source-map uploads beside Sentry\n\nThe shell starts Datadog RUM and browser logs next to Sentry, so the two\ncan be compared on the same sessions. Both remotes report through that\none init, with the Datadog SDKs shared as federation singletons. Views\nare named by route through Datadog''s React Router wrapper, and errors\nthat Sentry''s boundaries and the query cache catch are reported to\nDatadog too.\n\n`yarn build` uploads each build''s source maps to Datadog when\nDATADOG_API_KEY is set, under the same version as Sentry''s release, and\ndeletes them from dist/ once both uploads have read them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Continue the RUM trace through both backend services in Datadog\n\nBrowser RUM now writes a W3C traceparent on every call to /api/, and\nboth services continue it into Datadog APM beside Sentry, so a save is\none Datadog trace from the RUM resource through the account API, its\nPostgres queries and the notifications service.\n\nThe two services reach a local Datadog Agent (yarn datadog:start) by\ndifferent roads. The account API uses OpenTelemetry over OTLP, because\nDatadog''s .NET tracer has no macOS build. The notifications service\nuses dd-trace, because Sentry''s Node SDK already owns the global\nOpenTelemetry provider. Neither reads nor writes `baggage`, which stays\nSentry''s, and neither traces Sentry''s own uploads. docs/adr/0008\nrecords the decision.\n\nBoth are off unless DD_AGENT_HOST is set, so CI traces nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Datadog RUM to the mobile app beside Sentry\n\nThe Expo app starts Datadog''s React Native SDK through DatadogProvider\nwhen EXPO_PUBLIC_DATADOG_APPLICATION_ID and _CLIENT_TOKEN are set, and\nnever under jest. Views are named by Expo Router route, failed queries\nand mutations are reported next to Sentry''s, requests made through\nExpo''s native fetch are tracked, and calls to the account API carry a\nW3C traceparent so they join the backend trace.\n\nA native Release build uploads its dSYMs, source maps and Proguard\nmappings to Datadog when DATADOG_API_KEY is set at prebuild: app.config\nadds the expo-datadog plugin only then, so a build without a key still\nsucceeds. The Metro config stamps bundles with the debug IDs those maps\nare matched by.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexis Regnaud <alexis.regnaud@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"798c3cd527ec0f42f83d7d9336d763b13309c1be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aregnaud-newforma/frontend-demo-app/git/trees/798c3cd527ec0f42f83d7d9336d763b13309c1be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/aregnaud-newforma/frontend-demo-app/git/commits/48a8c18eb4c78f62cd007dd56a105c59a55491ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 798c3cd527ec0f42f83d7d9336d763b13309c1be\nparent 8d3301bf9a8ee3300e418781769d16b86c78033b\nauthor aregnaud-newforma <aregnaud@newforma.com> 1790867648 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790867648 +0200\n\nDatadog APM on the backend, and RUM on the mobile app (#24)\n\n* Add Datadog RUM, browser logs and source-map uploads beside Sentry\n\nThe shell starts Datadog RUM and browser logs next to Sentry, so the two\ncan be compared on the same sessions. Both remotes report through that\none init, with the Datadog SDKs shared as federation singletons. Views\nare named by route through Datadog''s React Router wrapper, and errors\nthat Sentry''s boundaries and the query cache catch are reported to\nDatadog too.\n\n`yarn build` uploads each build''s source maps to Datadog when\nDATADOG_API_KEY is set, under the same version as Sentry''s release, and\ndeletes them from dist/ once both uploads have read them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Continue the RUM trace through both backend services in Datadog\n\nBrowser RUM now writes a W3C traceparent on every call to /api/, and\nboth services continue it into Datadog APM beside Sentry, so a save is\none Datadog trace from the RUM resource through the account API, its\nPostgres queries and the notifications service.\n\nThe two services reach a local Datadog Agent (yarn datadog:start) by\ndifferent roads. The account API uses OpenTelemetry over OTLP, because\nDatadog''s .NET tracer has no macOS build. The notifications service\nuses dd-trace, because Sentry''s Node SDK already owns the global\nOpenTelemetry provider. Neither reads nor writes `baggage`, which stays\nSentry''s, and neither traces Sentry''s own uploads. docs/adr/0008\nrecords the decision.\n\nBoth are off unless DD_AGENT_HOST is set, so CI traces nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add Datadog RUM to the mobile app beside Sentry\n\nThe Expo app starts Datadog''s React Native SDK through DatadogProvider\nwhen EXPO_PUBLIC_DATADOG_APPLICATION_ID and _CLIENT_TOKEN are set, and\nnever under jest. Views are named by Expo Router route, failed queries\nand mutations are reported next to Sentry''s, requests made through\nExpo''s native fetch are tracked, and calls to the account API carry a\nW3C traceparent so they join the backend trace.\n\nA native Release build uploads its dSYMs, source maps and Proguard\nmappings to Datadog when DATADOG_API_KEY is set at prebuild: app.config\nadds the expo-datadog plugin only then, so a build without a key still\nsucceeds. The Metro config stamps bundles with the debug IDs those maps\nare matched by.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexis Regnaud <alexis.regnaud@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvnjACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwkEQAG3RS1oAbasJpHyMjDFh8tlc\nVsCg2kMrXjO1n0wkYHsZYNW4ux5DnZG2ssJJMc5u77tYznXZyyp5Owgj6tZcx53Z\n3M2hiiki5kP0+FHVw6bRtaaM2KEHqA3iFjNpWcf9cru6/hsS+tDydgNuf26u6a75\n1ZFuYcQ4DEl9K3z6l4